# Advanced Bestiary -- Special Abilities
SOURCELONG:Advanced Bestiary	SOURCESHORT:AB	SOURCEWEB:http://greenronin.com/	SOURCEDATE:2014-09
# ORIGINAL ENTRY: Seb Quenet
# ORIGINAL ENTRY DATE: 2026/09/20

###Block: Acid Creature, Agathion Invested, Airborne Creature, Alacritous Creature
Acid Pool	KEY:Acid Pool ~ Acid Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.Aura	DESC:An acid creature is surrounded at all times by a pool of acid, a spread with a radius of twice the creature's space (a creature with a 5 ft. space has a 10 ft. radius pool). Anything coming into contact with this acid takes acid damage (no save) equal to a base of 1d6 for Medium; the damage scales with size. A flying acid creature has no pool but drips acid on those below instead (see acid rain).	SOURCEPAGE:p.9
Acid Rain	KEY:Acid Rain ~ Acid Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Anything beneath a flying acid creature takes damage from dripping acid equal to the creature's acid pool damage. A Reflex save is allowed for half damage. If the acid creature can hover, anything under it takes this damage each round the hover is maintained. The Reflex save DC is Dexterity-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.9
Acidic Spellcasting	KEY:Acidic Spellcasting ~ Acid Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:An acid creature casts all spells and spell-like abilities with the acid descriptor at one caster level higher. Spells and spell-like abilities with the water descriptor are changed to the acid descriptor, deal acid damage and are cast at one caster level higher; if the spell creates water it now creates acid and deals damage equal to the creature's acidic strikes. As a free action the creature can have any damaging spell or spell-like ability deal half of its damage as acid damage, at the normal caster level.	SOURCEPAGE:p.9
Acidic Strikes	KEY:Acidic Strikes ~ Acid Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A Medium acid creature's natural attacks deal an additional 1d6 acid damage, plus a further 1d6 acid damage for every 5 racial HD of the base creature. The damage scales with size and stacks with any other acid damage the creature deals.	SOURCEPAGE:p.9
Acidic Body	KEY:Acidic Body ~ Acid Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An acid creature's touch corrodes any material it touches except stone. For each round it maintains its touch on an object, the acid creature deals its acidic strikes damage to that object, including most equipment. Anyone grappled by or grappling an acid creature takes this damage every round until the grapple is broken. Any supernatural or extraordinary ability of the base creature that has water in its name, or affects water, affects acid instead.	SOURCEPAGE:p.10
Acidic Swimming	KEY:Acidic Swimming ~ Acid Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An acid creature with a swim speed can swim through acid as a normal creature swims through water. If the base creature has no swim speed it gains one at its highest speed or 20 feet, whichever is larger.	SOURCEPAGE:p.10
Water Vulnerability	KEY:Water Vulnerability ~ Acid Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:For every gallon of freshwater an acid creature is exposed to it takes 1d6 damage. If submerged, the damage increases to 1d8 per round. An acid creature cannot heal this damage until it is no longer exposed to the water.	SOURCEPAGE:p.9
+4 sacred bonus on saves against poison and petrification	KEY:Agathion Invested ~ Sacred Saves	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality	ASPECT:SaveBonus|+4 sacred vs. poison and petrification	SOURCEPAGE:p.11
Sacred Attacks	KEY:Agathion Invested ~ Sacred Attacks	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Each of an agathion-invested creature's melee attacks with a natural or manufactured weapon deals +1d6 points of extra damage to creatures of evil alignment. All of its natural and manufactured weapons count as magic and good-aligned for overcoming damage reduction.	SOURCEPAGE:p.11
Spell Vulnerability	KEY:Spell Vulnerability ~ Agathion Invested	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:An agathion-invested creature subjected to dismissal or dispel good must succeed on a Will save or lose all modifications bestowed by this template for a number of rounds equal to the opponent's caster level. Subjected to banishment, it must succeed on a Will save or lose the template; the agathion is sent back to its plane of origin and cannot invest the same creature for a year and a day. Although not a lycanthrope, it is affected by spells and effects that specifically target lycanthropes.	SOURCEPAGE:p.11
Inhabited	KEY:Inhabited ~ Agathion Invested	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:The creature is inhabited by a specific agathion, which can neither control it nor read its mind and perceives only what the inhabited creature does. The agathion is in constant telepathic communication with its host regardless of language. While inhabiting, the agathion has no access to its own supernatural, spell-like or extraordinary abilities, cannot cast spells, and cannot be targeted by any spell or effect, though divination still detects it. Damage to the host does not harm the agathion. The agathion can leave or re-enter as a standard action; if the two are separated for more than a day the host loses the template permanently.	SOURCEPAGE:p.13
Agathion Form	KEY:Agathion Form ~ Agathion Invested	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:At will, as a full-round action, the creature can take the form of the agathion that invested it, as a lycanthrope's change shape ability but with no hybrid form. In agathion form its type changes to outsider with the augmented and native subtypes, and it gains a +4 racial bonus on Perception, low-light vision and truespeech, plus the movement rates and physical ability scores of the agathion. It can remain in agathion form a number of rounds per day equal to its Charisma score (minimum 1); this is a polymorph effect and need not be used consecutively.	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Agathion Form (Avoral)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Agathion Form ~ Agathion Invested	DESC:In avoral form the creature gains 1/day true seeing and blur (self only), and an additional +4 racial bonus on Perception.	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Agathion Form (Cetaceal)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Agathion Form ~ Agathion Invested	DESC:In cetaceal form the creature gains the aquatic subtype, amphibious and blindsense 60 ft.	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Agathion Form (Draconal)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Agathion Form ~ Agathion Invested	DESC:In draconal form the creature gains a breath weapon (30-ft. line, 1/day) and immunity to the energy type of that breath weapon. The energy type matches the draconal's. Damage is 1d6 plus a further 1d6 for every 2 Hit Dice of the base creature (10d6 maximum), Reflex save for half. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Agathion Form (Leonal)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Agathion Form ~ Agathion Invested	DESC:In leonal form the creature gains pounce, grab with its claws and rake with 2 claws. The rake damage equals the damage of its claw natural attack.	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Agathion Form (Silvanshee)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Agathion Form ~ Agathion Invested	DESC:In silvanshee form the creature gains lay on hands (1d6, 1/day), pounce, an additional +4 racial bonus on Perception and Stealth, and Weapon Finesse as a bonus feat.	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Agathion Form (Vulpinal)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Agathion Form ~ Agathion Invested	DESC:In vulpinal form the creature gains lay on hands (1d6, 1/day), pounce and a +4 racial bonus on Acrobatics checks made to jump.	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Cloud Sight	KEY:Cloud Sight ~ Airborne Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Vision	DESC:An airborne creature sees through fog, clouds and similar obscuring effects with perfect clarity, including magical or supernatural fogs and clouds. Creatures and objects gain no concealment against it from such conditions. It can use this ability while in cloud form.	SOURCEPAGE:p.14
Cloud Form	KEY:Cloud Form ~ Airborne Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:An airborne creature gains the flight special quality as an extraordinary ability. If the base creature had the amphibious special quality it exchanges it for water breathing; otherwise it gains hold breath as an extraordinary ability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.15
Improved Evasion	KEY:Improved Evasion ~ Alacritous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:As the rogue ability: on a successful Reflex save against an attack that deals half damage on a success, the creature takes no damage; on a failed save it takes only half damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.16
Improved Uncanny Dodge	KEY:Improved Uncanny Dodge ~ Alacritous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:As the barbarian ability, at a level equal to the creature's total HD + 4.	SOURCEPAGE:p.16
Duck Aside	KEY:Duck Aside ~ Alacritous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:Any round the alacritous creature does not use split second, it has a 20%% chance to step away from any attack that would otherwise hit it. This stacks with any miss chance from concealment.	SOURCEPAGE:p.16
Split Second	KEY:Split Second ~ Alacritous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a full-round action the creature can move up to double its movement, then take a standard action at its original location and another at its new location. Either action may be a charge, a pounce or an attack using Spring Attack. It is treated as being at both locations for attacks of opportunity and threatened squares until the end of its action, then comes to rest at its new position. Split second cannot be used two rounds in a row.	SOURCEPAGE:p.16

###Block: Amalgam, Amphibious Creature, Angelic Vessel, Apocalypse Swarm
Amalgam	KEY:Amalgam ~ Combined Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality	DESC:An amalgam combines two base creatures into one. Its body form is that of the base creature with the most Hit Dice, and it has the limbs of both. Cross-reference the two base creatures' types on Table 2-3 for the amalgam's type; it keeps both sets of subtypes unless two conflict, in which case it loses both. Its size is that of the larger base creature, its alignment mixes both, and it has the racial HD of the creature with the most racial HD, of a die size fitting its new type. Average the two natural armor bonuses (adjusting the smaller creature's by Table 2-4 first) and the two sets of ability scores (adjusting by Table 2-5 first), rounding down at 10 or higher and up below 10. It keeps the speeds, senses, auras, defenses, weaknesses, spellcasting, special attacks and special qualities of both, taking the better where they overlap, and drops any tied to a limb or body form it does not have. It keeps only the bonus feats of both and repurchases the rest; it keeps racial skill bonuses but repurchases all skill ranks. Set the CR by comparing the result to both base creatures, then to creatures of up to 3 CR higher. Apply these changes by hand; PCGen cannot derive them.	SOURCEPAGE:p.18
Breathing Skin	KEY:Breathing Skin ~ Amphibious Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:Because an amphibious creature's skin aids its breathing, it takes a -2 penalty on Fortitude saving throws against gases, contact and inhaled poisons, and all other inhaled effects.	ASPECT:SaveBonus|-2 vs. gases and inhaled effects	SOURCEPAGE:p.23
+4 sacred bonus on saves against poison and petrification	KEY:Angelic Vessel ~ Sacred Saves	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality	ASPECT:SaveBonus|+4 sacred vs. poison and petrification	SOURCEPAGE:p.25
Deflection Bonus	KEY:Angelic Vessel ~ Deflection	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Defensive	DESC:An angelic vessel gains a deflection bonus to its AC equal to its Charisma bonus (minimum +0).	SOURCEPAGE:p.25
Dying Burst	KEY:Angelic Vessel ~ Dying Burst	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:If an angelic vessel dies, the angel within is released in a burst of holy light as it returns to its home plane. The light is identical to a holy word spell with a range of 60 feet, and the angel counts as being on its home plane, so all nongood extraplanar creatures within range are banished. The caster level equals that of the specific angel; the save DC is Charisma-based, using the vessel's total Hit Dice.	SOURCEPAGE:p.25
Sacred Attacks	KEY:Angelic Vessel ~ Sacred Attacks	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Each of an angelic vessel's melee attacks with a natural or manufactured weapon deals +%1d6 points of extra damage to evil creatures. All its natural and manufactured weapons count as magic and good-aligned for overcoming damage reduction.|AngelicVesselSacredDice	SOURCEPAGE:p.25
Sacred Smite	KEY:Angelic Vessel ~ Sacred Smite	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a swift action an angelic vessel can smite an evil creature, adding its Charisma modifier to attack and damage; the damage is doubled against a foe with the evil subtype. Against an evil outsider, or a creature possessed or inhabited by an evil creature, the smite also acts as a banishment spell at a caster level equal to the vessel's total HD. A sacred smite must be declared before the attack, and a miss uses up that use. Usable 1 + 1 per 5 HD times per day.	SOURCEPAGE:p.25
Spell Vulnerability	KEY:Spell Vulnerability ~ Angelic Vessel	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:An angelic vessel subjected to dismissal or dispel good must succeed on a Will save or lose all modifications bestowed by this template for a number of rounds equal to the opponent's caster level. Subjected to banishment, it must succeed on a Will save or lose the template; the angel is sent back to its plane of origin without a dying burst and cannot inhabit the same creature for a year and a day. The vessel gets a +4 sacred bonus on these saves.	SOURCEPAGE:p.25
Angelic Inhabitation	KEY:Angelic Vessel ~ Angelic Inhabitation	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A specific angel is in full physical and mental control of the vessel, and the two are in constant two-way telepathic communication. The angel can release control at will and reassert it at any time; the vessel resists with a Will save against DC 20 plus the angel's Charisma or Wisdom modifier, whichever is higher, and on a success stays in control for a number of rounds equal to the amount by which the roll exceeded the DC (minimum 1). While inhabiting, the angel cannot cast its own spells or use its own supernatural, spell-like or extraordinary abilities, though it may use the vessel's spells. It cannot be targeted directly by spells but is detected normally by divination. Damage to the vessel does not harm the angel. The angel can exit as a standard action, leaving the vessel stunned for 1d6 rounds and stripped of the template until it returns; separated for more than a day, the base creature loses the template.	SOURCEPAGE:p.26
Cassisian Recall	KEY:Cassisian Recall ~ Angelic Vessel	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Thanks to the cassisian angel's perfect memory, the vessel can gain a +10 bonus on any Intelligence-based skill or check while taking 10, cast one more time any spell it has already cast that day, or perfectly recall any event it has sensed that day. Usable a number of times per day equal to its Intelligence modifier (minimum 1).	SOURCEPAGE:p.27
Truespeech	KEY:Truespeech ~ Angelic Vessel	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:The creature can speak with any creature that has a language, as though using a tongues spell. This is always active.	SOURCEPAGE:p.26
Extra Hit Dice	KEY:Extra Hit Dice ~ Apocalypse Swarm	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An apocalypse swarm gains 5 racial Hit Dice beyond the base creature's total. Recalculate its base saves, hit points, feats, skill points and the save DCs of its special attacks. PCGen cannot add racial Hit Dice through a template; add the 5 racial HD to the base race by hand.	SOURCEPAGE:p.28
Fear Aura	KEY:Fear Aura ~ Apocalypse Swarm	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:An apocalypse swarm radiates a fear aura with a range of 100 ft. A target that fails a Will save is frightened for 10 rounds; on a success it is only shaken for 10 rounds. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.28
Split	KEY:Split ~ Apocalypse Swarm	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:When an apocalypse swarm takes damage equal to or greater than its Hit Dice from a single attack, it splits into two identical swarms, each with half the original's current hit points (rounded down). Attacks dealing less than 10 points of damage do not cause a split, and damage from multiple attacks is not cumulative. A swarm reduced to 5 or fewer hit points cannot split, and disperses at 0 hit points.	SOURCEPAGE:p.28
Greater Distraction	CATEGORY:Ability Focus	TYPE:Ability Focus	SOURCEPAGE:p.29
Greater Distraction	KEY:Greater Distraction ~ Apocalypse Swarm	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Any living creature that takes damage from an apocalypse swarm's swarm attack is nauseated for 1d4 rounds; a successful Fortitude save (DC 10 + 1/2 the swarm's HD + its Con modifier) negates the effect. The save DC is Constitution-based. This replaces the swarm's distraction ability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.29
Swarm Damage	KEY:Swarm Damage ~ Apocalypse Swarm	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:An apocalypse swarm's melee attack damage increases by +2d6, which includes the increase in swarm damage from its additional Hit Dice.	SOURCEPAGE:p.29

###Block: Arboreal Creature, Archon-Graced, Augmented Creature
Brachiation	KEY:Brachiation ~ Arboreal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:By hanging beneath or within a canopy of trees, or a similar structure with many limbs, an arboreal creature can swing hand over hand at a speed equal to its climb speed. It follows the rules for climbing, but the base Climb DC for brachiation is 10. Any tree the creature can climb without bending it is suitable.	SOURCEPAGE:p.30
Tree Leap	KEY:Tree Leap ~ Arboreal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:While brachiating, when the distance between trees exceeds twice its reach, the creature can make the leap as if jumping with a running start. The DC equals the distance between the trees, and bonuses from a land speed greater than 30 do not apply. If it fails the Acrobatics check by less than 5, it may make a DC 15 Acrobatics check to catch a handhold 5 feet below the target. Failing by more than 5 it falls normally, but may still make the usual DC 15 Acrobatics check to ignore the first 10 ft. of the fall.	SOURCEPAGE:p.30
Brachiating Slam	KEY:Brachiating Slam ~ Arboreal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:While brachiating, an arboreal creature can attack with any one limb it is not using to brachiate. If the base creature has a leg attack it keeps that attack at normal damage; otherwise it gains a slam attack usable only while brachiating, primary if it has no other natural attacks and secondary otherwise. Slam damage is as for a creature one size larger.	SOURCEPAGE:p.30
Woodland Stealth	KEY:Woodland Stealth ~ Arboreal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:In forested or jungle environments an arboreal creature gains a +4 bonus on Stealth and Survival checks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.31
Aura of Menace	KEY:Aura of Menace ~ Archon-Graced	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:When the creature becomes angry or enters a fight, any hostile creature within 10 feet must make a Will save or take a -2 penalty on attacks, AC and saves for 24 hours, or until it successfully hits the archon-graced creature. A creature that resists is immune to that particular creature's aura for 24 hours. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.32
+4 racial bonus on saves against poison and petrification	KEY:Archon-Graced ~ Celestial Saves	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality	ASPECT:SaveBonus|+4 racial vs. poison and petrification	SOURCEPAGE:p.32
Graced	KEY:Graced ~ Archon-Graced	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:The creature carries part of a specific archon's divine essence. That archon is constantly aware of the creature and may intervene on its behalf at the GM's discretion. An archon can grace only one creature at a time and may withdraw its grace, and the template, at will. A banishment spell can force the grace out, but the graced creature gets a Will save to negate it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.33
Wrathful Burst	KEY:Wrathful Burst ~ Archon-Graced	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once every 6 rounds the creature can let loose a blast of force dealing 2d6 damage to all adjacent creatures, Reflex save for half. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.32
Harbinger's Awareness	KEY:Harbinger's Awareness ~ Archon-Graced	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The creature gains a +4 bonus on Perception rolls and cannot be surprised or caught flat-footed.	BONUS:SKILL|Perception|4	SOURCEPAGE:p.33
Bring Down the Quarry	KEY:Bring Down the Quarry ~ Archon-Graced	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Against the creature targeted by its bloodhound ability, the archon-graced creature gains a bonus to AC, CMB, CMD, attack and damage rolls equal to its Wisdom modifier (minimum +0).	SOURCEPAGE:p.32
Bloodhound	KEY:Bloodhound ~ Archon-Graced	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:The creature can track any one creature whose scent it has caught, anywhere on the same plane. This does not give an exact location but reveals the general direction to within 100 feet. It can change targets as a full-round action but may only have one target at a time.	SOURCEPAGE:p.33
Light Ray	KEY:Light Ray ~ Archon-Graced	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:At will, the creature can unleash a beam of light dealing 1d6 damage to a single creature. Against undead this is a ranged touch attack and a light effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.32
Burst of Light	KEY:Burst of Light ~ Archon-Graced	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Once a day, as a move action, the creature can instantaneously travel 100 feet to any unoccupied location within line of sight.	SOURCEPAGE:p.33
Ignite Weapon	KEY:Ignite Weapon ~ Archon-Graced	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Three times a day, as a standard action, the creature can turn any natural or manufactured weapon it has into a flaming weapon; the flames do not harm it. Once per day it can instead make that weapon flaming burst. The quality lasts a number of rounds equal to its Wisdom modifier (minimum +1) and may be ended at will.	SOURCEPAGE:p.32
Gift of Armor	KEY:Gift of Armor ~ Archon-Graced	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:The creature is proficient with all forms of armor, and takes no speed reduction or armor check penalty when wearing armor.	AUTO:ARMORPROF|ARMORTYPE=Light|ARMORTYPE=Medium|ARMORTYPE=Heavy	SOURCEPAGE:p.33
Defensive Strike	KEY:Defensive Strike ~ Archon-Graced	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Each time the creature strikes an opponent with a melee attack it learns that opponent's defensive weaknesses, gaining a +1 circumstance bonus on AC, CMB, attack and damage rolls against it. The bonus is cumulative for each successful strike, and is lost as soon as the creature attacks a different opponent, the opponent dies, or combat ends.	SOURCEPAGE:p.32
Communal Defense	KEY:Communal Defense ~ Archon-Graced	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:By touching an ally as an immediate action, the creature can lend that ally one of its feats for 1 round, even if the ally does not meet the prerequisites. For that round the creature loses the use of that feat and any feat that has it as a prerequisite. Only one feat may be lent to one creature at a time; the feat returns at the start of the creature's next action.	SOURCEPAGE:p.33
Smite Chaos or Evil	KEY:Smite Chaos or Evil ~ Archon-Graced	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Three times a day the creature can smite a chaotic or evil creature. The smite bonus equals its Charisma modifier (minimum +1), and doubles against a chaotic evil creature.	SOURCEPAGE:p.32
Graced Regeneration	KEY:Graced Regeneration ~ Archon-Graced	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:The creature gains regeneration equal to 1 plus half its Hit Dice. This regeneration is bypassed by evil weapons and effects.	SOURCEPAGE:p.33
Regeneration	KEY:Augmented ~ Regeneration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An augmented creature gains regeneration equal to 5 plus one-fifth of its total Hit Dice (rounded down), bypassed by electricity damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.35
Construct Hit Points	KEY:Augmented ~ Construct Hit Points	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.ModifyHP	DESC:An augmented creature's Hit Dice do not change, but it gains bonus hit points as a construct of its size (minimum 5 hp), and all bonus hit points from Constitution are halved.	SOURCEPAGE:p.35
Adamantine Strikes	KEY:Augmented ~ Adamantine Strikes	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:An augmented creature's natural attacks count as adamantine and cold iron for overcoming damage reduction.	SOURCEPAGE:p.35
Electricity Vulnerability	KEY:Electricity Vulnerability ~ Augmented Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:Electricity damage stuns an augmented creature for 1d4 rounds and bypasses its regeneration, though not its spell resistance. A Fortitude save against a DC equal to half the damage taken negates the stunning. An augmented creature loses any electricity resistance or immunity it had.	SOURCEPAGE:p.35
Of Two Worlds	KEY:Of Two Worlds ~ Augmented Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:An augmented creature counts as both a creature of its type and a construct against effects specific to type. Healing effects and repairs each restore only half damage, since each applies to only the flesh or the machine part. Spells that affect only objects can affect it. Damaging magical effects must still overcome its spell resistance.	SOURCEPAGE:p.35
Augmentation Psychosis	KEY:Augmentation Psychosis ~ Augmented Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An augmented creature with a Wisdom score of 2 or less, including none, is overcome with rage and gains the ferocity universal monster ability. The rage is identical to a barbarian's but permanent; effects that remove or calm rage instead leave it staggered for one round, and raising its Wisdom above 2 cures both rage and ferocity. At Wisdom 0 it becomes insane; the insanity, but not the rage, can be cured with healing magic.	SOURCEPAGE:p.36
Repairs	KEY:Repairs ~ Augmented Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An augmented creature can be healed with an appropriate Craft check against DC 15, paying 10 gp of materials per hit point healed. Repairs take a full day and can heal no more than half the total damage taken.	SOURCEPAGE:p.36
Augmentations	KEY:Augmentations ~ Augmented Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Augmentations are magical (supernatural) or technological (extraordinary). Each costs gold and augmentation points (AP); unless stated otherwise the gold cost is 100 gp times the number of augmentations the creature already has, and implanting takes 1 day. The creature has AP equal to its Constitution score, or Charisma score if it has no Constitution, and need not spend them all at once. Every AP spent beyond that maximum inflicts 1 point of permanent Wisdom drain that cannot be healed until its Constitution rises or augmentations are removed. It also has access to every animated object construction-point ability at 1 CP = 1 AP; abilities that normally do not stack do stack here, at +1 AP each time. Installing requires a Craft check against DC 20 + the AP cost: failing by 5 or more destroys the augmentation but refunds the AP, failing by 10 or more destroys it and loses the AP. Removing one deals the creature its HD in damage, permanent unless the augmentation is replaced. Making an augmentation internal costs its AP cost a second time and requires a DC 25 Perception check to detect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.36
Advanced Sensors	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Augmentation	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	DESC:The augmented creature gains one of darkvision +60 ft., low-light vision, blindsense +60 ft. or blindsight +60 ft. Taking it again for the same sense costs +1 AP each time.	SOURCEPAGE:p.37
Enhanced Ability Score	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Augmentation	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	DESC:Increase one ability score other than Wisdom by +2. Wisdom can only be raised in +1 steps. Each further enhancement costs +1 AP.	SOURCEPAGE:p.37
Enhanced Hit Dice	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Augmentation	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	DESC:Racial Hit Dice increase by +1; a creature with no racial HD gains one. Each further enhancement costs +1 AP.	SOURCEPAGE:p.37
Enhanced AC	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Augmentation	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	DESC:Increase AC by +1, as an armor, dodge or natural bonus if extraordinary, or a deflection or dodge bonus if supernatural. Bonuses from this augmentation stack with each other but not necessarily with bonuses from other sources.	SOURCEPAGE:p.37
Faster Movement	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Augmentation	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	DESC:Increase the speed of one existing mode of movement by +5 ft.	SOURCEPAGE:p.37
Hardened	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Augmentation	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	DESC:Gain hardness +1.	SOURCEPAGE:p.37
Integrated Ammunition	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Augmentation	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	DESC:The creature can store up to 20 arrows, 20 bolts, 50 sling bullets or 10 rounds of firearm ammunition in its body, recovering one piece as a free action. With an integrated ranged weapon or firearm it can reload as a standard action.	SOURCEPAGE:p.37
Integrated Magic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Augmentation	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	DESC:A single spell becomes a supernatural ability, usable once per day. The AP cost is half the spell's level; each extra AP adds one use per day, triple the cost makes it at will and quadruple makes it constant. Integrated magic is always supernatural.	SOURCEPAGE:p.37
Integrated Weaponry (Melee)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Augmentation	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	DESC:Replace one natural attack with a one-handed melee weapon that is part of the creature and cannot be dropped, though it can be made masterwork or magical at the usual cost. Adding the weapon without replacing a natural attack costs +1 AP. The creature is always proficient with it. The weapon counts as a natural attack but keeps any iterative attacks. The gold cost is the normal augmentation cost plus the weapon's price.	SOURCEPAGE:p.37
Integrated Weaponry (Ranged)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Augmentation	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	DESC:The creature has a non-firearm ranged weapon integrated. It must be one the creature could normally carry, cannot be dropped, and can be made masterwork or magical at the usual cost; it does not include ammunition. The creature is always proficient with it. The weapon counts as a natural attack but keeps any iterative attacks. The gold cost is the normal augmentation cost plus the weapon's price.	SOURCEPAGE:p.37
Integrated Weaponry (Firearm)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Augmentation	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	DESC:As integrated weaponry (ranged), but the weapon is a firearm.	SOURCEPAGE:p.37
Nimble Flyer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Augmentation	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	DESC:If the creature has a fly speed, increase its maneuverability by one step.	SOURCEPAGE:p.37
Powerful Weapon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Augmentation	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	DESC:Choose one integrated melee weapon; it is used as if wielded two-handed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.37

###Block: Avian Creature, Azata-Inspired, Bipedal Creature, Blood Knight
Avian	KEY:Avian ~ Avian Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An avian creature's body is covered in feathers and it has two large wings that let it fly. Its weight is 20%% less than the base creature's thanks to its lightweight body structure. It gains a fly speed equal to its highest speed with average maneuverability, or better if the base creature already flew better than that.	SOURCEPAGE:p.39
+4 racial bonus on saves against petrification	KEY:Azata-Inspired ~ Petrification Saves	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality	ASPECT:SaveBonus|+4 racial vs. petrification	SOURCEPAGE:p.40
Shatter Bonds	KEY:Shatter Bonds ~ Azata-Inspired	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:At will the creature can make a sunder attack against any physical or magical holding, binding, entangling or imprisoning effect. If the attack succeeds and the damage exceeds the item's hardness, or twice the magical effect's spell level, the effect is destroyed or dispelled. Against a mythic binding the attempt takes a -15 penalty unless the creature is itself mythic.	SOURCEPAGE:p.40
Smite Tyranny	KEY:Smite Tyranny ~ Azata-Inspired	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once a day plus once per 5 Hit Dice, the creature can make a devastating attack against a lawful evil creature, or anyone who imprisons or suppresses the freedom of others: a creature maintaining a hold spell, grappling another creature, or that has used imprisonment or similar magic. The smite must be declared before the attack roll. On a hit it is automatically a confirmed critical that bypasses damage reduction and hardness; on a miss the use is lost.	SOURCEPAGE:p.40
Forever Free	KEY:Forever Free ~ Azata-Inspired	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:The creature automatically gains a second save against any effect that would hold, bind or imprison it, and must take the result of the second save. Against such an effect that allows no save, it gains a Reflex or Will save, whichever bonus is better.	SOURCEPAGE:p.41
Inspired	KEY:Inspired ~ Azata-Inspired	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:The creature gains a circumstance bonus equal to half its total HD on a single Intelligence-, Wisdom- or Charisma-based skill. The chosen skill can be changed once a day, but the bonus cannot apply to two different skills within the same 24-hour period.	SOURCEPAGE:p.41
Freedom's Burden	KEY:Freedom's Burden ~ Azata-Inspired	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:If the creature magically or physically binds, holds or imprisons a creature with an Intelligence above 3 for more than a minute, it takes a -1 penalty on all attack rolls, skill checks and saving throws for a day. The penalty is cumulative for each creature and each minute they are held, and ends one day after they are freed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.40
Leaf on the Wind	KEY:Leaf on the Wind ~ Azata-Inspired	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Any airborne creature takes a -2 penalty on attack and damage rolls against a bralani-inspired creature, which is never considered flat-footed except when surprised.	SOURCEPAGE:p.41
Fire Walking	KEY:Fire Walking ~ Azata-Inspired	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A brijidine-inspired creature can walk across flames and molten rock and metal as if they were solid, and is immune to fire while doing so.	SOURCEPAGE:p.41
Fast as Light	KEY:Fast as Light ~ Azata-Inspired	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Once a day plus once for every 5 HD, a ghaele-inspired creature can, as a move action, instantly move to any unoccupied location within 400 ft. that it has line of sight to, and may take further actions on arrival.	SOURCEPAGE:p.41
Inner Bard	KEY:Inner Bard ~ Azata-Inspired	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A lillend-inspired creature gains a +4 bonus on one Perform skill, which also becomes a class skill. Without bard levels, it chooses each day one bardic performance available to a bard of its total Hit Dice and can use it, as a move action, a number of times per day equal to its Charisma modifier (minimum 1) while using that Perform skill; only one performance may be accessed per day. With bard levels, it instead adds its Charisma modifier to its daily uses of bardic performance.	SOURCEPAGE:p.41
Summon Mote	KEY:Summon Mote ~ Azata-Inspired	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Once a day, in darkness or at night, a lyrakien-inspired creature can summon a mote of soft starlight that follows it and sheds light as a torch without affecting darkvision, light sensitivity or causing light-based harm. It stays as long as the creature wishes but vanishes at dawn. The mote can counter a darkness or deeper darkness spell as a light spell using the creature's total Hit Dice as caster level; on success it dispels the darkness and burns out for the day.	SOURCEPAGE:p.41
Bipedal Body	KEY:Bipedal Body ~ Bipedal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Two of the base creature's limbs, usually the last pair, become legs, and every other limb except a head that had a natural attack becomes an arm able to wield a weapon or make a natural attack. The creature keeps all natural attacks except those on limbs that became legs, and loses rake. With Intelligence 3 or higher it can wield weapons normally and keeps all weapon and armor proficiencies. Space and reach follow its size, using the tall column at Large or greater, and any longer-than-normal reach is kept.	SOURCEPAGE:p.43
Bipedal Speed	KEY:Bipedal Speed ~ Bipedal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The creature's land speed becomes the value for its size, even if the base creature was faster: Fine 5 ft., Diminutive 10 ft., Tiny 20 ft., Small 20 ft., Medium 30 ft., Large 40 ft., Huge 50 ft., Gargantuan 60 ft., Colossal 60 ft. A base creature with no land speed gets half that value (minimum 5 feet). Set this speed by hand; PCGen cannot key a movement rate to size from a template.	SOURCEPAGE:p.43
Armor Bonus	KEY:Blood Knight ~ Armor Bonus	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A blood knight gains an armor bonus to AC from the armor it wears, usually full plate for +9. If the base creature had a natural armor bonus it loses it and gains instead a deflection bonus equal to 1 + that original natural armor bonus.	SOURCEPAGE:p.45
Armor Bonus	KEY:Dread Blood Knight ~ Armor Bonus	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A dread blood knight gains an armor bonus to AC from the armor it wears, usually full plate for +9. If the base creature had a natural armor bonus it loses it and gains instead a deflection bonus equal to 3 + that original natural armor bonus.	SOURCEPAGE:p.47
Blood Drain	KEY:Blood Drain ~ Blood Knight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Any living creature damaged by a blood knight's natural attack takes 1 point of Constitution damage on top of the normal damage, multiplied on a critical hit as normal damage is. In a grapple it deals 1d4 points of Constitution damage each round the grapple is held. For each point of Constitution damage caused, the blood knight gains 5 temporary hit points.	SOURCEPAGE:p.45
Blood Drain	KEY:Blood Drain ~ Dread Blood Knight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:As the blood knight's blood drain, but it deals 2 points of Constitution damage, or 2d4 in a grapple.	SOURCEPAGE:p.47
Blood Slick	KEY:Blood Slick ~ Blood Knight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.Aura	DESC:A blood knight constantly drips slippery blood in a 10-foot-radius spread. The area counts as difficult terrain and as though under a grease spell; the Reflex save DC to avoid falling is Charisma-based. Blood knights are immune to the slipperiness of any blood knight's blood slick.	SOURCEPAGE:p.45
Fountain of Blood	KEY:Fountain of Blood ~ Blood Knight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Once every 1d4 rounds, as a full-round action, a blood knight sprays blood from its armor. Each creature within a 15-foot radius is covered in blood and must succeed on a Fortitude save as though it had ingested the knight's poison blood. The spray fills the area until the knight's next turn, affecting a creature at most once per round. The area then counts as a blood slick for 1 round per two Hit Dice. The blood remains until washed away with at least 5 gallons of liquid or burned away as a full-round action. A creature wanting to use, pick up or cling to a coated item must succeed on a Charisma-based Reflex save or drop it, and a coated creature gains a +10 bonus on Escape Artist checks. Blood knights are immune to the slipperiness.	SOURCEPAGE:p.45
Fountain of Blood	KEY:Fountain of Blood ~ Dread Blood Knight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:As the blood knight's fountain of blood, but with a 30-foot radius.	SOURCEPAGE:p.47
Poison Blood	KEY:Poison Blood ~ Blood Knight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Any opponent that strikes a blood knight with a bite attack is subject to this poison, as is any creature caught in its fountain of blood. Poison blood--ingested; save Fortitude; onset 1 minute; frequency 1/minute for 6 minutes; effect 1 Con plus nauseated; cure 1 save. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.46
Poison Blood	KEY:Poison Blood ~ Dread Blood Knight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:As the blood knight's poison blood, with a +3 racial bonus to the save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.47
Bleeding Strikes	KEY:Bleeding Strikes ~ Blood Knight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A blood knight gains a primary slam attack if it has no other natural attack, dealing damage as a creature one size larger. All its natural attacks gain the grab universal monster ability and deliver its blood drain. All its piercing or slashing attacks, natural or manufactured, gain bleed (2 hp/round).	SOURCEPAGE:p.45
Bleeding Strikes	KEY:Bleeding Strikes ~ Dread Blood Knight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:As the blood knight's bleeding strikes, but the bleed deals 2d4 points of damage per round.	SOURCEPAGE:p.47
Blood Body	KEY:Blood Body ~ Blood Knight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Because its body is entirely blood, a blood knight can store items within its form and retrieve one as a move action, or as a free action that is part of a move. A stored item must fit within the part of the armor it is placed in, and its weight still counts against encumbrance.	SOURCEPAGE:p.46
Bonded Armor	KEY:Bonded Armor ~ Blood Knight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A blood knight always wears the suit of armor it died in and can neither remove nor exchange it. If the armor is destroyed, so is the blood knight. It has a +5 bonus on saving throws made on behalf of its armor.	SOURCEPAGE:p.46
Slithering Blood	KEY:Slithering Blood ~ Dread Blood Knight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:At will, a dread blood knight can leave its bonded armor as a slick pool of mobile blood, for a number of minutes per day equal to its Charisma modifier (minimum 1), spread over any number of uses. In this form it gains the immunities of the ooze type, moves at its land speed, gains a slam attack for its size, and keeps every blood knight ability except bonded armor, blood body, blood slick, fountain of blood and its armor bonus. Its poison blood becomes a contact poison. It also gains the flow, pseudopodia, incredible compression and slick abilities of the slithering ooze template, and any items held by blood body drop into its armor. Staying past its daily allotment costs 1 Cha damage per minute and destroys it at Cha 0. If its armor is destroyed while in this form it loses half its Charisma at once and 1 more per round until it inhabits another suitable suit of armor, which becomes its new bonded armor; back in armor it regains 1 point of Charisma per day.	SOURCEPAGE:p.47

###Block: Bramble, Cave Creature, Chaosborne, Clockwork
Vulnerability to Fire	KEY:Vulnerability to Fire ~ Bramble	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A bramble takes half again as much damage (+50%%) from fire, regardless of whether a saving throw is allowed or whether the save succeeds.	SOURCEPAGE:p.49
Gore and Grab	KEY:Bramble ~ Gore and Grab	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A bramble gains a gore attack if it did not have one, secondary if it has other natural attacks and primary otherwise, dealing damage for the base creature's size. All of a bramble's natural attacks gain the grab universal monster ability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.49
Prickle Whip	KEY:Prickle Whip ~ Bramble	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Once per day a bramble can unravel and detach one of the tangled strands of its body as a move action, as though drawing a melee weapon. The strand works as a whip whose damage is lethal and is not negated by armor or natural armor of any value. It becomes stiff, brittle and useless after 1 hour.	SOURCEPAGE:p.49
Thorn Dart	KEY:Thorn Dart ~ Bramble	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Twice per day per Hit Die, a bramble can pull a long thorn from its body as a free action. The thorn is identical to a dart and the bramble is automatically proficient with it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.49
Thorny Grasp	KEY:Thorny Grasp ~ Bramble	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A bramble deals automatic piercing damage equal to the base damage of its gore attack, unmodified by Strength, each round it grapples a foe. Any creature that attempts to bull rush, grapple, overrun or trip a bramble takes this damage as well.	SOURCEPAGE:p.49
Woodland Stride	KEY:Woodland Stride ~ Bramble	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A bramble may move through any sort of undergrowth at its natural speed without taking damage or suffering any other impairment. Undergrowth magically manipulated to impede motion still affects it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.49
Thicket Stealth	KEY:Bramble ~ Thicket Stealth	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A bramble gains a +8 circumstance bonus on Stealth checks in forested areas and thickets.	SOURCEPAGE:p.49
Cave Senses	KEY:Cave Creature ~ Cave Senses	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Vision	DESC:A cave creature gains either blindsight 60 ft. or darkvision +60 ft. Once the choice is made it cannot be changed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.51
Light Blindness	KEY:Light Blindness ~ Cave Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:Abrupt exposure to bright light blinds a cave creature for 1 round; on subsequent rounds it is dazzled as long as it remains in the affected area.	SOURCEPAGE:p.51
Claws	KEY:Cave Creature ~ Claws	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A cave creature gains one or more primary claw attacks if it has no other natural attacks, one on each arm, wing, fin or similar appendage. The damage is that of a creature one size larger than the base creature.	SOURCEPAGE:p.51
Stone Stealth	KEY:Cave Creature ~ Stone Stealth	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Cave creatures are coloured much like the caves they live in, so a cave creature in an area of natural stone gains a +4 circumstance bonus on Stealth checks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.51
See Chaos	KEY:See Chaos ~ Chaosborne	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Vision	DESC:At will, a chaosborne can identify any chaotic creature, spell or magic item it can see, as the detect chaos spell at a caster level equal to its character level, and as though it had studied them for 3 rounds.	SOURCEPAGE:p.52
Aura of Anarchy	KEY:Aura of Anarchy ~ Chaosborne	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:Every nonchaotic creature within 10 feet takes a -5 penalty on all ability checks, skill checks and level checks unless it succeeds on a Charisma-based Will save. An affected target also automatically misses attack rolls and fails saving throws on a natural roll of 5 or below.	SOURCEPAGE:p.52
Law's Failing	KEY:Law's Failing ~ Chaosborne	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:A caster within 60 feet of a chaosborne who is lawfully aligned, or who casts a spell or spell-like ability with the lawful descriptor, must succeed on a caster level check (1d20 + caster level) or the ability fails and is wasted. The DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.52
Random Energy Immunity	KEY:Random Energy Immunity ~ Chaosborne	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:A chaosborne is immune to one type of energy damage at all times, but the type changes each round. Roll 1d8 at the start of each round: 1 acid, 2 cold, 3 electricity, 4 fire, 5 sonic, 6 force, 7 positive energy, 8 negative energy.	SOURCEPAGE:p.52
Chaosborne Curse	KEY:Chaosborne Curse ~ Chaosborne	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A chaosborne gains a primary touch attack that deals no damage but transmits its curse. Any chaotic-aligned creature, or creature with the chaotic subtype, hit by it must succeed on a Charisma-based Will save or gain the chaosborne template. A chaotic neutral target takes a -2 penalty on the save, a chaotic evil or chaotic good target a -1 penalty. The victim's alignment becomes chaotic neutral, with the usual penalties for changing alignment, and it falls unconscious for 1d4 rounds before rising as a chaosborne owing no allegiance to its maker.	SOURCEPAGE:p.52
Entropic Blow	KEY:Entropic Blow ~ Chaosborne	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any melee attack a chaosborne makes with a natural or manufactured weapon deals an extra 1d6 points of damage to lawful creatures and creatures with the lawful subtype.	SOURCEPAGE:p.52
Gaze of Discord	KEY:Gaze of Discord ~ Chaosborne	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Any chaotically aligned creature within 30 feet is dazed for 1 round; any lawfully aligned creature within 30 feet is confused, as the confusion spell, for the same period. A successful Charisma-based Will save resists. A chaosborne is immune to the gaze of other chaosbornes. This is a mind-affecting compulsion gaze effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.52
Ability Score Shift	KEY:Chaosborne ~ Ability Score Shift	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:When a creature acquires the chaosborne curse, roll 1d8 once for its ability score changes: 1 Str -2, Dex +2, Con -2, Int +2, Wis -2, Cha +2; 2 Str +2, Dex -2, Con +2, Int -2, Wis +2, Cha -2; 3 Str +2, Dex +2, Con +2, Int -2, Wis -2, Cha -2; 4 Str -2, Dex -2, Con -2, Int +2, Wis +2, Cha +2; 5 Str +4, Dex -4, Con +4, Int -4, Wis +4, Cha -4; 6 Str -4, Dex +4, Con -4, Int +4, Wis -4, Cha +4; 7 Str +4, Dex +4, Con -8, Int -4, Wis -4, Cha +8; 8 Str -4, Dex -8, Con +8, Int +4, Wis -8, Cha +8. No ability can be reduced below 1 by this template. Apply the rolled line by hand.	SOURCEPAGE:p.53
Spell Vulnerability	KEY:Spell Vulnerability ~ Chaosborne	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A remove curse or break enchantment spell cast on a chaosborne within a week of it contracting the curse strips the template permanently. Failing a saving throw against a dispel chaos effect removes the template however long it has been held.	SOURCEPAGE:p.52
Vulnerability to Electricity	KEY:Vulnerability to Electricity ~ Clockwork	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A clockwork takes half again as much damage (+50%%) from electricity, and loses any electricity resistance or immunity the base creature had.	SOURCEPAGE:p.56
Metal Body	KEY:Metal Body ~ Clockwork	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A clockwork creature is largely composed of metal and counts as a ferrous creature for rusting grasp and other spells with special effects on metal.	SOURCEPAGE:p.56
Armored Frame	KEY:Clockwork ~ Armored Frame	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A clockwork's natural armor increases by 1 for every 2 racial Hit Dice, and it ignores armor check penalties and the maximum Dexterity bonus of any armor it wears. It gains bonus hit points for its size as a construct and loses any bonus hit points from Constitution. Its damage reduction follows its total HD: 1-5 DR 5/adamantine, 6-10 DR 10/adamantine, 11-15 DR 15/adamantine, 16-20 DR 20/adamantine, 21+ DR 25/adamantine.	SOURCEPAGE:p.55
Slam	KEY:Clockwork ~ Slam	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A clockwork with no natural attacks gains a primary slam attack dealing damage for its size.	SOURCEPAGE:p.56
Created Mind	KEY:Created Mind ~ Clockwork	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A clockwork creature only accepts commands from its creator or a designated surrogate, whom the creator may appoint and dismiss at will. A clockwork that is not mindless may act independently, but to directly disobey a command it must succeed on a DC 20 Will save, or else follow the order as if under a command spell; a command that would destroy or harm it grants a second DC 15 Will save immediately after the first.	SOURCEPAGE:p.56
Creator Bond	KEY:Creator Bond ~ Clockwork	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A clockwork creature instinctively senses its creator's location within 100 ft. regardless of magical or natural barriers, and within that range gains a +10 circumstance bonus against Bluff and Disguise checks and any other effect meant to impersonate its creator.	SOURCEPAGE:p.56
Construction	KEY:Clockwork ~ Construction	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A clockwork is built like a golem and weighs nearly twice what the base creature does. Construction costs at least 2,000 gp times its CR and requires the Craft Construct feat, the ability to cast spells, and a Craft (clockwork) check against DC 25, +5 for every 10 CR. The creator's caster level is 10th or the clockwork's CR -1, whichever is higher (minimum 1st); above CR 20 the creator also needs the Mythic Crafter feat. Some or all of animate objects, geas/quest, limited wish, polymorph any object and resist energy are needed to finish it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.57

###Block: Cold Creature, Consuming Creature, Creature Swarm
Cold Aura	KEY:Cold Aura ~ Cold Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:A cold creature emits supernatural cold in a 10-foot radius. Everything within takes 1d6 cold damage, plus a further 1d6 for every 5 racial HD of the base creature. The aura cannot be suppressed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.58
Vulnerability to Fire	KEY:Vulnerability to Fire ~ Cold Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A cold creature takes half again as much damage (+50%%) from fire, regardless of whether a saving throw is allowed or whether the save succeeds.	SOURCEPAGE:p.58
Cold Spellcasting	KEY:Cold Spellcasting ~ Cold Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A cold creature casts all spells and spell-like abilities with the cold descriptor at one caster level higher. It can add the cold descriptor to any damaging spell, which is then cast at the normal caster level and deals half its damage as cold. It cannot cast spells or use spell-like abilities with the fire descriptor.	SOURCEPAGE:p.58
Freezing Blows	KEY:Freezing Blows ~ Cold Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A cold creature's attacks deal extra cold damage as a slam attack of a creature one size larger, one step higher again against a creature with the water subtype. This stacks with any other cold damage it deals. A cold creature with no natural attack gains a slam attack of biting winds and slashing ice, but it can never use manufactured weapons.	SOURCEPAGE:p.58
Freezing Embrace	KEY:Freezing Embrace ~ Cold Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once per day, plus once more per 5 racial Hit Dice of the base creature, a cold creature can try to freeze opponents solid by moving over them, affecting an area equal to its own space. A creature that fails a Charisma-based Fortitude save is turned to solid ice, as flesh to stone. A creature larger than the cold creature's space cannot be frozen but takes 1d6 cold damage per total Hit Die (minimum 1d6, maximum 20d6), halved on a successful save. Stone to flesh or equivalent magic restores a frozen creature; if it dies, it melts.	SOURCEPAGE:p.58
Freezing Touch	KEY:Freezing Touch ~ Cold Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Touching a body of liquid that is not a water-based creature freezes it 1 inch deep in a 10-foot radius, growing by 1 inch and 10 feet each further round of contact, up to its racial HD in inches of depth and ten times its racial HD in feet of radius. The ice lasts 1 round per racial Hit Die after contact ends. Creatures within the ice are trapped with no save and take cold damage as though hit by its freezing blows; escaping is a full-round action requiring a DC 20 Strength or Escape Artist check, +1 per inch of depth beyond the first. Against a creature with the water subtype, freezing touch works as freezing embrace without the need to move over the target.	SOURCEPAGE:p.58
Cold Body	KEY:Cold Body ~ Cold Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A cold creature's body freezes whatever it touches and whatever touches it. Anyone striking it with a natural or manufactured melee weapon takes 1d6 cold damage. If the base creature had a similar ability this one replaces it, but the damage of the two stacks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.59
Cold Walk	KEY:Cold Walk ~ Cold Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A cold creature walks over snow and ice without penalty, treats them as normal terrain, and needs no Acrobatics check to run or charge on them.	SOURCEPAGE:p.59
Snow Stealth	KEY:Cold Creature ~ Snow Stealth	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A cold creature has a +8 racial bonus on Stealth in cold environments, rising to +12 in a blizzard or similar bad weather.	SOURCEPAGE:p.59
Consume	KEY:Consume ~ Consuming Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once per month, as a full-round action, a consuming creature can devour the corpse of a creature it killed whose CR was no lower than its own CR -4. It gains 1 ingestion point per 5 HD of the consumed creature (minimum 1), and each ingestion point grants one of that creature's extraordinary, supernatural or spell-like abilities, never spellcasting. A gained ability uses the consumed creature's statistics except where a calculation depends on an ability score or total Hit Dice, which use the consuming creature's own. Every 2 ingestion points also add 1 racial Hit Die and 1 to the creature's CR.	SOURCEPAGE:p.60
Consuming Curse	KEY:Consuming Curse ~ Consuming Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:On a successful bite or engulf, the victim must succeed on a Charisma-based Will save or be cursed. Consuming curse: bite or engulf--injury; save Will negates; onset immediate; frequency 1/day; effect the cursed creature loses one randomly determined universal monster ability or class feature that is not spellcasting, and the consuming creature gains it. The consuming creature keeps the ability until the cursed creature dies, and must itself be destroyed before the curse can be lifted. It also automatically succeeds on all saves against that creature's remaining abilities, spells and spell-like abilities, and gains evasion and the Stalwart feat against them; physical attacks, effects without saves and magic items still affect it normally.	SOURCEPAGE:p.60
Quicken Special Attack	KEY:Quicken Special Attack ~ Consuming Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Once per round a consuming creature can quicken any one extraordinary or supernatural attack other than consume, making it a swift action, and may take another action, even another special attack, in the same round. An attack whose activation takes more than 1 round or a full-round action cannot be quickened. A consuming creature with spell-like abilities gains Quicken Spell-Like Ability as a bonus feat and may change the chosen ability whenever it gains an ingestion point.	SOURCEPAGE:p.60
Consumption Bonus	KEY:Consumption Bonus ~ Consuming Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A consuming creature gains a circumstance bonus equal to half its ingestion point total on its base attack bonus, saving throws and skill checks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.61
Distraction	KEY:Distraction ~ Creature Swarm	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Any living creature that takes damage from the swarm attack is nauseated for 1 round; a Fortitude save (DC 10 + 1/2 the swarm's HD + its Con modifier) negates.	SOURCEPAGE:p.62
Swarm Traits	KEY:Swarm Traits ~ Creature Swarm	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A creature swarm occupies a 10-foot square, or cube if its members fly, and has a reach of 0 feet; it does not threaten squares and cannot make attacks of opportunity with its swarm attack. It uses no equipment and gains no benefit from armor or shields. Its size modifier to AC becomes that of the swarm's new size and its natural armor drops as shown on Table 2-12. It loses any special attack that depends on the base creature's size, Strength, weapons, combat maneuver bonus or reach, and keeps the rest, including ranged and area attacks, at the base creature's own parameters and damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.62
Hive Mind	KEY:Hive Mind ~ Creature Swarm	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:If the base creature has Intelligence 3 or higher, the swarm has a hive mind. It keeps its Intelligence score while it has at least 1 hit point per HD; below that it becomes mindless and immune to mind-affecting effects.	SOURCEPAGE:p.63
Swarm Attack	KEY:Creature Swarm ~ Swarm Attack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:The swarm loses the base creature's melee and ranged attacks and gains the swarm attack of the swarm subtype. Any extra damage the base creature's natural attacks dealt, such as fire damage or energy drain, is added to the swarm attack; where several attacks carried different extra damage, the swarm attack carries all of it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.62

###Block: Crystal Creature, Daemon-Host
Immunity to Light	KEY:Immunity to Light ~ Crystal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A crystal creature is immune to the harmful effects of bright light, including effects that blind with light, to all effects with the light descriptor, and to light-based attacks such as color spray, prismatic spray and searing light. It also loses light blindness and light sensitivity, and any sonic resistance or immunity it had.	SOURCEPAGE:p.64
Vulnerability to Sonic	KEY:Vulnerability to Sonic ~ Crystal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A crystal creature takes half again as much damage (+50%%) from sonic damage, regardless of whether a saving throw is allowed or whether the save succeeds.	SOURCEPAGE:p.64
Brilliant Pestilence	KEY:Brilliant Pestilence ~ Crystal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:All of a crystal creature's natural attacks carry a supernatural disease. Brilliant pestilence: all natural attacks--injury; save Fortitude negates; onset 1 day; frequency 1 day; effect 1d6 Dex damage; cure 2 consecutive saves. The save DC is Charisma-based. A creature reduced to Dexterity 0 is petrified into lifeless crystal and revives 24 hours later as a crystal creature; only a miracle or wish, or similar magic, can change it back.	SOURCEPAGE:p.64
Dazzling Form	KEY:Dazzling Form ~ Crystal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.Aura	DESC:Within the area of a crystal creature's light amplification, all sighted creatures are dazzled for 1 minute if they fail an initial Fortitude save. Once dazzled, a creature that stays in the area must save every round or be permanently blinded (Fortitude negates). The DC rises by +2 in bright light and by +2 in a light effect the crystal creature is immune to, and these stack. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.65
Light Amplification	KEY:Light Amplification ~ Crystal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A crystal creature's body captures and magnifies the light striking it. In dim light or brighter it sheds light one step higher in a 30-foot radius; in bright light it sheds bright light in a 60-foot radius.	SOURCEPAGE:p.65
Slam	KEY:Crystal Creature ~ Slam	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A crystal creature with no other natural attacks gains a primary slam attack. Its slam deals damage as though the creature were one size category larger.	SOURCEPAGE:p.64
+4 bonus on saves against disease and poison	KEY:Daemon-Host ~ Disease and Poison Saves	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality	ASPECT:SaveBonus|+4 vs. disease and poison	SOURCEPAGE:p.66
Regeneration	KEY:Daemon-Host ~ Regeneration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A daemon host has regeneration 5, bypassed by good weapons and effects.	SOURCEPAGE:p.66
Immunity to Death Effects	KEY:Daemon-Host ~ Death Immunity	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A daemon host is immune to death effects.	SOURCEPAGE:p.66
Ability Score Bonuses	KEY:Daemon-Host ~ Chosen Ability Bonuses	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An olethrodaemon host gains +4 to one ability score and +2 to any two others; the bonuses may all be applied to the same score. A purrodaemon host gains +2 to any three different ability scores. Apply the chosen bonuses by hand.	SOURCEPAGE:p.67
Daemon Doom	KEY:Daemon Doom ~ Daemon-Host	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:Daemons wear down the creatures they inhabit: a daemon host takes 1 hp of drain each day, with no save. The drain cannot be healed by rest or magic and lasts until the daemon leaves or the host dies. On the host's death the daemon devours its soul and returns to its origin, and the base creature can then only be restored by wish, miracle or true resurrection. The drain can be staved off for one day per sentient creature (Int 3 or higher) killed in the manner associated with the daemon, up to the base creature's Wisdom modifier in days (minimum 1). The deaths are: astradaemon energy drain or level drain, crucidaemon torture or trap, derghodaemon violent insanity, hydrodaemon drowning, leukodaemon disease, maladaemon starvation, olethrodaemon apocalypse or natural disaster, piscodaemon poison, purrodaemon battle during warfare, thanadaemon old age or aging effects, vulnudaemon murder.	SOURCEPAGE:p.66
Daemon Call	KEY:Daemon Call ~ Daemon-Host	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A daemon host is a living conduit for daemons. Once a day it can use the summon universal monster ability to call daemons whose total Hit Dice do not exceed its own, none of a kind more powerful than the daemon it hosts, and no more than three of the same type at once. The summon level is half the host's HD (maximum 9), and the chance of success is 15%% times the ability modifier used for its other spell-like ability save DCs (minimum 1, maximum 100%%).	SOURCEPAGE:p.67
Daemonic Soul	KEY:Daemonic Soul ~ Daemon-Host	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The daemon's soul and the base creature's are intertwined. The daemon can be removed by casting dispel evil, protection from evil and atonement together on the creature in a hallowed area; the daemon gets a Will save against DC 15 + the caster's Wisdom or Charisma modifier, whichever is higher. On a failure the daemon is separated and returns to its own plane, and the base creature dies but can be raised normally without the template. A wish or miracle removes the daemon with no save and leaves the host alive.	SOURCEPAGE:p.68
Killing Heal	KEY:Killing Heal ~ Daemon-Host	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:When a daemon host directly kills a sentient creature (Int 3 or higher) in the manner associated with its daemon, it heals 1d8 hp per creature killed, up to its maximum hit points.	SOURCEPAGE:p.68

###Block: Demon-Possessed
+4 profane bonus on saves against poison	KEY:Demon-Possessed ~ Poison Saves	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality	ASPECT:SaveBonus|+4 profane vs. poison	SOURCEPAGE:p.69
Profane Attacks	KEY:Profane Attacks ~ Demon-Possessed	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Each melee attack with a natural or manufactured weapon deals an extra %1d6 points of damage to good creatures, one die per point of the template's CR bonus. All the creature's natural and manufactured weapons count as magic, chaotic and evil-aligned for overcoming damage reduction.|DemonPossessedProfaneDice	SOURCEPAGE:p.69
Borrowed Power	KEY:Borrowed Power ~ Demon-Possessed	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:If the possessing demon has the summon ability, the possessed creature gains it too, at half the demon's chance of success and only once a day. The creature also gains one of the demon's supernatural attacks or special qualities that does not depend on another of the demon's abilities; the choice is permanent. The chosen ability is usable once per day and every numeric factor except save DCs is halved. If it depends on a particular natural attack, the creature gains that attack but only delivers the effect once a day. A permanent defense or aura, such as a babau's protective slime, can be activated and dismissed at will but still only once a day. Effects that trigger automatically, such as a balor's death throes, work normally with halved numbers. The creature is immune to its own chosen ability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.69
Ability Score Bonuses	KEY:Demon-Possessed ~ Chosen Ability Bonuses	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A balor-, marilith-, shemhazian- or vrolikai-possessed creature gains +4 to any three different ability scores. Apply the chosen bonuses by hand.	SOURCEPAGE:p.70
Possessed	KEY:Possessed ~ Demon-Possessed	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A specific demon inhabits the creature. It can neither control the possessed creature nor read its mind, and perceives only what the creature does, but the two are in constant telepathic communication regardless of language, and the demon usually offers suggestions a chaotic evil creature would find appealing. While possessing, the demon has no access to its own supernatural, spell-like or extraordinary abilities, cannot cast spells and can take no mental action beyond thinking and using Intelligence-based skills. It cannot be targeted by spells, except as described under spell vulnerability, but divination detects it normally. Damage to the host does not harm it, and if the host dies the demon returns to its plane unharmed. The demon can enter or leave as a standard action, appearing in the nearest open space; killed outside the host, it returns to its plane and the possession ends.	SOURCEPAGE:p.71
Spell Vulnerability	KEY:Spell Vulnerability ~ Demon-Possessed	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A demon-possessed creature subjected to dispel chaos or dispel evil must succeed on a Will save or lose all the template's modifications for a number of rounds equal to the opponent's caster level, and the demon is immediately ejected into the nearest open square. Subjected to banishment, it must succeed on a Will save or lose the template until possessed again, the demon returning to its home plane. An antimagic field or effect suppresses the whole template and also stops the demon communicating, perceiving, or leaving the body unless it dies, for as long as the creature stays in the area.	SOURCEPAGE:p.69

###Block: Dread Allip, Allip, Dread Bodak, Bodak, Dread Devourer, Devourer
Babble	KEY:Babble ~ Dread Allip	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:A dread allip constantly mutters and whines to itself with a hypnotic effect. All sane creatures within 60 feet must succeed on a Will save or be affected as by a hypnotism spell for 2d4 rounds; a creature that saves is immune to that allip's babble for 24 hours. While the allip casts a spell with a verbal component the babble is negated and anyone already hypnotized is freed. This is a sonic, mind-affecting compulsion effect with a Charisma-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.72
Touch of Insanity	KEY:Touch of Insanity ~ Dread Allip	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:All the base creature's natural attacks become incorporeal touch attacks, keeping their primary or secondary status, and a dread allip with no natural attacks gains a primary incorporeal touch. Each touch deals 1d6 points of Wisdom damage (Will negates); a critical hit deals 1d6 Wisdom damage plus 1d4 Wisdom drain instead of doubling the damage. The allip gains 5 temporary hit points per point of Wisdom damage or drain. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.73
Touch of Insanity	KEY:Touch of Insanity ~ Allip	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As the dread allip's touch of insanity, but it deals 1d4 points of Wisdom damage and a critical hit drains 1 point of Wisdom. The allip gains 5 temporary hit points for each successful attack rather than per point of damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.74
Command Allips	KEY:Command Allips ~ Dread Allip	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a free action, a dread allip automatically commands all normal allips within 30 feet, as the command undead spell. Normal allips never attack a dread allip unless compelled.	SOURCEPAGE:p.72
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Dread Allip	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A creature that dies while dominated by a dread allip rises as a new dread allip in 1d6 rounds if it committed suicide, died fulfilling an obviously self-destructive command, or had 0 Wisdom and was within 30 feet at the time of death. The new dread allip regains its normal Wisdom score at once and is under the command, as dominate monster, of the allip that dominated it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.72
Dominating Trample	KEY:Dominating Trample ~ Dread Allip	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once every 1d4 rounds, as a standard action, a dread allip can take a single move in a straight line and dominate the creatures it passes through. Each such creature may make an attack of opportunity or a Reflex save to avoid the attack; failing that, it must succeed on a Will save or be controlled as by dominate monster at caster level 20th, and a success grants immunity to that allip's dominating trample for 24 hours. The allip may give the usual simple commands plus commit suicide, which is an exception to the normal ban on self-destructive orders. A creature so ordered gets a second save at +5 to break free, and a new save at +5 each round; while dominated it attacks itself once per round with its most damaging weapon or natural attack, treated as a coup de grace against a helpless target. Any other command whose obedience would obviously be self-destructive also grants a new save at +5 once that becomes apparent. This is a mind-affecting compulsion effect; the save DCs are Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.72
Madness	KEY:Madness ~ Dread Allip	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:Any creature that targets a dread allip with a thought-detecting, mind-control or telepathic effect takes 1d6 points of Wisdom damage with no save, though the effect otherwise works normally.	SOURCEPAGE:p.73
Madness	KEY:Madness ~ Allip	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:As the dread allip's madness, but it deals 1d4 points of Wisdom damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.74
Vulnerability to Sunlight	KEY:Vulnerability to Sunlight ~ Dread Bodak	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:Sunlight burns a dread bodak's impure flesh: each round of exposure to direct sunlight deals it 2d6 points of damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.75
Slams	KEY:Dread Bodak ~ Slams	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A dread bodak with no natural attacks gains one slam attack per arm, dealing damage as though the base creature were two size categories larger.	SOURCEPAGE:p.75
Command Bodaks	KEY:Command Bodaks ~ Dread Bodak	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a free action, a dread bodak automatically commands all normal bodaks within 30 feet, as the command undead spell. Normal bodaks never attack a dread bodak unless compelled.	SOURCEPAGE:p.75
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Dread Bodak	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any creature killed by a dread bodak's death wail rises as a dread bodak in 1d6 rounds, under its creator's command as by dominate monster, until one of them is destroyed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.75
Death Wail	KEY:Death Wail ~ Dread Bodak	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A dread bodak can keen to draw the souls of the dying to the afterlife. A dying creature within 100 feet dies instantly and need not hear the keening, though a silence spell blocks the effect. For each creature slain this way the bodak gains 1d8 temporary hit points, a +2 bonus to Strength and a +1 increase in effective caster level for all its spells and spell-like abilities, for 10 minutes. This is a sonic death effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.75
Killing Gaze	KEY:Killing Gaze ~ Dread Bodak	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Reduced to -1 hp, 30 feet, Fortitude negates. The save DC is Charisma-based. This is a death and gaze effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.76
Death Gaze	KEY:Death Gaze ~ Bodak	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:1d4 negative levels, 30 feet, Fortitude negates. The save DC is Charisma-based. A creature slain by this gaze rises as a bodak 24 hours later. This is a death and gaze effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.76
Spell Deflection	KEY:Spell Deflection ~ Dread Devourer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:If banishment, chaos hammer, confusion, crushing despair, detect thoughts, dispel evil, dominate person, fear, geas/quest, holy word, hypnotism, imprisonment, magic jar, maze, suggestion, trap the soul, or any charm or compulsion is cast at the devourer and overcomes its spell resistance, it affects a trapped soul instead. The soul is not harmed, but the caster makes a DC 25 caster level check; on a success the trapped soul is released and the creature it belonged to can be restored to life normally.	SOURCEPAGE:p.77
Slams	KEY:Dread Devourer ~ Slams	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A dread devourer with no other natural attacks gains one primary slam per hand or limb, dealing damage as though the base creature were one size larger. It also gains a single touch attack for its devour soul ability. All its attacks, natural and manufactured, count as evil-aligned for overcoming damage reduction, and every natural attack except the devour soul touch gains energy drain (1 level) with a Charisma-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.77
Devour Soul	KEY:Devour Soul ~ Dread Devourer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:With a touch attack as a standard action, a dread devourer deals 12d6 + 1 point per caster level of damage as a slay living spell; a Fortitude save reduces this to 3d6 + 1 point per caster level. Its caster level is its total HD + 4 + 2 per soul trapped within it. The soul of a creature slain this way is trapped in the devourer's chest and cannot be brought back to life until the devourer is destroyed or a spell deflection releases it. A dread devourer can hold a number of souls equal to its HD. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.78
Devour Soul	KEY:Devour Soul ~ Devourer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As the dread devourer's devour soul, but a devourer can hold only one soul at a time and its caster level is its total HD + 4.	SOURCEPAGE:p.79
Essence Points	KEY:Essence Points ~ Dread Devourer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A trapped soul provides 5 essence points per Hit Die it possessed. The devourer spends essence points equal to a spell's level to use its spell-like abilities: animate dead (4th), circle of death (6th), confusion (4th), control undead (7th), create undead (6th), deeper darkness (3rd), desecrate (2nd), dominate monster (9th), horrid wilting (8th), inflict serious wounds (3rd), lesser planar ally (4th), plane shift (7th, self only, five essence points), ray of enfeeblement (1st) and true seeing (6th), all at will and with Charisma-based save DCs. At the start of an encounter a dread devourer usually has one soul and 3d4+3 essence points. The trapped essence takes one permanent negative level for every 5 points drained, which remain if the creature is brought back to life and do not stack with the levels from being raised. A soul consumed entirely can only be restored by miracle or wish.	SOURCEPAGE:p.78
Command Devourers	KEY:Command Devourers ~ Dread Devourer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a free action, a dread devourer automatically commands all normal devourers within 30 feet, as the command undead spell. Normal devourers never attack a dread devourer unless compelled.	SOURCEPAGE:p.77

###Block: Dread Ghast, Ghast, Dread Ghost, Dread Ghoul, Ghoul
Stench	KEY:Stench ~ Dread Ghast	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.Aura	DESC:A dread ghast has the stench universal monster ability in a 20-foot radius; a creature that fails a Charisma-based Fortitude save is sickened for 1d6+4 minutes.	SOURCEPAGE:p.80
Stench	KEY:Stench ~ Ghast	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.Aura	DESC:A ghast has the stench universal monster ability in a 10-foot radius; a creature that fails a Charisma-based Fortitude save is sickened for 1d6+4 minutes.	SOURCEPAGE:p.82
Unnatural Aura	KEY:Unnatural Aura ~ Dread Ghast	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:Animals do not willingly approach a dread ghast within 30 feet unless their master succeeds on a DC 25 Handle Animal, Ride or wild empathy check.	SOURCEPAGE:p.80
Paralysis	KEY:Paralysis ~ Dread Ghast	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:All the base creature's natural attacks gain paralysis (1d4+1 rounds).	SOURCEPAGE:p.80
Paralysis	KEY:Paralysis ~ Dread Ghoul	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:All the base creature's natural attacks gain paralysis (1d4+1 rounds). Elves are not immune to a dread ghoul's paralysis.	SOURCEPAGE:p.86
Paralysis	KEY:Paralysis ~ Ghoul	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:All the base creature's natural attacks gain paralysis (1d4+1 rounds). Elves are immune to a ghoul's paralysis.	SOURCEPAGE:p.88
Ghoul Fever	KEY:Ghoul Fever ~ Ghoul	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any bite attack carries ghoul fever--injury; save Fortitude; onset 1 day; frequency 1/day; effect 1d3 Con and 1d3 Dex damage; cure 2 consecutive saves.	SOURCEPAGE:p.88
Ghoulish Attacks	KEY:Ghoulish Attacks ~ Dread Ghast	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:If the base creature has at least one mouth and no natural attack with it, it gains a bite attack per mouth, primary if it had no natural attacks and secondary otherwise. If it has at least one arm with no natural attack other than a slam, it gains a primary claw attack with each such limb, and existing arm slams become claws. Damage follows the base creature's size, and any bite or claw granted by the template deals damage as though the creature were one size larger.	SOURCEPAGE:p.80
Ghoulish Climb	KEY:Ghoulish Climb ~ Dread Ghast	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:If the base creature has both a climb and a land speed, the climb speed rises to match the land speed unless already higher. If it lacks one, it gains the missing mode at the other's speed. If it lacks both, it gains both at half its highest speed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.80
Command Ghasts and Ghouls	KEY:Command Ghasts and Ghouls ~ Dread Ghast	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a free action, a dread ghast automatically commands all normal ghasts and ghouls within 30 feet, as the command undead spell. They never attack a dread ghast unless compelled.	SOURCEPAGE:p.80
Command Ghouls	KEY:Command Ghouls ~ Dread Ghoul	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a free action, a dread ghoul automatically commands all normal ghouls within 30 feet, as the command undead spell. Normal ghouls never attack a dread ghoul unless compelled.	SOURCEPAGE:p.86
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Dread Ghast	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any creature killed by a dread ghast that lies undisturbed until the next midnight rises then as a dread ghast, not under its creator's control. A protection from evil or gentle repose spell on the corpse prevents this.	SOURCEPAGE:p.80
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Dread Ghoul	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Dread ghouls usually feast on the fallen, but any creature killed by one that lies undisturbed until the next midnight rises then as a dread ghoul, not under its creator's control. A protection from evil or gentle repose spell on the corpse prevents this.	SOURCEPAGE:p.87
Improved Rejuvenation	KEY:Improved Rejuvenation ~ Dread Ghost	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:A dread ghost destroyed in combat restores itself in 1d4 hours, and even powerful spells are only a temporary solution. The only permanent way to destroy it is to find the reason for its existence and set right whatever keeps it from resting; the means differ for each spirit and are for the GM to devise.	SOURCEPAGE:p.83
Ghostly Form	KEY:Ghostly Form ~ Dread Ghost	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A dread ghost loses the base creature's natural armor and all armor and shield bonuses that are not force effects or ghost touch items, gaining instead a deflection bonus equal to its Charisma modifier (minimum +1). It loses all the base creature's attacks, though if it could wield weapons in life it can wield ghost touch weapons. Special attacks that rely on physical contact do not function. It gains a fly speed of double the base creature's highest speed with perfect maneuverability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.83
Corrupting Touch	KEY:Corrupting Touch ~ Dread Ghost	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Every dread ghost has this incorporeal touch attack. By passing part of its body through a foe as a standard action it deals a number of d8s of damage equal to its CR. The damage is not negative energy but physical wounds and aches from supernatural aging; creatures immune to magical aging are immune to it, and otherwise it bypasses all damage reduction. A Fortitude save halves the damage. A dread ghost gains one special attack from the dread ghost list per 3 points of CR, minimum 1, and corrupting touch is always the first.	SOURCEPAGE:p.84
Aligned Attacks	KEY:Dread Ghost ~ Aligned Attacks	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DreadGhostAbility	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	DESC:The dread ghost held strong-aligned convictions in life. All its attacks count as magic and aligned for overcoming damage reduction, matching one component of its own alignment chosen at creation, and it gains the matching alignment subtype. Its attacks also deal +1d6 damage per 2 HD (maximum 10d6) to creatures of the opposing alignment. This can be taken once for each component of the ghost's alignment.	SOURCEPAGE:p.83
Chilling Aura	KEY:Dread Ghost ~ Chilling Aura	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DreadGhostAbility	DESC:The dread ghost died in the cold or was emotionally distant in life. When it manifests it emits a deadly chill in a 20-foot radius on both the Material and Ethereal Planes, dealing 3d6 points of cold damage per round, halved on a successful Fortitude save. It is immune to its own aura and to those of other dread ghosts.	SOURCEPAGE:p.83
Corrupting Gaze	KEY:Dread Ghost ~ Corrupting Gaze	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DreadGhostAbility	DESC:The dread ghost is disfigured through age or violence. It has a gaze attack with a range of 60 feet dealing 4d10 damage and 1d6 Charisma damage; a Fortitude save negates the Charisma damage but not the physical damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.83
Death Wail	KEY:Dread Ghost ~ Death Wail	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DreadGhostAbility	DESC:The dread ghost died in psychological torment. Once every 1d4 rounds, as a full-round action, it wails at one creature within 100 feet; if that creature can hear it, it must succeed on a Fortitude save or be reduced to -1 hp and dying. Every other creature within 100 feet that hears the wail must succeed on the same save or gain 1 negative level. A creature that saves is immune to that ghost's death wail for 24 hours. This is a sonic death effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.84
Draining Touch	KEY:Dread Ghost ~ Draining Touch	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DreadGhostAbility	DESC:The dread ghost died insane or diseased. It gains a touch attack that drains 1d2 points from each of two different ability scores of its choice on a hit; a successful Fortitude save turns the drain into damage. Each successful attack heals the ghost 5 points of damage. While using draining touch it cannot use corrupting touch.	SOURCEPAGE:p.84
Frightful Moan	KEY:Dread Ghost ~ Frightful Moan	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DreadGhostAbility	DESC:The dread ghost died in the throes of crippling terror. As a standard action it emits a moan; all living creatures within a 30-foot spread must succeed on a Will save or be panicked for 4d4 rounds. A creature that saves is immune to that ghost's moan for 24 hours. This is a sonic mind-affecting fear effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.84
Horrific Appearance	KEY:Dread Ghost ~ Horrific Appearance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DreadGhostAbility	DESC:The dread ghost died extremely violently or was mutilated. Any living creature within 60 feet that sees it must succeed on a Fortitude save or take 1d4 points of Strength, Dexterity and Constitution damage, rolled separately. A creature that saves is immune to that ghost's horrific appearance for 24 hours. This is a gaze effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.84
Invisibility	KEY:Dread Ghost ~ Invisibility	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DreadGhostAbility	DESC:The dread ghost can use greater invisibility, as the spell, at will.	SOURCEPAGE:p.84
Malevolence	KEY:Dread Ghost ~ Malevolence	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DreadGhostAbility	DESC:The ghost's jealousy of the living is particularly potent. Once per round it can merge its body with an adjacent creature on the Material Plane, as a magic jar spell at caster level 15th or its Hit Dice, whichever is higher, but without a receptacle. The target resists with a Will save and, on a success, is immune to that ghost's malevolence for 24 hours.	SOURCEPAGE:p.84
Power over Undead	KEY:Dread Ghost ~ Power over Undead	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DreadGhostAbility	DESC:The dread ghost was a leader of renown or died leading others. It can enslave other undead within 30 feet, as the Command Undead feat using its total HD for the DC, 3 + its Charisma modifier times per day (minimum 0).	SOURCEPAGE:p.84
Shattering Presence	KEY:Dread Ghost ~ Shattering Presence	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DreadGhostAbility	DESC:The dread ghost died by bludgeoning or in a great fall. As a full-round action it releases a burst of pure force dealing 6d6 damage to all nonmagical objects in a 30-foot burst; objects weighing more than 5 pounds per character level of the ghost are unaffected, and a magic item must succeed on a Fortitude save or take the damage. Constructs, crystalline and otherwise fragile creatures in the area take 1d6 damage per 3 HD of the ghost (maximum 6d6), halved on a successful Reflex save; undead and living creatures are unaffected. Objects destroyed or creatures killed shatter in a 5-foot burst of shards, and every creature in range must succeed on a DC 20 Reflex save or take 1d6 points of slashing damage; a creature wearing or carrying a shattering object takes 2d6 points of slashing damage with no save. This is a force effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.85

###Block: Dread Lacedon, Lacedon, Dread Lich, Dread Mohrg, Mohrg
Grab and Paralysis	KEY:Grab and Paralysis ~ Dread Lacedon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:All of a dread lacedon's natural attacks gain the grab universal monster ability and paralysis (1d4+1 rounds). The save DC is Charisma-based. Appendix C on page 308 lists the dread lacedon at +3 CR; this template follows its own entry on page 89, which says +2.	SOURCEPAGE:p.89
Lacedon Swim	KEY:Lacedon Swim ~ Dread Lacedon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:If the base creature has both a swim and a land speed, the lower rises to match the higher. If it lacks one, it gains the missing mode at the other's speed. If it lacks both, it gains both at half its highest speed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.89
Command Lacedons and Ghouls	KEY:Command Lacedons and Ghouls ~ Dread Lacedon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a free action, a dread lacedon automatically commands all normal lacedons and ghouls within 30 feet, as the command undead spell. They never attack a dread lacedon unless compelled.	SOURCEPAGE:p.89
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Dread Lacedon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any creature killed by a dread lacedon that lies undisturbed until the next midnight rises then as a dread lacedon, under its creator's control as by dominate monster if the creator is within 30 feet at that moment. A protection from evil or gentle repose spell on the corpse prevents this.	SOURCEPAGE:p.89
Nauseating Flesh	KEY:Nauseating Flesh ~ Dread Lacedon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:A creature that damages a dread lacedon with a bite, swallows one whole, or otherwise eats its flesh must succeed on a DC 20 Fortitude save or be nauseated for 1 day; a success reduces the nausea to 1d4 rounds. Remove disease or purify food and drink negates it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.89
Dread Fear Aura	KEY:Dread Fear Aura ~ Dread Lich	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:A creature of fewer than 5 HD within 60 feet that looks upon a dread lich must succeed on a Will save or be panicked; a creature of 5 HD or more must save or be frightened for a number of rounds equal to the lich's total Hit Dice. A creature that saves is immune to that lich's aura for 24 hours. This is a mind-affecting fear effect with a Charisma-based save DC. On a base creature that is already a lich, this replaces its fear aura.	SOURCEPAGE:p.91
Stable Form	KEY:Stable Form ~ Dread Lich	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:A dread lich is immune to all polymorph effects except those it casts on itself.	SOURCEPAGE:p.92
Rejuvenation	KEY:Rejuvenation ~ Dread Lich	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:When a dread lich is destroyed, its phylactery immediately begins rebuilding its body nearby, a process taking 1d10 days; destroying the body before then simply restarts it. The lich then wakes fully healed, though without any gear left on its old body.	SOURCEPAGE:p.92
Phylactery	KEY:Phylactery ~ Dread Lich	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A dread lich stores its life force in a phylactery it must craft itself, requiring Craft Wondrous Item, the ability to cast spells or use spell-like abilities, and caster level 15th or higher. It costs 200,000 gp and has the creator's caster level. The usual form is a Tiny mithral box with hardness 20, 40 hit points and break DC 40, though rings, amulets and similar items also occur, and powerful magic such as wish or miracle can make another nonliving creature, but never another dread lich, into the phylactery. Unless the phylactery is found and destroyed, the lich reforms beside it 1d4 days after its apparent death, at any distance but only on the same plane; on a different plane, it reforms 1d4 days after the phylactery is brought to the plane where the lich was destroyed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.91
Touch Attack	KEY:Dread Lich ~ Touch Attack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:All a dread lich's natural attacks count as magic and evil-aligned for overcoming damage reduction. A dread lich that was not already a lich gains a touch attack usable once per round: fighting unarmed it counts as a primary natural weapon replacing one claw or slam, and armed it is a secondary natural weapon. The touch deals 1d10 points of negative energy damage to living creatures plus 1 point per 2 Hit Dice, which instead heals undead; the lich can take a full-round action to infuse itself and heal as though it had touched itself.	SOURCEPAGE:p.92
Cursed Touch	KEY:Cursed Touch ~ Dread Lich	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any living creature hit by a dread lich's touch attack must succeed on a Fortitude save or be paralyzed and struck by a death curse. The curse must be removed before the paralysis can be, and it drains 1 point of Constitution per day, which cannot be restored while the curse lasts; at Constitution 0 the victim disintegrates into ash and bone, recoverable only by true resurrection, miracle or wish. Once the curse is lifted, remove paralysis frees the victim; if either attempt fails, the victim's Constitution drops to 0 at once and it dies. Neither effect can otherwise be dispelled. A victim appears dead, though a DC 20 Perception or DC 15 Heal check reveals otherwise. Creatures immune to paralysis, other than dread liches, still suffer the curse. Both the save DC and the DC to remove the curse are Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.92
Empowered Spells	KEY:Empowered Spells ~ Dread Lich	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:All a dread lich's necromancy spells, spells with the evil descriptor and spell-like abilities are automatically affected as if by the Empower Spell feat, without higher-level slots or longer casting times. Empower Spell cannot augment them further.	SOURCEPAGE:p.92
Strong Spellweaving	KEY:Strong Spellweaving ~ Dread Lich	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A -4 penalty applies to any dispel check made against a spell cast by a dread lich.	SOURCEPAGE:p.93
Paralysis	KEY:Paralysis ~ Dread Mohrg	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Each of a dread mohrg's natural attacks carries paralysis (1d4+4 rounds).	SOURCEPAGE:p.94
Tongue and Slams	KEY:Tongue and Slams ~ Dread Mohrg	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A dread mohrg gains two primary slam attacks if it has no other natural attacks, and a primary tongue attack for each head. The tongue deals damage as a gore attack of a creature one size larger and has 5 feet more reach than the base creature; slams granted by the template deal damage as though the base creature were three size categories larger.	SOURCEPAGE:p.94
Tongue and Slams	KEY:Tongue and Slams ~ Mohrg	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A mohrg gains two primary slam attacks if it has no other natural attacks, and a tongue attack for each head. The tongue is a melee touch attack that deals no damage and has no extra reach. Slams granted by the template deal damage as though the base creature were three size categories larger. All the mohrg's natural melee attacks except the tongue gain grab.	SOURCEPAGE:p.96
Command Mohrgs and Zombies	KEY:Command Mohrgs and Zombies ~ Dread Mohrg	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a free action, a dread mohrg automatically commands all normal mohrgs and zombies within 30 feet, as the command undead spell. They never attack a dread mohrg unless compelled.	SOURCEPAGE:p.94
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Dread Mohrg	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any living creature of the dread mohrg's size or smaller that it kills rises immediately as an advanced fast zombie under its control, as by dominate monster. The surge of negative energy heals the dread mohrg 1d6 hit points per HD of the slain creature and leaves it hasted for the round after the spawn appears.	SOURCEPAGE:p.94
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Mohrg	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A mohrg gains the standard mohrg's create spawn ability, but it applies only to creatures of its own original type.	SOURCEPAGE:p.96
Clumsy Wings	KEY:Clumsy Wings ~ Dread Mohrg	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:If the base creature flies with wings, its maneuverability drops one step, to a minimum of clumsy. A fly speed from a supernatural source is unchanged.	SOURCEPAGE:p.94

###Block: Dread Mummy, Mummy, Dread Poltergeist, Poltergeist
Vulnerability to Fire	KEY:Vulnerability to Fire ~ Dread Mummy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A dread mummy takes half again as much damage (+50%%) from fire, regardless of whether a saving throw is allowed or whether the save succeeds.	SOURCEPAGE:p.97
Greater Despair	KEY:Greater Despair ~ Dread Mummy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:Any creature within 100 feet of a dread mummy must succeed on a Fortitude save or be paralyzed by fear for 1d4 rounds, then staggered for 1 more round on recovering. Whether or not the save succeeds, that creature cannot be affected again by the same mummy's despair for 24 hours. This is a paralysis and mind-affecting fear effect with a Charisma-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.97
Despair	KEY:Despair ~ Mummy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:A mummy gains the standard mummy's despair aura in place of greater despair.	SOURCEPAGE:p.99
Mummy Rot	KEY:Mummy Rot ~ Dread Mummy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:All the creature's natural attacks transmit mummy rot--curse and disease; save Fortitude; onset 1 minute; frequency 1/day; effect 1d6 Con and 1d6 Cha; cure none. Mummy rot is both curse and disease: the curse must be removed before the disease can be, and even then the victim cannot recover naturally. Anyone casting a conjuration (healing) spell on the victim must succeed on a DC 20 caster level check or waste the spell. A creature that dies from mummy rot turns to dust and cannot be raised without resurrection or greater magic. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.97
Slam	KEY:Dread Mummy ~ Slam	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A dread mummy with no other natural attacks gains a primary slam attack dealing damage as though the base creature were two size categories larger.	SOURCEPAGE:p.97
Breath of Death	KEY:Breath of Death ~ Dread Mummy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once every 1d4 rounds a dread mummy can breathe a 30-foot cone of tomb gas, sand and dust. Each living creature in the area must succeed on a Fortitude save or gain 1d4 negative levels. A creature killed by it rises as a juju zombie or dread zombie in 1d4 rounds, under its creator's command as by command undead until one of them is destroyed. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.97
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Dread Mummy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any creature killed by a dread mummy's mummy rot turns to dust and blows away. If the dread mummy that infected it is not destroyed within a week, the dust reforms as a new dread mummy under its creator's command, as by dominate monster, until one of them is destroyed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.97
Natural Invisibility	KEY:Natural Invisibility ~ Dread Poltergeist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:A dread poltergeist is naturally invisible. This is an ongoing effect, not a spell, and it cannot be dispelled.	SOURCEPAGE:p.100
Rejuvenation	KEY:Rejuvenation ~ Dread Poltergeist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:A destroyed dread poltergeist stays destroyed for only 2d4 days, then reforms fully healed where it fell. The only way to destroy it permanently is to find the reason for its existence and set right whatever keeps it from resting; the means differ for each spirit and are for the GM to devise.	SOURCEPAGE:p.100
Manipulation	KEY:Manipulation ~ Dread Poltergeist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Although incorporeal, a dread poltergeist can use and carry equipment as it did in life, up to 10 pounds per Hit Die. It can wear armor, use weapons and benefit from worn magic items with no encumbrance, no armor check penalty and no arcane spell failure chance. Its items stay visible and corporeal and cannot travel with it through objects and creatures. While manipulating objects it can perform all combat maneuvers normally forbidden to incorporeal creatures. An opponent can grab its clothing or armor with a successful combat maneuver; the poltergeist then chooses either to move with the garments or to stay put and lose them.	SOURCEPAGE:p.101
Poltergeist Touch	KEY:Poltergeist Touch ~ Dread Poltergeist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:All the base creature's attacks become incorporeal touch attacks, keeping their primary or secondary status, and a poltergeist with no natural attacks gains a primary incorporeal touch. These touches deal slashing damage unmodified by Strength, as a talon attack of a creature one size larger. It can also use weapons appropriate to its size.	SOURCEPAGE:p.100
Poltergeist Strength	KEY:Poltergeist Strength ~ Dread Poltergeist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:If the base creature's Strength was higher than its Dexterity, the poltergeist's Dexterity becomes equal to that Strength. It uses the base creature's CMB and CMD when manipulating objects, substituting its Charisma bonus for the Strength bonus, and satisfies any feat prerequisite that called for a Strength score with its Dexterity instead.	SOURCEPAGE:p.101
Frightener	KEY:Frightener ~ Dread Poltergeist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once per minute, as a standard action, a dread poltergeist can drop its natural invisibility to reveal a skeletal, ghostlike shape. All creatures within 30 feet must make a Will save or be frightened for 1d4 rounds; it resumes invisibility at the end of its turn as a free action. A creature that saves is immune to that poltergeist's frightener for 24 hours but remains subject to its terrifying and killing images. The ability cannot be used if the poltergeist's invisibility is already negated, and creatures that see invisible are immune. This is a mind-affecting fear effect; the Charisma-based save DC gains a +3 racial bonus.	SOURCEPAGE:p.100
Frightener	KEY:Frightener ~ Poltergeist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As the dread poltergeist's frightener, but without the +3 racial bonus to the save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.102
Terrifying Image	KEY:Terrifying Image ~ Dread Poltergeist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:At will, the poltergeist can produce an effect like major image at a caster level equal to its total Hit Dice, and can make the image extremely frightening. A creature that first sees or hears such an illusion must succeed on a Will save or be affected as by a fear spell; a creature that saves is immune to that poltergeist's terrifying image for 24 hours. This is a mind-affecting fear effect; the Charisma-based save DC gains a +3 racial bonus.	SOURCEPAGE:p.101
Killing Image	KEY:Killing Image ~ Dread Poltergeist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once per day a dread poltergeist can turn its terrifying image into a deadly manifestation, identical to a phantasmal killer spell but affecting everyone who can directly see or hear the poltergeist. Targets must save against the killing image even if they already saved against the terrifying image. The caster level equals the poltergeist's total Hit Dice, and the Charisma-based save DC gains a +3 racial bonus.	SOURCEPAGE:p.101
Site Bound	KEY:Site Bound ~ Dread Poltergeist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A dread poltergeist must stay within 300 feet of the site where its living form died. Taken beyond that range it vanishes at once and reappears near the centre of its domain a round later.	SOURCEPAGE:p.101
Site Bound	KEY:Site Bound ~ Poltergeist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:As the dread poltergeist's site bound, but the range is 120 feet.	SOURCEPAGE:p.102

###Block: Dread Shadow, Shadow, Greater Shadow, Dread Greater Shadow, Dread Skeleton, Dread Spectre, Spectre
Shadow Touch	KEY:Shadow Touch ~ Dread Shadow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A dread shadow loses all attacks with manufactured weapons, and its natural attacks become incorporeal touch attacks keeping their primary or secondary status; with no natural attacks it gains a primary incorporeal touch. These touches deal no normal damage, only Strength damage. A dread shadow cannot cast spells with material components unless it has Eschew Materials.	SOURCEPAGE:p.103
Strength Damage	KEY:Strength Damage ~ Dread Shadow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A creature struck by the incorporeal touch takes Strength damage by size: Fine to Tiny 1d4, Small to Large 1d6, Huge to Colossal 1d8. This is a negative energy effect, and a creature dies if the Strength damage equals or exceeds its actual Strength score.	SOURCEPAGE:p.104
Strength Damage	KEY:Strength Damage ~ Greater Shadow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A creature struck by the incorporeal touch takes Strength damage by size: Fine to Tiny 1d6, Small to Large 1d8, Huge to Colossal 1d10. This is a negative energy effect, and a creature dies if the Strength damage equals or exceeds its actual Strength score. A greater shadow also gains 6 racial HD, with the feats and skill points that follow; add those by hand.	SOURCEPAGE:p.106
Shadow Stealth	KEY:Shadow Stealth ~ Dread Shadow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A dread shadow gains a +4 bonus on Stealth checks in dim light and takes a -4 penalty on Stealth checks in bright light. If its Intelligence falls below 1 it becomes mindless, losing all skill points and feats and having no Intelligence score.	SOURCEPAGE:p.104
Command Shadows	KEY:Command Shadows ~ Dread Shadow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a free action, a dread shadow automatically commands all normal shadows within 30 feet, as the command undead spell. Normal shadows never attack a dread shadow unless compelled.	SOURCEPAGE:p.103
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Dread Shadow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A creature with Charisma 15 or higher killed by a dread shadow rises as a dread shadow in 1d4 rounds; any other creature rises as a normal shadow. Either is under its creator's command, as by dominate monster, until one of them is destroyed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.104
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Shadow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A creature killed by the shadow rises as a normal shadow in 1d4 rounds, under its creator's command as by dominate monster until one of them is destroyed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.106
Shadow Slip	KEY:Shadow Slip ~ Dread Shadow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:At will, as a move action, a dread shadow can use dimension door at caster level 7th, moving from one place of darkness or shadow to another within line of sight. This does not provoke attacks of opportunity.	SOURCEPAGE:p.104
Bone Frame	KEY:Bone Frame ~ Dread Skeleton	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The base creature's natural armor is replaced by a bonus for the skeleton's size: Tiny or smaller +0, Small +1, Medium or Large +2, Huge +3, Gargantuan +6, Colossal +10. It keeps every attack made with a limb that has bone, teeth or exoskeleton and loses those made with boneless limbs such as tentacles. An arm with no natural attack gains a claw attack, primary if the base creature had no natural attacks and secondary otherwise, dealing damage for the base creature's size.	SOURCEPAGE:p.107
Command Skeletons	KEY:Command Skeletons ~ Dread Skeleton	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a free action, a dread skeleton automatically commands all normal skeletons within 30 feet, as the command undead spell. It may also try to command skeleton warriors, which get a Will save to resist at a caster level equal to the dread skeleton's total HD and a Charisma-based DC. Normal skeletons never attack a dread skeleton unless compelled.	SOURCEPAGE:p.108
Frightful Presence	KEY:Frightful Presence ~ Dread Spectre	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:A dread spectre has frightful presence with a 60-foot range and a Charisma-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.109
Daylight Vulnerability	KEY:Daylight Vulnerability ~ Dread Spectre	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A dread spectre is not powerless in natural daylight and does not flee from it as a normal spectre does, but it takes a -4 penalty on all attack rolls, checks and saves in natural sunlight, though not within the radius of a daylight spell.	SOURCEPAGE:p.109
Sunlight Powerlessness	KEY:Sunlight Powerlessness ~ Spectre	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:In sunlight, though not in the area of a daylight spell or similar, the spectre cannot attack and is staggered.	SOURCEPAGE:p.111
Resurrection Vulnerability	KEY:Resurrection Vulnerability ~ Spectre	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Weakness	DESC:A raise dead or similar spell cast on a spectre destroys it unless it succeeds on a Will save.	SOURCEPAGE:p.111
Spectral Touch	KEY:Spectral Touch ~ Dread Spectre	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:All the base creature's attacks become incorporeal touch attacks, keeping their primary or secondary status, and a spectre with no natural attacks gains a primary incorporeal touch. The touches deal normal damage plus energy drain (2 levels); a touch attack granted by the template deals damage as a slam of a creature two size categories larger. A dread spectre can carry no equipment of any kind and cannot cast spells with material components unless it has Eschew Materials.	SOURCEPAGE:p.109
Command Spectres	KEY:Command Spectres ~ Dread Spectre	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a free action, a dread spectre automatically commands all normal spectres within 30 feet, as the command undead spell. Normal spectres never attack a dread spectre unless compelled.	SOURCEPAGE:p.109
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Dread Spectre	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A creature with Charisma 16 or higher killed by a dread spectre rises as a dread spectre in 1d4 rounds; any other creature rises as a normal spectre. Either is under its creator's command, as by dominate monster, until one of them is destroyed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.109
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Spectre	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A creature killed by the spectre rises as a normal spectre in 1d4 rounds, under its creator's command as by dominate monster until one of them is destroyed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.111

###Block: Dread Vampire
Dread Rejuvenation	KEY:Dread Rejuvenation ~ Dread Vampire	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:Reduced to 0 hit points in combat, a dread vampire assumes gaseous form and flees; it must reach its coffin home within 2 days or be destroyed, travelling up to 9 miles per hour. Further damage in gaseous form has no effect. At rest it is helpless, regains 1 hit point after 1 hour, and then heals at 5 hit points per round. Even a killed dread vampire returns to unlife within 1d4 minutes if its remains are bathed in the blood of a single non-extraplanar good creature with at least as many HD as itself. The way to destroy a given dread vampire permanently is unique to it and is for the GM to devise.	SOURCEPAGE:p.112
Dread Vampire Weaknesses	KEY:Dread Vampire Weaknesses ~ Dread Vampire	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:Garlic and mirrors do not affect a dread vampire, and it ignores a holy symbol unless it is presented by someone of strong faith, meaning a divine caster or someone otherwise favoured by a deity. Presenting a symbol is a standard action; the vampire gets a Wisdom- or Charisma-based Will save, whichever is better, and on a failure it recoils, is staggered, and can neither come within 5 feet of nor act against the presenter, with a new save each round. It cannot enter a private home unless invited by someone with the authority to do so; once invited it is immune to its normal weaknesses in that dwelling for a month or until the invitation is revoked, at which point it is expelled 30 feet from the entrance. Direct sunlight staggers it on the first round and deals 5 hit points per round thereafter, and it gains no fast healing in sunlight. Unless the base creature is aquatic or has a swim speed, each round immersed in running water deals 5 hit points of damage, destroying it at 0. Driving a blessed wooden stake through a helpless dread vampire's heart, a full-round action, slays it instantly; any other wooden stake deals only its normal damage. Removing the blessed stake revives the vampire unless its head has been severed, head and body anointed with holy water, the body sanctified with gentle repose, and the corpse buried in hallowed ground.	SOURCEPAGE:p.112
Vampiric Movement	KEY:Vampiric Movement ~ Dread Vampire	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:If the base creature has both a climb and a land speed, the lower rises to match the higher; if it lacks one, it gains that mode at the other's speed; if it lacks both, it gains both at half its highest speed. A dread vampire that cannot already fly also gains a supernatural fly speed equal to half the base creature's highest speed, with perfect maneuverability. A base creature with a swim speed keeps it and is not vulnerable to immersion in running water.	SOURCEPAGE:p.113
Vampiric Attacks	KEY:Vampiric Attacks ~ Dread Vampire	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A dread vampire with no other natural attacks gains a primary slam attack dealing damage for the base creature's size, and it gains energy drain (2 levels) on any one natural attack type the base creature has. Save DCs are Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.113
Blood Drain	KEY:Blood Drain ~ Dread Vampire	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A dread vampire can drink blood from a living victim with its fangs on a successful grapple CMB roll. While it pins the foe it deals 1d6 points of Constitution damage per round and heals 5 hit points, or gains 5 temporary hit points lasting 1 hour up to its full normal hit points.	SOURCEPAGE:p.113
Children of the Night	KEY:Children of the Night ~ Dread Vampire	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Three times a day, as a standard action, a dread vampire can summon animals, vermin or undead, each with Intelligence 2 or lower, in any combination whose total Hit Dice is less than its own. They arrive in 2d6 rounds and serve for up to 1 hour.	SOURCEPAGE:p.113
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Dread Vampire	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A dread vampire creates spawn only if its victims are kept in coffin homes until they rise, a coffin home being any container that fits the corpse; if a vampire's coffin home is destroyed it cannot reform and is destroyed at 0 hit points. Under those conditions, a creature slain by its energy drain rises as a standard vampire 24 hours later, and a creature of Intelligence 10 or higher whose Constitution reaches 0 from its blood drain rises as a dread vampire 24 hours later. Spawn are commanded as by dominate monster until one of them is destroyed. A dread vampire may enslave vampires totalling no more than three times its own Hit Dice; spawn beyond that limit rise free-willed. An enslaved vampire may create and enslave its own spawn, so a master indirectly controls many. It may free a spawn to enslave a new one, but a freed spawn can never be enslaved again.	SOURCEPAGE:p.113
Dominate	KEY:Dominate ~ Dread Vampire	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a standard action, a dread vampire can crush an opponent's will at a range of 30 feet. The target must succeed on a Will save or fall under its influence as by dominate monster at a caster level equal to the vampire's character level. This is a mind-affecting effect with a Charisma-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.114
Change Shape	KEY:Change Shape ~ Dread Vampire	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:As a standard action, a dread vampire can take the shape of any creature it could summon with children of the night, as the polymorph spell. In that form it loses its dominate ability but keeps every other special attack and quality from this template and gains the natural attacks and extraordinary abilities of the new form. It stays in that form until it assumes another or until the next sunrise.	SOURCEPAGE:p.114
Gaseous Form	KEY:Gaseous Form ~ Dread Vampire	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:As a standard action, a dread vampire can assume gaseous form at will at caster level 5th, remain gaseous indefinitely, and fly at 40 feet with perfect maneuverability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.114
Swarm Shape	KEY:Swarm Shape ~ Dread Vampire	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:As a standard action, a dread vampire can take the form of a swarm of any animals, vermin or undead with the swarm subtype that its children of the night ability allows. This is a polymorph effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.114
Uncanny Climber	KEY:Uncanny Climber ~ Dread Vampire	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A dread vampire climbs with its hands or upper limbs free and can walk on ceilings as though under a spider climb spell. It can use the accelerated climb action to cover up to four times its climb speed, each check covering a distance equal to its climb speed; climbing a distance up to its climb speed is a move-equivalent action.	SOURCEPAGE:p.114

###Block: Dread Wight, Wight, Dread Wraith Sovereign, Dread Wraith, Wraith, Dread Zombie
Draining Attacks	KEY:Draining Attacks ~ Dread Wight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A dread wight with no natural attack gains a primary slam attack dealing damage for the base creature's size, and all its natural attacks gain energy drain (1 level). The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.116
Command Wights	KEY:Command Wights ~ Dread Wight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a free action, a dread wight automatically commands all normal wights within 30 feet, as the command undead spell. Normal wights never attack a dread wight unless compelled.	SOURCEPAGE:p.116
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Dread Wight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Any creature killed by a dread wight's energy drain rises as a dread wight in 1d4 rounds, under its creator's command as by dominate monster until one of them is destroyed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.116
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Wight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Any creature killed by the wight's energy drain rises as a normal wight in 1d4 rounds, under its creator's command as by dominate monster until one of them is destroyed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.117
Lifesense	KEY:Lifesense ~ Dread Wraith Sovereign	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Vision	DESC:The creature notices and locates living creatures within 60 feet, exactly as if it had the blindsight ability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.118
Unnatural Aura	KEY:Unnatural Aura ~ Dread Wraith Sovereign	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:Animals do not willingly approach a dread wraith sovereign within 100 feet unless their master succeeds on a DC 25 Handle Animal, Ride or wild empathy check.	SOURCEPAGE:p.118
Unnatural Chill	KEY:Unnatural Chill ~ Dread Wraith Sovereign	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:The air around a dread wraith sovereign is noticeably colder than its surroundings. Each creature within 30 feet takes 2d6 points of cold damage and must succeed on a Fortitude save or be paralyzed, repeating both each round it stays in range. A creature that takes the damage or is paralyzed is automatically shaken for 1 minute. Incorporeal creatures are immune. The shaken condition is a mind-affecting fear effect and the save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.118
Wraith Touch	KEY:Wraith Touch ~ Dread Wraith Sovereign	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:All the base creature's attacks become incorporeal touch attacks, keeping their primary or secondary status, and a creature with no natural attacks gains a primary incorporeal touch. The touches deal negative energy damage and Constitution drain; a touch granted by the template deals damage as a slam of a creature three size categories larger. A dread wraith sovereign can carry no equipment of any kind and cannot cast spells with material components unless it has Eschew Materials.	SOURCEPAGE:p.118
Wraith Touch	KEY:Wraith Touch ~ Wraith	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As the dread wraith sovereign's wraith touch, but a touch attack granted by the template deals damage as a slam of a creature one size category larger.	SOURCEPAGE:p.120
Constitution Drain	KEY:Constitution Drain ~ Dread Wraith Sovereign	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:The incorporeal touch deals 1d8 points of Constitution drain unless the creature struck succeeds on a Charisma-based Fortitude save.	SOURCEPAGE:p.118
Constitution Drain	KEY:Constitution Drain ~ Wraith	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:The incorporeal touch deals 1d6 points of Constitution drain unless the creature struck succeeds on a Charisma-based Fortitude save. Appendix C on page 308 lists the wraith at +2 CR; this template follows the entry on page 120, which says +1.	SOURCEPAGE:p.120
Command Wraiths	KEY:Command Wraiths ~ Dread Wraith Sovereign	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a free action, a dread wraith sovereign automatically commands all normal wraiths and dread wraiths within 30 feet, as the command undead spell. They never attack a dread wraith sovereign unless compelled.	SOURCEPAGE:p.118
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Dread Wraith Sovereign	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any creature slain by the sovereign's Constitution drain or incorporeal touch rises as a dread wraith in 1d4 rounds, commanded as by dominate monster until one of them is destroyed. When the sovereign is killed, each of its dread wraith spawn that had 10 or more Hit Dice in life becomes a dread wraith sovereign itself.	SOURCEPAGE:p.118
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Wraith	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any creature slain by the wraith's Constitution drain or incorporeal touch rises as a normal wraith in 1d4 rounds, commanded as by dominate monster until one of them is destroyed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.120
Penetrating Touch	KEY:Penetrating Touch ~ Dread Wraith Sovereign	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Damage dealt by a dread wraith sovereign's natural attacks ignores damage reduction.	SOURCEPAGE:p.119
Rotting Frame	KEY:Rotting Frame ~ Dread Zombie	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The base creature's natural armor rises by its size: Tiny or smaller +0, Small +1, Medium +2, Large +3, Huge +4, Gargantuan +7, Colossal +11. A dread zombie keeps the base creature's speeds but cannot run.	SOURCEPAGE:p.121
Extra Hit Dice	KEY:Extra Hit Dice ~ Dread Zombie	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A dread zombie adds 2 racial Hit Dice to its total, and a creature with no racial HD gains 2. PCGen cannot add racial Hit Dice through a template; add them to the base race by hand.	SOURCEPAGE:p.121
Zombie Attacks	KEY:Zombie Attacks ~ Dread Zombie	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A dread zombie with no other natural attacks gains a primary slam attack, and if it has at least one mouth with no natural attack it gains a secondary bite with each mouth. A slam granted this way deals damage as though the creature were one size larger, and a bite as though it were one size smaller.	SOURCEPAGE:p.122
Brain Consumption	KEY:Brain Consumption ~ Dread Zombie	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:When a dread zombie succeeds on a grapple check to deal bite damage to a pinned or helpless living foe, that foe must succeed on a Fortitude save or die as the zombie consumes its brain. Creatures immune to critical hits and creatures with multiple heads are not killed by this attack. The save DC is Strength-based and uses the dread zombie's total HD.	SOURCEPAGE:p.122
Command Zombies	KEY:Command Zombies ~ Dread Zombie	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a free action, a dread zombie automatically commands all normal zombies within 30 feet, as the command undead spell. Normal zombies never attack a dread zombie unless compelled.	SOURCEPAGE:p.122

###Block: Dream Creature, Drider, Drowblood, Dunesage
Immunity to Illusion	KEY:Immunity to Illusion ~ Dream Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A dream creature is immune to figment, glamer and pattern spells.	SOURCEPAGE:p.123
Sleep Vulnerability	KEY:Sleep Vulnerability ~ Dream Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A dream creature takes a -2 penalty on saves against sleep effects and counts as having 2 fewer Hit Dice than it does for working out how many creatures, and of what HD, a sleep spell affects. A base creature immune to sleep loses that immunity.	SOURCEPAGE:p.123
Dream Spellcasting	KEY:Dream Spellcasting ~ Dream Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A dream creature's effective caster level for figment, glamer and pattern spells is +2 higher than the base creature's. The increase is cumulative, so a spell that is both a figment and a glamer is cast at +4 caster levels.	SOURCEPAGE:p.123
Lulling Gaze	KEY:Lulling Gaze ~ Dream Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any creature within 20 feet must succeed on a Will save or take a -5 penalty on Perception checks and a -2 penalty on Will saves against sleep effects while it stays in range, with a new save each round until it fails or leaves. The dream creature can suppress or resume the gaze as a free action. This is a gaze effect with a Charisma-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.123
Sleep Song	KEY:Sleep Song ~ Dream Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a full-round action, a dream creature sings a lullaby. Any creature within 100 feet that can hear it must succeed on a Will save, DC equal to the dream creature's Perform (sing) check result, or fall asleep as by a sleep spell for a number of rounds equal to the dream creature's total Hit Dice. A creature that saves is immune to that dream creature's sleep song for 24 hours, and dream creatures are immune to all sleep songs. This is a sonic, mind-affecting sleep effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.123
Waking Dreams	KEY:Waking Dreams ~ Dream Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:At will, as a standard action, a dream creature makes the area within 100 feet hazy and dreamlike, an effect that passes through solid objects and crosses into the Ethereal Plane. Distances and speeds become hard to judge, bright areas seem dark and dark areas hazily lit, colours blend and creatures seem to take on the features of objects or other creatures. Every creature in the area takes a -4 penalty on all attack rolls, checks and saves while it remains, and a creature outside the area acting on or through it takes the same penalty. This is an illusion (figment) effect with no save; creatures immune to illusions are immune to it, and true seeing and similar effects let a creature act without the penalty. Dream creatures are immune to their own and each other's waking dreams.	SOURCEPAGE:p.123
Dream Travel	KEY:Dream Travel ~ Dream Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Once per day a dream creature can sleep and travel the realm of dreams, as an ethereal jaunt spell except that it leaves its material body behind and may stay in dream form as long as that body sleeps. A dream version rises from the sleeping body and roams material areas like an ethereal creature. If the sleeping body is damaged, subjected to a harmful spell or effect, or woken by loud noise or vigorous motion, the dream form vanishes and the creature wakes knowing what its dream-self experienced; the same happens if the dream form leaves the dream realm, dies, or would become material. Beneficial spells cast on the sleeping body also benefit the dream form, but harm to the dream form never reaches the body.	SOURCEPAGE:p.124
Poison	KEY:Poison ~ Drider	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Bite--injury; save Fortitude; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d2 Str; cure 1 save. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.126
Drider Bite	KEY:Drider Bite ~ Drider	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A drider without a bite attack gains one that delivers its poison, dealing damage for the base creature's original size, primary if it has no other natural attacks and secondary otherwise. A drider that already had a bite keeps that damage and delivers its poison with it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.126
Drider Legs	KEY:Drider Legs ~ Drider	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The base creature's size increases by one step, and its natural armor rises by +5 plus the increase from the size change. Space and reach are normal for the new size, using the long column at Large or greater. It gains a climb speed equal to half its land speed, or a land speed equal to its highest speed plus half that as a climb speed if it had no land speed; an existing climb speed is kept if it is faster. Natural attacks from the lower body, such as a tail or rake, are kept and come from extra limbs on the abdomen. It gains the CMD bonus against trip of an eight-legged creature.	SOURCEPAGE:p.126
Undersized Weapons	KEY:Undersized Weapons ~ Drider	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A drider uses manufactured weapons as if it were one size category smaller.	SOURCEPAGE:p.127
Drider Spellcasting	KEY:Drider Spellcasting ~ Drider	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A drider casts spells as a 6th-level cleric, sorcerer or wizard, or as one of those classes at a level equal to its total HD -3, whichever is higher, gaining no other class abilities. A base creature that already casts spells as a racial ability adds these spells to what it already knows.	SOURCEPAGE:p.126
Immunity to Sleep	KEY:Immunity to Sleep ~ Drowblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A drowblood is immune to magic sleep effects.	SOURCEPAGE:p.128
+1 racial bonus on Will saves against spells and spell-like abilities	KEY:Drowblood ~ Will Saves	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality	ASPECT:SaveBonus|+1 racial vs. spells and spell-like abilities	SOURCEPAGE:p.128
Drow Blood	KEY:Drow Blood ~ Drowblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A drowblood counts as a member of the base creature's race and of the drow and elf races for racially specific abilities and effects. Its darkvision is 60 ft., or +20 ft. on an existing darkvision to a maximum of 120 ft.	SOURCEPAGE:p.128
Earth Glide	KEY:Earth Glide ~ Dunesage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A dunesage gains a burrow speed equal to its base movement rate and the earth glide universal monster ability, passing through stone, dirt and almost any other earth except metal as easily as a fish swims through water, leaving no tunnel and disturbing nothing.	SOURCEPAGE:p.129
Change Shape	KEY:Change Shape ~ Dunesage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A dunesage can take the shape of an earth elemental of its own size, functioning as the elemental body spell appropriate to that size. For a dunesage larger than Huge, use the Huge earth elemental's statistics and increase the size as needed. This is a polymorph effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.130
Dunesage Lore	KEY:Dunesage Lore ~ Dunesage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A dunesage gains spell-like abilities cumulatively with its total Hit Dice, at a caster level equal to its total HD or the base creature's caster level, whichever is higher: 1-4 constant endure elements and 1/day augury; 5-8 3/day stone call and 1/day share memory; 9-12 1/day divination and shifting sands; 13-16 1/day legend lore and move earth; 17+ 1/day foresight and scouring winds. It also gains any two additional Intelligence-based skills as class skills.	SOURCEPAGE:p.129

###Block: Dust Creature, Eldritch
Air Mastery	KEY:Air Mastery ~ Dust Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:Airborne creatures take a -1 penalty on attack and damage rolls against a dust creature.	SOURCEPAGE:p.131
Dust Blast	KEY:Dust Blast ~ Dust Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once every 1d4 rounds, as a standard action, a dust creature emits an abrasive jet of dust-filled wind in a 5-foot-wide, 20-foot-long line, dealing 1d4 points of slashing damage per 2 Hit Dice (minimum 1d4, maximum 20d4) to creatures and objects. A Reflex save halves the damage; the save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.131
Exude Dust	KEY:Exude Dust ~ Dust Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:At will, as a free action, a dust creature surrounds itself with a 10-foot spread of dust that works as an obscuring mist spell, though all dust creatures see through it normally. Any other creature in the cloud must succeed on a Constitution-based Fortitude save or be blinded; a creature that shuts or covers its eyes first gains a +10 circumstance bonus, and one that enters with eyes closed need not save unless it opens them. Blinded creatures recover 1d4 rounds after their last exposure with open eyes, and exposure of a single eye blinds all eyes supernaturally. This is a blinding effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.131
Air Breather	KEY:Air Breather ~ Dust Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A dust creature can breathe air even if the base creature breathed only water.	SOURCEPAGE:p.132
Airborne	KEY:Airborne ~ Dust Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:At will, a dust creature can walk on air as though under an air walk spell, and it always falls as if affected by feather fall. While falling it can be carried on the wind as described under air walk.	SOURCEPAGE:p.132
Eldritch Points	KEY:Eldritch Points ~ Eldritch	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality	DESC:An eldritch creature gains one eldritch point (EP) per 2 Hit Dice, minimum 1, and spends them on the abilities below. Each ability costs or grants EP and raises or lowers the creature's CR adjustment, rounded up; once chosen, an ability cannot be changed unless the ability says otherwise. Set the final CR by summing those adjustments and comparing the result to other creatures of that CR.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Eldritch Limbs	KEY:Eldritch Limbs ~ Eldritch	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:An eldritch creature with no natural attacks gains two tentacle or claw attacks dealing damage as a creature one size category larger. It loses all skill ranks except racial bonuses and repurchases them as a creature of its new type, treating its former skills as class skills.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Ability Damage	KEY:Eldritch ~ Ability Damage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	DESC:(+1/2 CR) One of the eldritch's natural attacks deals 1d2 points of damage to an ability score chosen when the ability is selected. Taking it again applies the damage to another natural attack, raises the damage die by 1, or targets a different ability score.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Ability Drain	KEY:Eldritch ~ Ability Drain	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:3	DESC:(+1/2 CR) As ability damage, but the attack deals ability drain.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Ability Score Increase	KEY:Eldritch ~ Ability Score Increase	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/4 CR) Increase one ability score by +2.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Ability Score Decrease	KEY:Eldritch ~ Ability Score Decrease	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:-1	DESC:(-1/4 CR) Decrease one ability score by -2. A score reduced to 0 or lower becomes no score.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Abnormal Reach	KEY:Eldritch ~ Abnormal Reach	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/4 CR) Increase the reach of one of the eldritch's natural attacks by 5 ft.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Additional Attack	KEY:Eldritch ~ Additional Attack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/2 CR) The eldritch gains a natural attack of a type it does not already have, dealing damage appropriate for its size.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Additional Movement	KEY:Eldritch ~ Additional Movement	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/2 CR) The eldritch gains another mode of movement equal to its base speed or 10 feet, whichever is higher; a fly speed gained this way has clumsy maneuverability. Each time this is taken it must be a different mode.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Additional Natural Attack	KEY:Eldritch ~ Additional Natural Attack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/4 CR) The number of one of the eldritch's natural attacks increases by one, with a matching change in its anatomy.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Amorphous Body	KEY:Eldritch ~ Amorphous Body	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/2 CR) The eldritch's internal anatomy constantly shifts, making it immune to precision damage such as sneak attacks and critical hits.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Armor Class (Deflection)	KEY:Eldritch ~ Armor Class (Deflection)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	DESC:(+1/2 CR) The eldritch gains a deflection bonus to AC equal to its Charisma modifier (minimum 1).	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Armor Class (Natural)	KEY:Eldritch ~ Armor Class (Natural)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/4 CR) The eldritch gains a +3 natural armor bonus.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Bleed	KEY:Eldritch ~ Bleed	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/2 CR) All the eldritch's natural attacks gain bleed for 1d4 damage. Each further time raises the number or type of bleed damage dice by 1.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Blood Drain	KEY:Eldritch ~ Blood Drain	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	DESC:(+1/2 CR) One of the eldritch's attacks drains blood for 1d2 Con damage. Each further time raises the number or type of dice by 1, or gives blood drain at 1d2 Con to another attack.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Bonus Feat	KEY:Eldritch ~ Bonus Feat	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	DESC:(+1/2 CR) The eldritch gains a feat as a racial bonus feat. It can take this no more than one plus a third of its total Hit Dice times.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Constrict	KEY:Eldritch ~ Constrict	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/2 CR) The eldritch gains a constrict attack with an appropriate limb, dealing damage equal to its slam attack or to a slam of a creature one size larger.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Damage Reduction	KEY:Eldritch ~ Damage Reduction	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/4 CR) The eldritch gains DR 5 with a specific bypass, taken up to four times per bypass and adding 5 each time. Several DRs of equal value default to 'or'; joining two with 'and' costs another +1/4 CR. A DR with no bypass costs 2 EP and +1/2 CR.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Devour Soul	KEY:Eldritch ~ Devour Soul	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	DESC:(+1 CR) One of the eldritch's natural attacks gains energy drain (1 level). It can be taken up to three times, each raising the levels drained by 1. The DC to regain drained levels is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Disease	KEY:Eldritch ~ Disease	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/4 CR) One of the eldritch's attacks transmits eldritch rot--injury or contact; save Fortitude; onset immediate; frequency 1/day; effect 1d4 of the chosen ability score; cure 1 save; Constitution-based DC. Taking it again adds a disease on another attack, or applies the existing disease to another attack, raises its damage as a natural attack, adds a second ability score starting at 1d4, adds a required save to a maximum of 3, or gives a +1 racial bonus to the DC up to the eldritch's total Hit Dice.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Dual Essence	KEY:Eldritch ~ Dual Essence	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	DESC:(+1 CR) The eldritch keeps the defenses, spell-like abilities, special attacks and special qualities of its former type as well as its new one, and counts as both types for spell effects.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Energy Resistance	KEY:Eldritch ~ Energy Resistance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/4 CR) The eldritch gains resistance 5 to acid, cold, electricity, fire or sonic. Each further time adds a new energy type or raises an existing resistance by 5, to a maximum of 30.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Fast Healing	KEY:Eldritch ~ Fast Healing	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/4 CR) The eldritch gains fast healing 1, increasing by 1 each further time. It cannot be taken alongside regeneration.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Healing Bypass	KEY:Eldritch ~ Healing Bypass	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:-1	DESC:(-1/2 CR) A specific type of attack, such as fire or good, bypasses the eldritch's fast healing or regeneration. Each further time adds another bypass as an 'or'.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Incorporeal	KEY:Eldritch ~ Incorporeal	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	DESC:(+1 CR) The eldritch gains the incorporeal subtype and every ability that comes with it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Larger Weapons	KEY:Eldritch ~ Larger Weapons	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/4 CR) The eldritch can use manufactured weapons one size category larger than itself. This grants no proficiency.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Light Blindness	KEY:Eldritch ~ Light Blindness	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:-1	DESC:(-1/4 CR) Abrupt exposure to bright light blinds the eldritch for 1 round, and it is dazzled on subsequent rounds while it stays in the area.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Light Sensitivity	KEY:Eldritch ~ Light Sensitivity	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:-1	DESC:(-1/4 CR) The eldritch is dazzled as long as it remains in an area of bright light.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Maddening Presence	KEY:Eldritch ~ Maddening Presence	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	DESC:(+1 CR) Every creature within 30 feet goes permanently insane, as the insanity spell; a successful Will save reduces this to confusion for 1d6 rounds and grants immunity to that eldritch's maddening presence for a day. This is a mind-affecting effect with a Charisma-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Maneuverability Adjustment	KEY:Eldritch ~ Maneuverability Adjustment	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/4 CR) If the eldritch has a fly speed, raise its maneuverability one step for 1 EP and +1/4 CR, or lower it one step to gain 1 EP and lose 1/4 CR.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
No Breath	KEY:Eldritch ~ No Breath	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/2 CR) The eldritch does not breathe and is immune to anything that requires breathing, such as inhaled poison. This grants no immunity to cloud or gas attacks that do not require breathing.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Poison	KEY:Eldritch ~ Poison	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/2 CR) One of the eldritch's attacks inflicts eldritch essence--injury or contact; save Fortitude or Will; frequency 1/round for 2 rounds; effect 1 point of the chosen ability score; cure 1 consecutive save. A physical score uses a Constitution-based Fortitude save, a mental score a Charisma-based Will save. Each further time raises the damage as a natural attack, adds a required save to a maximum of 3, extends the frequency by 1 round to a maximum of 6, adds a second ability score taking 1 point, adds +1 natural bonus to the DC, or delivers the same poison with a second natural attack.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Racial Skill	KEY:Eldritch ~ Racial Skill	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/8 CR) The selected skill becomes a racial skill for the eldritch. Applying it to a whole skill group doubles the CR cost.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Regeneration	KEY:Eldritch ~ Regeneration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	DESC:(+1/4 CR) The eldritch gains regeneration 2, rising by 2 each further time. It cannot be taken alongside fast healing.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Resistance	KEY:Eldritch ~ Resistance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/4 CR) The eldritch gains a racial bonus on saves against one specific kind of attack, such as poison, disease or spell effects, equal to a third of its total Hit Dice (minimum +1). Each further time raises that bonus by another third of its HD or covers another attack type.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Sense	KEY:Eldritch ~ Sense	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/8 CR) The eldritch gains darkvision +60 ft., low-light vision, blindsense +30 ft. or blindsight +60 ft.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Skill Bonus	KEY:Eldritch ~ Skill Bonus	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/8 CR) The eldritch gains a +2 racial bonus on one specific skill. Applying it to a whole skill group doubles the CR cost. Each further time adds to the bonus or covers a new skill.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Smaller Weapons	KEY:Eldritch ~ Smaller Weapons	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/4 CR) The eldritch can use manufactured weapons one size category smaller than itself. This grants no proficiency.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Spell Resistance	KEY:Eldritch ~ Spell Resistance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	DESC:(+1/2 CR) The eldritch gains spell resistance equal to 11 + its total Hit Dice.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Spell-Like Abilities	KEY:Eldritch ~ Spell-Like Abilities	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(varies CR) The eldritch can use a number of spells as spell-like abilities at a caster level equal to its total Hit Dice. The EP cost is a third of the summed levels of all of them, each usable 1/day by default. For EP purposes, halve a spell's level to drop it from per day to per week, per week to per month or per month to per year; raise it by half to add uses per day; and raise it by 1 to go from per day to at will, or at will to constant. The CR adjustment is a quarter of the total EP spent this way, minimum +0. These modifiers only affect the EP calculation, never the spell's actual level.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Spellcasting	KEY:Eldritch ~ Spellcasting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:4	DESC:(+2 CR) The eldritch casts spells as a cleric, druid, oracle, sorcerer, witch or wizard of a level equal to its racial Hit Dice, to a maximum of 20, provided its relevant ability score is high enough.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Starflight	KEY:Eldritch ~ Starflight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/2 CR) The eldritch survives the void of outer space and needs no air there, flying through space at incredible speed. A trip within one solar system normally takes 3d20 months and a trip beyond 3d20 years, or longer at the GM's discretion.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Stench	KEY:Eldritch ~ Stench	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/2 CR) The eldritch gains the stench universal monster ability, lasting 10 rounds, with a Constitution-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Swap Movement	KEY:Eldritch ~ Swap Movement	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(varies CR) Swap one of the eldritch's modes of movement for one it does not have. Gaining flight this way gives average maneuverability and costs +1/4 CR; any other swap costs +1/8 CR.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Trample	KEY:Eldritch ~ Trample	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:2	DESC:(+1/2 CR) The eldritch gains the trample special attack, dealing its slam damage plus 1-1/2 its Strength bonus, or a slam appropriate for its size plus 1-1/2 its Strength bonus if it has no slam. The save DC is Strength-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Variable Natural Attack	KEY:Eldritch ~ Variable Natural Attack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/2 CR) One of the eldritch's natural attacks changes type each round--claw, slam, bite and so on--while its damage stays the same.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Vulnerable to Sunlight	KEY:Eldritch ~ Vulnerable to Sunlight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:-2	DESC:(-1/2 CR) The eldritch takes 1 point of Con damage each round it is exposed to sunlight.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Vulnerability to Energy	KEY:Eldritch ~ Vulnerability to Energy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:-1	DESC:(-1/4 CR) The eldritch gains vulnerability to one energy type: acid, cold, electricity, fire or sonic.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133
Whistle	KEY:Eldritch ~ Whistle	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EldritchPoint	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	COST:1	DESC:(+1/2 CR) At will, the eldritch whistles a hypnotic tune; every creature within 30 feet must make a Will save or be fascinated. This is a sonic, mind-affecting effect whose save DC is Charisma-based if supernatural or Constitution-based if extraordinary.	SOURCEPAGE:p.133

###Block: Electric Creature, Element-Infused
Water Vulnerability	KEY:Water Vulnerability ~ Electric Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:For every gallon of water an electric creature is exposed to it takes 1d8 damage. Submerged, it takes 1d10 per round and also deals 1d6 electricity damage to everything within a radius equal to its own space.	SOURCEPAGE:p.137
Electric Touch	KEY:Electric Touch ~ Electric Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:All the base creature's natural attacks become incorporeal touch attacks, and a creature with none gains a primary incorporeal touch. Any such attack that dealt hit point damage now deals electricity damage, and any energy damage it carried becomes electricity damage too. A touch attack granted by the template deals damage as a slam of a creature one size larger. The creature keeps only its land and fly speeds, gaining or raising a fly speed to its highest speed with perfect maneuverability, and can carry no equipment of any kind.	SOURCEPAGE:p.137
Chain Lightning Strike	KEY:Chain Lightning Strike ~ Electric Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once per day, an electric creature can strike any creatures within 100 feet as a chain lightning spell with no upper limit to the damage. The caster level equals its total Hit Dice and the save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.137
Electric Burst	KEY:Electric Burst ~ Electric Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Three times per day, an electric creature releases a 20-foot burst of electricity centred on itself, dealing half the damage of its lightning strike. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.137
Electric Spellcasting	KEY:Electric Spellcasting ~ Electric Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:An electric creature casts all spells and spell-like abilities with the electricity descriptor at one caster level higher, and can add that descriptor to any damaging spell, which is then cast at the normal caster level with half its damage as electricity. It cannot cast spells or use spell-like abilities with the water descriptor, and cannot cast spells with material components unless it has Eschew Materials. Spell-like abilities that dealt acid, cold, fire or sonic damage now deal electricity damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.137
Lightning Strike	KEY:Lightning Strike ~ Electric Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once per day, plus once more per 5 racial Hit Dice, an electric creature can direct a lightning bolt at any foe within 100 ft. It works as the lightning bolt spell with no upper limit to the damage, at a caster level equal to its total racial Hit Dice, with a Constitution-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.138
Electric Body	KEY:Electric Body ~ Electric Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:Anyone striking an electric creature with a natural or non-metallic manufactured melee weapon takes 1d6 electricity damage; with a metallic weapon or object, 1d8.	SOURCEPAGE:p.138
Electric Leap	KEY:Electric Leap ~ Electric Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:When using lightning strike or chain lightning strike, an electric creature can travel along its own bolt as a swift action, reappearing in any open 5-foot square beside a creature the bolt struck, or where the bolt ends if it hit nobody, or the nearest available square.	SOURCEPAGE:p.138
Elemental Body	KEY:Elemental Body ~ Element-Infused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:The creature's body takes on some elemental qualities: each time it is exposed to a bleed, precision damage, poison, paralysis, sleep or stunning effect it has a 25%% chance to avoid it. It also loses any weakness tied to its element, and loses that element as a bypass for any ability such as regeneration.	SOURCEPAGE:p.139
Air Mastery	KEY:Air Mastery ~ Air-Infused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Air-infused creatures take a -1 penalty on attack and damage rolls against an air elemental.	SOURCEPAGE:p.140
Wind Blast	KEY:Wind Blast ~ Air-Infused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once every 1d4 rounds, an air-infused creature breathes a 60-foot cone of wind like a windstorm. Every non-flying creature in the area must succeed on an Acrobatics or Strength check against the blast's DC or fall prone. A flying creature that fails is blown away from the air-infused creature 5 feet per point by which it failed, taking 1d6 points of damage per 5 feet of that movement a large object such as a wall prevents. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.140
Barrage	KEY:Barrage ~ Earth-Infused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once every 1d4 rounds, an earth-infused creature releases a storm of rock in a 30-foot-radius spread dealing 1d6 bludgeoning damage per 2 of its Hit Dice, halved on a successful Reflex save. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.140
Earth Mastery	KEY:Earth Mastery ~ Earth-Infused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An earth-infused creature gains a +1 bonus on attack and damage rolls when both it and its foe touch the ground, and takes a -4 penalty when its opponent is airborne or waterborne. These modifiers apply to overrun and bull rush as well.	SOURCEPAGE:p.140
Earth's Armor	KEY:Earth's Armor ~ Earth-Infused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The earth-infused creature's natural armor bonus improves by +2 over the base creature's.	SOURCEPAGE:p.141
Fire Breath	KEY:Fire Breath ~ Fire-Infused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once every 1d4 rounds, a fire-infused creature breathes a 30-foot cone of fire dealing 1d6 points of fire damage per 2 of its Hit Dice, to a maximum of 20d6, halved on a successful Reflex save. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.140
Heat	KEY:Heat ~ Fire-Infused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Each of a fire-infused creature's natural attacks, and its melee attacks with metallic weapons, deal an extra 1d6 points of fire damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.140
Fire Healing	KEY:Fire Healing ~ Fire-Infused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A fire-infused creature regains 1 hit point for each full round it stays in contact with a fire at least one size category smaller than itself, and heals 1 point of damage per 10 points a magical fire effect would otherwise deal to it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.141
Firewalk	KEY:Firewalk ~ Fire-Infused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A fire-infused creature can climb a burning object as though it had a climb speed equal to its highest speed, fly at its highest speed with perfect maneuverability while in contact with fire, and walk on flames at its highest speed as though walking on air.	SOURCEPAGE:p.141
Waterball	KEY:Waterball ~ Water-Infused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:With water within reach, a water-infused creature can scoop up a cohesive ball of water and hurl it as a ranged attack, devoting as many of its ranged attacks per round to this as it likes. Waterballs can be thrown underwater or across the air-water boundary with no penalty to range or attack roll. A waterball is a thrown weapon with a 20-foot range increment dealing nonlethal damage as a slam for the creature's size, with its full Strength bonus to damage. It can instead be used to snuff a nonmagical fire as a quench spell with a ranged touch attack. Waterballs lose cohesion when not held or thrown by a water-infused creature. At the GM's discretion other liquids work the same way, though the creature must touch the liquid and suffer any harm it causes.	SOURCEPAGE:p.140
Water Mastery	KEY:Water Mastery ~ Water-Infused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A water-infused creature gains a +1 bonus on attack and damage rolls when both it and its opponent touch water, and takes a -4 penalty when either of them touches the ground. These modifiers apply to CMB and CMD as well.	SOURCEPAGE:p.140

###Block: Eye King, Feral Dragon, Fire Creature, Flesh Plant
All-Around Vision	KEY:All-Around Vision ~ Eye King	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:The eye king sees in all directions at once and cannot be flanked.	SOURCEPAGE:p.142
Eyes or Eyestalks	KEY:Eyes or Eyestalks ~ Eye King	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An eye king has a roughly spherical body with a single central eye at the front and a number of eyes or eyestalks equal to the base creature's racial Hit Dice, minimum 1 and maximum 20, rising from the top of its head. Base creatures of the animal, fey, humanoid, monstrous humanoid or vermin type become aberrations with the matching subtype; other types are unchanged.	SOURCEPAGE:p.143
Eye Rays	KEY:Eye Rays ~ Eye King	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Each eyestalk produces a single spell-like effect as a ray, at will, once per round as a free action, with a range of 100 feet, at a caster level equal to the eye king's total racial Hit Dice and a Charisma-based save DC. An eye ray can be any spell a sorcerer or cleric of that level could cast, and sorcerer or cleric class levels stack with its HD for this. It must already have chosen a spell of every lower level before taking one of a given level, unless it has the Powerful Eye Ray feat, and once chosen a spell cannot be changed. No two eye rays may produce the same spell, and every eye ray spell affects a single target whatever the original spell's target, area or effect. The eye king can aim only a third of its eyestalks into any one 90-degree arc. It cannot cast spells from class levels unless it has the Eye Caster feat, and a metamagic feat applies to one chosen eye ray only.	SOURCEPAGE:p.143
Central Eye Beam	KEY:Central Eye Beam ~ Eye King	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:While its central eye is open, an eye king constantly produces a magical emanation in a 100-foot cone. It must duplicate a spell that notes it is an emanation and that a sorcerer or cleric of a level equal to the eye king's racial Hit Dice, minimum 1st, could cast. The spell is chosen at creation and cannot be changed, and the save DC, if any, is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.143
Eye King Attacks	KEY:Eye King Attacks ~ Eye King	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Except for bite and wing attacks, an eye king's natural attacks deal damage as though it were two size categories smaller. If it has a mouth with no natural attack it gains a secondary bite per mouth, dealing damage as though it were one size larger. Except for wing attacks, every attack of a Small or larger eye king has 5 feet of reach, and of a Tiny or smaller eye king 0 feet.	SOURCEPAGE:p.143
Naturally Buoyant	KEY:Naturally Buoyant ~ Eye King	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An eye king is naturally buoyant and acts as though under a constant feather fall effect. A base creature that could fly keeps its fly speed, maneuverability and manner of flight; otherwise the eye king gains an extraordinary fly speed of half the base creature's highest speed, minimum 5 feet, with perfect maneuverability. A base creature with a swim speed swims as fast as it flies. Every other mode of movement drops to a quarter of its original value, minimum 5 feet.	SOURCEPAGE:p.143
Feral Mind	KEY:Feral Mind ~ Feral Dragon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A feral dragon's CR equals its racial Hit Dice divided by 2, or the base creature's CR -4, whichever is greater. It loses the base creature's damage reduction, spell resistance, spell-like abilities, innate spellcasting, every supernatural attack except its breath weapon, and all supernatural and spell-like special qualities; it can still cast spells from classes. It keeps the same number of feats, chosen to suit its diminished mind, recalculates skill points for its racial HD with the base creature's class skills, and its treasure drops one step. Its alignment is usually neutral but drifts towards the base creature's as it ages.	SOURCEPAGE:p.144
Heat Aura	KEY:Heat Aura ~ Fire Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:A fire creature emits supernatural heat in a 10-foot radius. Everything within takes 1d6 fire damage plus a further 1d6 for every 5 racial HD of the base creature, stacking with any other fire damage it deals. The aura cannot be suppressed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.146
Vulnerability to Cold	KEY:Vulnerability to Cold ~ Fire Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A fire creature takes half again as much damage (+50%%) from cold, regardless of whether a saving throw is allowed or whether the save succeeds.	SOURCEPAGE:p.146
Fire Touch	KEY:Fire Touch ~ Fire Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:All the base creature's natural attacks become incorporeal touch attacks, and a creature with none gains a primary incorporeal touch. Any such attack that dealt hit point damage now deals fire damage, and any other energy damage it carried becomes fire damage too. A touch granted by the template deals damage as a slam of a creature one size larger. Special attacks requiring corporeal contact are lost unless they deal hit point damage, which becomes fire damage in the same amount.	SOURCEPAGE:p.146
Burn	KEY:Burn ~ Fire Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Each of a fire creature's incorporeal touch attacks gains the burn universal monster ability, dealing 1d6 fire damage plus 1d6 for every 3 HD of the base creature. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.146
Fire Spellcasting	KEY:Fire Spellcasting ~ Fire Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A fire creature casts all spells and spell-like abilities with the fire descriptor at one caster level higher, and can add the fire descriptor to any damaging spell, which is then cast at the normal caster level with half its damage as fire. It cannot cast spells or use spell-like abilities with the cold descriptor.	SOURCEPAGE:p.146
Fire Bolt	KEY:Fire Bolt ~ Fire Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Each round, as an attack action, a fire creature can lob a bolt of fire as a ranged touch attack with a 100-foot range, dealing fire damage as a slam attack of a creature one size larger.	SOURCEPAGE:p.146
Melt	KEY:Melt ~ Fire Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:As a touch attack, a fire creature can try to melt any material, dealing it three times the creature's Hit Dice in fire damage. If that exceeds the material's hit points it melts or bursts into flames. The material gets a save to avoid the damage; the save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.146
Fire Body	KEY:Fire Body ~ Fire Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A fire creature's body burns whatever it touches and whatever touches it. Anyone striking it with a natural or manufactured melee weapon takes 1d6 fire damage and catches fire.	SOURCEPAGE:p.147
Fire Leap	KEY:Fire Leap ~ Fire Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A fire creature can leap between nonmagical open flames at least one size smaller than itself, as a dimension door, provided the fires are within 200 ft. of each other and in line of sight. It cannot leap into or out of a creature with the fire subtype or one that exudes or is made of flame.	SOURCEPAGE:p.147
Molten Swim	KEY:Molten Swim ~ Fire Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A fire creature with a swim speed moves through molten materials at that speed, but can no longer move through water.	SOURCEPAGE:p.146
Flesh Body	KEY:Flesh Body ~ Flesh Plant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A flesh plant's body is muscle, soft organs and cartilage instead of vegetable matter. It loses every ability granted by the plant type and every plant-based weakness such as vulnerability to fire or a need for sunshine, along with any Stealth bonus that came from resembling or blending with natural plants. Its natural armor becomes a value set by size: Medium or smaller +0, Large +2, Huge +5, Gargantuan +9, Colossal +14. Every speed rises by 10 feet, and a base plant with no land speed gains one of 10 feet. A base plant with no Intelligence score gains Intelligence 1 and the standard number of feats for its Hit Dice, and the aberration class skills become its own.	SOURCEPAGE:p.148
Weeping Toxin	KEY:Weeping Toxin ~ Flesh Plant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A toxin weeping from its flesh gives all a flesh plant's natural attacks bleed (1d4 hp). Creatures immune to poison are immune to this bleed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.149

###Block: Force Creature, Fortune-Blessed, Fortune-Spurned, Genie-Bound
Force Aura	KEY:Force Aura ~ Force Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.Aura	DESC:A force creature is always surrounded by a force aura shedding dull blue light about as bright as a candle. Any opponent that hits it with a natural weapon or unarmed attack takes 1d6 points of force damage, and the force creature deals the same damage on any successful combat maneuver involving physical contact. The aura flares brighter at the point of impact when the creature is struck.	SOURCEPAGE:p.150
Force Body	KEY:Force Body ~ Force Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:A force creature takes half damage from all attacks and effects that deal hit point damage. Its natural armor no longer applies; instead it gains a deflection bonus to AC equal to the base creature's natural armor bonus plus its own Charisma modifier (minimum +0).	SOURCEPAGE:p.150
Force Vulnerability	KEY:Force Vulnerability ~ Force Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:Disintegration and force effects automatically bypass a force creature's spell resistance and all its damage resistance, including its force body.	SOURCEPAGE:p.150
Force Strikes	KEY:Force Strikes ~ Force Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A force creature with no other natural attacks gains a primary slam dealing damage as a creature one size larger. All its natural attacks deal force damage, like a magic missile, rather than bludgeoning, piercing or slashing, so it strikes incorporeal creatures as though with ghost touch weapons.	SOURCEPAGE:p.150
Draw Force	KEY:Draw Force ~ Force Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:At will, as a standard action, a force creature draws every magical effect with the force descriptor within 30 feet into itself, as a targeted dispel magic at a caster level equal to its total Hit Dice. On beating the effect's DC of 11 + its caster level, the effect is dispelled and the force creature heals 1d8 hit points for each point by which it beat the DC. Healing above its maximum becomes temporary hit points, capped at half its maximum hit points and lasting until used.	SOURCEPAGE:p.150
Force Strength	KEY:Force Strength ~ Force Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A force creature gains a +4 bonus on CMB checks to overrun, bull rush and sunder and on Strength checks to break items, and a +4 bonus to CMD against overrun, bull rush, push and trip.	SOURCEPAGE:p.150
Force Leap	KEY:Force Leap ~ Force Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A force creature gains a +20 racial bonus on Acrobatics checks made to jump. Because it continuously sheds dull blue light it takes a -5 circumstance penalty on Stealth checks except in bright light, a penalty that can be reduced or negated by covering its body with a material that blocks light.	SOURCEPAGE:p.150
Augmented Criticals	KEY:Augmented Criticals ~ Fortune-Blessed	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:The critical threat range of each of the creature's attacks doubles, following the normal rules for doubling critical ranges. It does not stack with other doubling effects such as keen edge or Improved Critical.	SOURCEPAGE:p.151
Lucky Strike	KEY:Lucky Strike ~ Fortune-Blessed	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a swift action, once per minute, a fortune-blessed creature can apply a true strike effect to a single attack.	SOURCEPAGE:p.151
Favored	KEY:Favored ~ Fortune-Blessed	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A fortune-blessed creature gains a +2 luck bonus on all saves and opposed checks and a +1 luck bonus on all attack rolls, plus a +2 luck bonus to AC and a +2 luck bonus on all skills that stacks with the bonus on opposed checks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.151
Turn of Fate	KEY:Turn of Fate ~ Fortune-Blessed	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Once per day, a fortune-blessed creature can reroll any failed roll it has just made, and must accept the second result.	SOURCEPAGE:p.151
Aura of Misfortune	KEY:Aura of Misfortune ~ Fortune-Spurned	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:Every creature within 10 feet gains the diminished criticals and unlucky strike qualities of the fortune-spurned template while it stays in range, and takes a -4 penalty on all checks and saving throws.	SOURCEPAGE:p.153
Calamitous Mishap	KEY:Calamitous Mishap ~ Fortune-Spurned	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a swift action, once per minute, the creature can bring a calamity down on itself and one creature within 5 feet. The mishap must be a possible result of the surroundings, though it may be the worst possible one, and it must be as dangerous to the fortune-spurned creature as to its target: both make the same saving throw and suffer the same result. In some surroundings no calamity is available.	SOURCEPAGE:p.153
Cursed	KEY:Cursed ~ Fortune-Spurned	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A fortune-spurned creature takes a -2 luck penalty on all opposed checks and saves, a -1 luck penalty on all attack rolls, and a -2 penalty on all skill checks that stacks with the penalty on opposed checks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.153
Diminished Criticals	KEY:Diminished Criticals ~ Fortune-Spurned	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Weakness	DESC:A fortune-spurned creature must roll twice to confirm a critical hit.	SOURCEPAGE:p.153
Twist of Fate	KEY:Twist of Fate ~ Fortune-Spurned	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Weakness	DESC:The first time each day that a fortune-spurned creature rolls a natural 20 on a saving throw, it fails the save.	SOURCEPAGE:p.153
Unlucky Strike	KEY:Unlucky Strike ~ Fortune-Spurned	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Weakness	DESC:When a fortune-spurned creature attacks with a weapon and rolls a natural 1, it provokes an attack of opportunity from its target, even if that creature would not otherwise have one.	SOURCEPAGE:p.153
Genie Grace	KEY:Genie Grace ~ Genie-Bound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:The creature is immune to the planar effects of its genie's home plane but still takes damage from non-planar sources of the same kind; an efreeti-bound creature is immune to the Plane of Fire itself but not to a fireball. The genie can revoke this at will.	SOURCEPAGE:p.154
Genie Magic	KEY:Genie Magic ~ Genie-Bound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:The genie lets its bound creature use the genie's spell-like abilities, though not spells from classes or magic items, as though it were a genie of that kind, and the creature may use them as it wishes. As a free action the genie can revoke or reinstate them, end their durations early, or spoil their effects. The caster level is the bound creature's total Hit Dice and the save DCs are Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.154
Ability Score Boon	KEY:Ability Score Boon ~ Genie-Bound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A genie-bound creature gains 6 points to distribute among its ability scores as it chooses. Apply them by hand.	SOURCEPAGE:p.155
Genie-Bond	KEY:Genie-Bond ~ Genie-Bound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:The genie is in constant telepathic communication with the bound creature whatever the language or distance, even across planes, and is always aware of its servant's actions, though not its thoughts, and of its condition as though by a status spell. The servant has no special awareness of the genie but can answer telepathically.	SOURCEPAGE:p.156
Genie-Empowered	KEY:Genie-Empowered ~ Genie-Bound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Three times per day a genie-bound creature can gain a +10 bonus on one skill check, a +5 bonus on a single saving throw, or double speed for a round. It may claim the saving throw bonus even on another creature's turn.	SOURCEPAGE:p.156
Djinni Boon	KEY:Djinni Boon ~ Genie-Bound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A creature bound to a djinni gains a +4 morale bonus on all attack, damage, CMB and CMD rolls. The genie can remove this boon at will.	SOURCEPAGE:p.156
Efreeti Boon	KEY:Efreeti Boon ~ Genie-Bound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:An efreeti-bound creature gains extra hit points equal to its Charisma bonus (minimum 0) per Hit Die. The genie can remove this boon at will.	SOURCEPAGE:p.156
Janni Boon	KEY:Janni Boon ~ Genie-Bound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A janni-bound creature is immune to the damaging effects of desert environments, including dehydration and heat exposure, though magical effects of that nature still affect it. The genie can remove this boon at will.	SOURCEPAGE:p.156
Marid Boon	KEY:Marid Boon ~ Genie-Bound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A marid-bound creature gains water breathing as a supernatural ability and a +4 circumstance bonus on Swim checks. The genie can remove this boon at will.	SOURCEPAGE:p.156
Shaitan Boon	KEY:Shaitan Boon ~ Genie-Bound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A shaitan-bound creature gains a +4 morale bonus on all attack, damage, CMB and CMD rolls. The genie can remove this boon at will.	SOURCEPAGE:p.156

###Block: Giantblood
Giant Size	KEY:Giant Size ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:If the base creature is smaller than its giant parent it gains one size category, to a maximum of Colossal, without the usual bonuses for an increase in size: it uses this template's values instead. On gaining a size category every speed rises by 10 feet, a flying creature's maneuverability drops one step, and its space and reach grow by the bonus for its final size (Medium +0 ft., Large +5 ft., Huge +5 ft., Gargantuan +5 ft., Colossal +10 ft.), though reach bonuses from specific attacks do not. Its natural armor rises by its final size (Medium +1, Large +3, Huge +4, Gargantuan +5, Colossal +6) and it takes the size penalty to AC. Its ability scores change by final size, even if its size did not change: Medium Str +6, Dex -2, Con +2; Large and Huge Str +10, Dex -2, Con +4; Gargantuan and Colossal Str +14, Dex -4, Con +6, no score dropping below 1. Natural attack damage increases by one step, and a creature that grew replaces its size modifier on Fly and Stealth with the one for its new size. A humanoid base creature gains the giant subtype.	SOURCEPAGE:p.157
Rock Throwing	KEY:Rock Throwing ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A giantblood gains rock throwing with a range increment set by its final size: Medium 60 ft., Large 120 ft., Huge 140 ft., Gargantuan 180 ft., Colossal 220 ft. A base creature that already threw rocks uses whichever range is greater.	SOURCEPAGE:p.158
Rock Catching	KEY:Rock Catching ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A giantblood gains rock catching if its giant parent has it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.158
Extra Arm	KEY:Extra Arm ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:An athach-blood has a third arm growing from its torso and gains a claw attack with it, dealing damage for its size. The claw is primary if the base creature has no natural attacks and secondary otherwise.	SOURCEPAGE:p.158
Ferocity	KEY:Ferocity ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A cave-blood gains the ferocity universal monster ability: it can fight on without penalty while disabled or dying.	SOURCEPAGE:p.158
Flash of Insight	KEY:Flash of Insight ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Once per day, as an immediate action, a cyclops-blood peers into possible futures and chooses the exact result of one die roll before it is made. This can only alter one of its own actions, never another creature's roll.	SOURCEPAGE:p.158
Sandwalking	KEY:Sandwalking ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A desert-blood moves at full speed across sand, rocky ground and dust, and leaves no trail unless it chooses to.	SOURCEPAGE:p.159
Second Head	KEY:Second Head ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An ettin-blood has a second head, granting a +2 racial bonus on Perception checks and Multiattack as a bonus feat. If the base creature has a bite attack, the second head grants a second bite at the same attack modifier and base damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.159
Hill's Strength	KEY:Hill's Strength ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:While in contact with solid ground, not the deck of a ship or a floor above a basement, a hill-blood gains a +2 enhancement bonus to Strength.	SOURCEPAGE:p.159
One with the Bog	KEY:One with the Bog ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A marsh-blood gains a +4 racial bonus on Stealth, rising to +8 in swamps.	SOURCEPAGE:p.159
Natural Swimmer	KEY:Natural Swimmer ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A merrow-blood, fresh or saltwater, gains a +8 bonus on Swim, and Swim is a class skill.	SOURCEPAGE:p.159
Salt in the Veins	KEY:Salt in the Veins ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An ocean-blood gains a +8 bonus on Swim, +10 feet of swim speed, and Swim as a class skill.	SOURCEPAGE:p.159
Call of the River	KEY:Call of the River ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A river-blood gains a +4 bonus on Swim, and Profession (sailor) is a class skill for it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.159
Commanding Presence	KEY:Commanding Presence ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A rune-blood gains +4 on all Charisma-based skill checks against a creature with the giant subtype or the giantblood template, except rune giants and other rune-bloods.	SOURCEPAGE:p.159
Natural Craftsman	KEY:Natural Craftsman ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:All Craft skills are class skills for a slag-blood.	SOURCEPAGE:p.159
Stony Soul	KEY:Stony Soul ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A stone-blood's natural armor bonus improves by +2.	SOURCEPAGE:p.159
Wisdom of the Spirits	KEY:Wisdom of the Spirits ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A taiga-blood gains a +4 bonus on saves against enchantment and illusion spells.	ASPECT:SaveBonus|+4 vs. enchantments and illusions	SOURCEPAGE:p.159
Troll Regeneration	KEY:Troll Regeneration ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A troll-blood gains regeneration 2, bypassed by fire or acid. A giantblood with any kind of troll parent gains fast healing 2 instead if the GM prefers.	SOURCEPAGE:p.159
One with the Forest	KEY:One with the Forest ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A wood-blood gains a +4 racial bonus on Stealth, rising to +8 in forests.	SOURCEPAGE:p.159
Giant Heritage	KEY:Giant Heritage ~ Giantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A giantblood from any other kind of giant gains a +2 competence bonus on Perception checks and a +2 bonus on Fortitude saves.	SOURCEPAGE:p.159

###Block: Gigantean
Gigantean Growth	KEY:Gigantean Growth ~ Gigantean	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A gigantean grows by up to four size categories, to a maximum of Colossal, keeping its proportions relative to other creatures pushed to the same category, so a gigantean human is smaller than a gigantean ogre. Its size modifier to AC becomes the one for its new size and its natural armor rises by the amount for its old size: Fine +0, Diminutive +2, Tiny +5, Small +9, Medium +14, Large +12, Huge +9, Gargantuan +5, Colossal +0. Its racial Hit Dice multiply by 6 from Fine to Medium, 4 from Large or Huge, and 2 from Gargantuan or Colossal; class Hit Dice do not multiply, a creature with only class levels counts as having 1 racial HD, and a Fine to Medium creature with 2 or fewer racial HD simply ends up with 15 HD. Recalculate base attack bonus, base saves, skill points and CMB/CMD for the new HD, type, size and ability scores, keeping only the base creature's bonus feats and racial skill bonuses. Each speed is multiplied by the number of size categories gained, and natural attack damage, ability damage or drain and energy damage each scale up one step per size category gained, though negative levels do not. An undead or construct base creature ignores the Constitution bonus. The CR rises by +1 per 4 added HD, or +1 per 2 for dragons and outsiders and +1 per 3 for magical beasts and monstrous humanoids; check the result against creatures of up to 3 CR higher.	SOURCEPAGE:p.160
Gigantean Senses	KEY:Gigantean Senses ~ Gigantean	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The range of each of the gigantean's senses grows by the base creature's value multiplied by the number of size categories gained. The ranges and areas of its special attacks other than spells and spell-like abilities grow the same way.	SOURCEPAGE:p.160
Trample	KEY:Trample ~ Gigantean	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A gigantean gains the trample special attack. A creature with no slam attack uses the slam damage for a creature of the gigantean's size.	SOURCEPAGE:p.162
Massive	KEY:Massive ~ Gigantean	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A gigantean grown from a Gargantuan or Colossal base creature is so massive that uneven ground and other difficult terrain barely slow it, though forest and settlements still count as difficult terrain for it. A Huge or smaller creature can move through a square the gigantean occupies, and the gigantean through theirs.	SOURCEPAGE:p.162

###Block: Green Warden, Green Blighter
Warden Regeneration	KEY:Warden Regeneration ~ Green Warden	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A green warden has regeneration 5, bypassed by fire or cold. Its land speed rises by 10 feet, and a base creature with no land speed gains one of 15 feet.	SOURCEPAGE:p.164
Renew Deadwood	KEY:Renew Deadwood ~ Green Warden	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once every 1d4 rounds, a green warden produces an effect like warp wood at a caster level equal to its racial Hit Dice, affecting only dead wood. Wooden objects so affected become living plants that root themselves on touching the ground. It cannot unwarp wood or restore its shape with this ability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.164
Favored Terrain	KEY:Favored Terrain ~ Green Warden	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The environment a green warden inhabits counts as favored terrain for it, as the ranger ability, stacking with a ranger's own choices. It must live in that territory for more than half the year to gain and keep this.	SOURCEPAGE:p.165
Natural Druid	KEY:Natural Druid ~ Green Warden	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A green warden with druid levels counts as one level higher for druid spells and other druid abilities.	SOURCEPAGE:p.165
Trackless Step	KEY:Trackless Step ~ Green Warden	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A green warden leaves no trail in natural surroundings and cannot be tracked, though it may choose to leave a trail.	SOURCEPAGE:p.165
Blighting Spells	KEY:Blighting Spells ~ Green Blighter	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any of a green blighter's spells or spell-like abilities that affect living plants instead affect only dead, diseased or rotting ones, and healing spells such as goodberry deal that amount as damage. Its purify food and drink becomes putrefy food and drink, and any water or food it creates is mildly poisonous: a creature that consumes it is nauseated for 1d6 rounds, or 1 round on a successful Fortitude save against the spell's DC. Created water kills normal plants watered with it within 24 hours; plant creatures are not killed but are nauseated as above.	SOURCEPAGE:p.166
Deadwood	KEY:Deadwood ~ Green Blighter	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once every 1d4 rounds, a green blighter produces an effect like warp wood at a caster level equal to its racial Hit Dice, affecting only living wood, which turns to deadwood. It cannot unwarp wood or restore its shape. A plant creature caught by the effect takes 1d4 damage per total HD of the blighter, to a maximum of 20d4, negated by a Fortitude save. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.166

###Block: Heralds of the Apocalypse
Apocalyptic Fear	KEY:Apocalyptic Fear ~ Herald of the Apocalypse	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:Any living creature within 100 feet of a Herald must succeed on a Will save or suffer cumulative fear. Failing against one Herald leaves a creature shaken for 1 hour; failing against a second while still shaken leaves it frightened for 10 rounds; failing against a third while still frightened leaves it panicked for 1d6 rounds; failing against the fourth while still panicked kills it instantly. The durations overlap. A creature that saves is immune to that Herald's fear for 1 hour, or until its shaken condition ends if it is already shaken. This is a mind-affecting fear effect with a Charisma-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.167
Herald Immunities	KEY:Herald Immunities ~ Herald of the Apocalypse	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A Herald is immune to energy drain, ability damage and drain, spells and effects of the illusion school, and mind-affecting effects.	SOURCEPAGE:p.167
Herald Protection	KEY:Herald Protection ~ Herald of the Apocalypse	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:The Four Heralds sometimes work in concert. Each is immune to the others' special attacks and to the special attacks of the others' possessed hosts, such as breath weapons, poison, gaze attacks or energy drain.	SOURCEPAGE:p.167
Channel Energy Vulnerability	KEY:Channel Energy Vulnerability ~ Herald of the Apocalypse	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A Herald takes +50%% damage from channeled positive energy. A Herald destroyed by channeled positive energy is free to possess a new host.	SOURCEPAGE:p.167
Turn and Command Vulnerability	KEY:Turn and Command Vulnerability ~ Herald of the Apocalypse	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A Herald can be turned or commanded with the Turn Undead and Command Undead feats as though it were an undead creature with HD equal to its character level. Destruction frees it to possess a new host.	SOURCEPAGE:p.167
Possess Creature	KEY:Possess Creature ~ Herald of the Apocalypse	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once per hour, as a full-round action, a Herald without a host can try to possess any creature within 500 feet of an existing Herald, needing no line of effect and no knowledge of the target. The target must succeed on a DC 20 Will save or gain the matching Herald template; on a success it is immune to possession by any Herald for 1 hour. Once applied, the essence cannot be expelled by magic. Killing the host expels the essence, which may immediately try another creature within 500 feet of another possessed Herald; a Herald whose host is incapacitated, immobilised, paralyzed or unconscious may also move on, and the abandoned host is then immune to possession for 1 hour. When all four Heralds are hostless at once, their essences return whence they came until another apocalypse calls them.	SOURCEPAGE:p.167
Hive Mind	KEY:Hive Mind ~ Herald of the Apocalypse	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:While possessing hosts, the four Heralds are in constant mental communication whatever the distance or their hosts' languages. If one knows of a danger they all do; if one is not flat-footed, none are; and none is flanked unless all are. An essence without a host does not share the hive mind.	SOURCEPAGE:p.167
Phantom Mount	KEY:Phantom Mount ~ Herald of the Apocalypse	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:At will, as a standard action, a Herald summons a saddled phantom mount one size category larger than itself, which appears beneath it and lifts it into the saddle even if the Herald could not normally ride. The mount lasts until dismissed, dispelled, or until the Herald dismounts or is unhorsed. It has no real body and can carry only its summoner, flies at 10 feet per character level of the Herald with perfect maneuverability, and gives no cover, though its bulk may give concealment. A Herald cannot use Trample or bull rush while mounted on it, and attacks and creatures pass through it, though dispel magic at the Herald's character level can dispel it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.167
Herald's Weapon	KEY:Herald's Weapon ~ Herald of the Apocalypse	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:While riding its phantom mount, a Herald is automatically equipped with a minor artifact weapon matching its nature. The weapon vanishes if it ever leaves the Herald's hands and can be wielded only while mounted.	SOURCEPAGE:p.167
Immunity to Death Effects	KEY:Immunity to Death Effects ~ Herald of Death	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A Herald of Death is immune to all death effects.	SOURCEPAGE:p.168
Death Scythe	KEY:Death Scythe ~ Herald of Death	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a standard action while riding its phantom mount, the Herald of Death summons a grave-dirt-covered +1 keen adamantine scythe sized for the base creature. Besides its normal damage, a foe struck must succeed on a Fortitude save or drop to -1 hp and gain the dying condition. The scythe vanishes if released and cannot be summoned while unmounted. This is a death effect with a Charisma-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.168
Finger of Death	KEY:Finger of Death ~ Herald of Death	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a standard action, once every 1d4 rounds, the Herald of Death points at any creature within 500 feet; it must succeed on a Fortitude save or die instantly. Any other creature that touches the corpse within 1 hour must save at the same DC or die as well. This is a death effect with a Charisma-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.168
Aura of Desolation	KEY:Aura of Desolation ~ Herald of Famine	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:Normal plants within 500 feet of the Herald of Famine wilt and lose all fruit and seeds; trees and other hardy plants lie dormant until renewed by water and sunlight, and smaller plants die at once. A plant creature or magic plant must succeed on a Fortitude save each round in the aura or take 2d6 points of damage. Animals and vermin are automatically sickened while in the aura and for at least 24 hours after leaving it, with a Fortitude save each day thereafter to end the effect. The save DCs are Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.170
Scales of Want	KEY:Scales of Want ~ Herald of Famine	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a standard action while riding its phantom mount, the Herald of Famine summons a set of black scales it wields as a +1 countering adamantine heavy flail sized for the base creature. Besides its normal damage, a creature struck must succeed on a Constitution check (DC 10 + the Herald's Cha modifier) or take 4d6 points of nonlethal damage and become fatigued. Neither the nonlethal damage nor the fatigue can be removed by rest, magic, fast healing or regeneration until the creature eats a full day's meals. A second failed check deals the same nonlethal damage but does not extend the fatigue or make the target exhausted. The scales vanish if released and cannot be summoned while unmounted.	SOURCEPAGE:p.170
Immunity to Starvation	KEY:Immunity to Starvation ~ Herald of Famine	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A Herald of Famine is immune to the effects of starvation and of dehydration and never takes damage from either.	SOURCEPAGE:p.170
Air of Contagion	KEY:Air of Contagion ~ Herald of Pestilence	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.Aura	DESC:An invisible cloud of contagion surrounds the Herald of Pestilence at all times. Any breathing creature that begins its turn within 30 feet must succeed on two Fortitude saves, one against cackle fever and one against mindfire. The save DCs are Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.172
Pestilence	KEY:Pestilence ~ Herald of Pestilence	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:The Herald of Pestilence gains a melee touch attack that deals no damage but inflicts the black rot, as do all its natural attacks. Black rot--contact; save Fortitude; onset 1d4 rounds; frequency 1/day; effect 1d6 Con, 1d6 Dex and nauseated; cure 3 consecutive saves; Constitution-based DC. Black boils cover the victim, who suffers chills, hot flashes and nausea, and can pass the disease on by touch. It is so virulent that it can infect creatures immune to disease, other Heralds excepted, though they save at +10.	SOURCEPAGE:p.172
Fell Bow	KEY:Fell Bow ~ Herald of Pestilence	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a standard action while riding its phantom mount, the Herald of Pestilence summons a ghostly white +1 longbow sized for the base creature, firing an endless supply of white arrows. Besides its normal damage, a foe struck must succeed on a Fortitude save against the Herald's pestilence or contract black rot. The bow vanishes if released and cannot be summoned while unmounted.	SOURCEPAGE:p.172
Battle Gaze	KEY:Battle Gaze ~ Herald of War	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any creature within 10 feet that meets the Herald of War's gaze must make a Will save or be filled with battle lust and attack the nearest creature other than the Herald as well as it can for 1d4 rounds. A creature that fails need not save again until that battle lust ends. This is a gaze and mind-affecting effect with a Charisma-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.174
Fell Sword	KEY:Fell Sword ~ Herald of War	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a free action while riding its phantom mount, the Herald of War summons a blood-red +1 ominous adamantine greatsword sized for the base creature. Besides its normal damage, a creature struck must succeed on a Will save or be affected as by dominate monster at the Herald's character level. It can dominate up to twice its total HD in creatures at once, usually setting them as an honour guard. The sword vanishes if released and cannot be summoned while unmounted. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.174

###Block: Holy Creature, Icy Creature, Id Ooze, Instrument of the Gods
Grace	KEY:Grace ~ Holy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:Every nongood creature within 30 ft. of a holy creature automatically takes a -1 penalty on all attack rolls, checks and saves. Grace is a mind-affecting effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.175
Negative Energy Resistance	KEY:Negative Energy Resistance ~ Holy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:When struck by a negative energy attack, whether energy drain, ability damage or drain, or hit point damage such as an inflict spell, a holy creature may make a level check (1d20 + total HD) against DC 11 + the attacker's total Hit Dice. On a success the attack is cancelled in a bright flash, and if it came from a melee or melee touch attack the attacker takes 2d6 points of damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.175
Protection from Evil	KEY:Protection from Evil ~ Holy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:A holy creature gains a +2 deflection bonus to AC and a +2 resistance bonus on saves against attacks by evil creatures, and is immune to any attempt by an evil creature to possess, charm or influence it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.175
Holy Spellcasting	KEY:Holy Spellcasting ~ Holy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A holy creature's effective caster level for spells and spell-like abilities of the healing subschool and those with the good or light descriptor is +1 higher than the base creature's. The bonus stacks with itself, so a spell with both the good and light descriptors is cast at +2 caster levels.	SOURCEPAGE:p.175
Sacredness	KEY:Sacredness ~ Holy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Each of a holy creature's melee attacks with a natural or manufactured weapon deals +1d6 points of holy damage to evil creatures, and all its natural and manufactured weapons count as good-aligned for overcoming damage reduction.	SOURCEPAGE:p.175
Holy Body	KEY:Holy Body ~ Holy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A holy creature gains double the normal healing from positive energy: a cure light wounds that would restore 7 hit points restores 14 instead.	SOURCEPAGE:p.176
Cold Aura	KEY:Cold Aura ~ Icy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.Aura	DESC:An icy creature emits an aura of cold. Any creature within 10 feet takes 2d6 points of cold damage per round it stays in range, halved on a successful Fortitude save. The icy creature can suppress or resume the aura as a free action. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.177
Exude Ice	KEY:Exude Ice ~ Icy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:At will, as a full-round action, an icy creature exudes a 20-foot-diameter spread of slippery ice centred on itself. The ice stays until it melts at the ambient temperature. Creatures spend 2 squares of movement to enter any iced square, and the DC of any Acrobatics check in the area rises by +5.	SOURCEPAGE:p.177
Ice Mastery	KEY:Ice Mastery ~ Icy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An icy creature gains a +1 morale bonus on attack and damage rolls when its foe is touching ice.	SOURCEPAGE:p.177
Icy Touch	KEY:Icy Touch ~ Icy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Each of an icy creature's natural melee attacks, including successful grapple checks on its turn, and its attacks with metallic melee weapons deal +1d6 points of cold damage. A creature so damaged must succeed on a Fortitude save or be paralyzed for 1d4 rounds. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.177
Icewalking	KEY:Icewalking ~ Icy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:As the spider climb spell, but only on icy surfaces. The creature moves across ice without penalty and needs no Acrobatics check to run or charge on it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.178
Icy Body	KEY:Icy Body ~ Icy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:Any creature that makes a natural or unarmed attack against an icy creature takes 1d6 points of cold damage, and a creature grappling it takes that damage on top of the damage from its cold aura.	SOURCEPAGE:p.178
Awakened Ooze	KEY:Awakened Ooze ~ Id Ooze	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An id ooze loses the mindless quality and any immunity to mind-affecting effects. A base creature with no Intelligence score, or one below 10, gains Intelligence 10; one with 10 or more gains +4 Intelligence instead. It gains the normal number of feats for its HD, and skills with Perception and Stealth as class skills, plus Climb with a climb speed and Swim with a swim speed. It cannot speak but understands languages if its Intelligence allows.	SOURCEPAGE:p.179
Pseudopod Grasp	KEY:Pseudopod Grasp ~ Id Ooze	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:An id ooze keeps the base creature's attacks but not its weapon and armor proficiencies, and can wield a weapon of its size instead of attacking naturally. One pseudopod can hold or manipulate any one-handed object; a creature with more than one natural attack can use two pseudopods as a creature wielding a weapon two-handed, which prevents any natural attacks. It gains no proficiency without the matching feats. It can use a shield, though a creature with only one natural attack cannot attack at all while doing so. It deals normal damage with natural attacks and wielded weapons, but an object it holds takes its touch or slam energy damage, such as acid, once per round at the end of its turn, unless the material is immune.	SOURCEPAGE:p.179
Blindsight	KEY:Blindsight ~ Instrument of the Gods	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Vision	DESC:An instrument of the gods gains blindsight to a range of 10 feet per CR of the base creature.	SOURCEPAGE:p.180
Instrument Immunities	KEY:Instrument Immunities ~ Instrument of the Gods	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:An instrument of the gods is immune to ability damage, bleed, disease, energy drain, mind-affecting effects, paralysis, permanent wounds, petrification, poison and polymorph, and loses all its weaknesses. Its spell resistance equals its final CR + 10, or rises by 4 if it already had at least that much.	SOURCEPAGE:p.180
Divine Regeneration	KEY:Divine Regeneration ~ Instrument of the Gods	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An instrument of the gods has regeneration equal to the base creature's CR plus 20, which no attack can suppress: it regenerates even if disintegrated or slain by a death effect. If it fails a save against an effect that would kill it instantly, it rises 3 rounds later with 1 hit point provided its remains take no further damage. It can be banished or transported away to save a region, but no way to truly kill it is known. This replaces any regeneration or fast healing the base creature had.	SOURCEPAGE:p.180
Improved Mythic Surge	KEY:Improved Mythic Surge ~ Instrument of the Gods	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Instead of spending mythic power, an instrument of the gods can use its surge ability once per round as a free action.	SOURCEPAGE:p.180
Instrument Mythic Tier	KEY:Instrument Mythic Tier ~ Instrument of the Gods	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:An instrument of the gods has a mythic tier equal to half the base creature's CR, to a maximum of tier 10, gaining all the cumulative base mythic abilities of that tier without choosing a mythic path, plus bonus hit points equal to its Hit Die per tier. It gains the mythic subtype but none of that subtype's other abilities.	SOURCEPAGE:p.180

###Block: Inveigler, Jotunblood Giant
Charming Falsehood	KEY:Charming Falsehood ~ Inveigler	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once per day an inveigler tells a lie so convincing that it enchants one creature that hears it. It need not see the target or have line of effect, but a target that cannot hear the lie wastes the use. The lie must be one that would make the target treat the inveigler as a trusted friend or follow its orders, however outlandish. The target attempts a Sense Motive check opposed by the inveigler's Bluff check; failing by less than 5 leaves it charmed as by charm monster, and failing by 5 or more dominated as by dominate monster, in both cases at the inveigler's character level. This is a sonic, mind-affecting charm effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.182
Hidden Enchantment	KEY:Hidden Enchantment ~ Inveigler	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:When an inveigler uses any effect that mimics charm monster, dominate monster or the like, spells such as detect magic cannot detect it, and any Sense Motive check to spot the influence takes a -15 penalty. True seeing and other magic that reveals magical effects or the truth of a situation work normally.	SOURCEPAGE:p.183
Taken to the Grave	KEY:Taken to the Grave ~ Inveigler	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Speak with dead used on an inveigler's corpse or head returns nothing but lies. Only a wish or miracle mimicking speak with dead can pry the truth from it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.183
Undetectable Nature	KEY:Undetectable Nature ~ Inveigler	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Magic used to determine an inveigler's alignment or true form automatically reports it as matching the detecting creature's own, and an inveigler aware of the attempt can make the magic report any alignment it likes. This also defeats spells that detect a single alignment component, such as detect evil, and even true seeing; only a wish or miracle, even one mimicking a lesser spell, reveals the truth.	SOURCEPAGE:p.183
Undetectable Thoughts	KEY:Undetectable Thoughts ~ Inveigler	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Whenever a creature tries to detect an inveigler's thoughts, with detect thoughts for example, the inveigler knows at once and can make the effect report any thoughts it chooses. A wish or miracle mimicking detect thoughts reveals its true thoughts.	SOURCEPAGE:p.183
Jotunblood Growth	KEY:Jotunblood Growth ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A jotunblood giant grows one size category and gains 10 racial Hit Dice; PCGen cannot add racial HD through a template, so add them to the base race by hand. Its size modifier to AC becomes the one for its new size and its natural armor rises by that size's bonus: Large +6, Huge +7, Gargantuan +8, Colossal +9. Every speed rises by 10 ft., and each natural weapon's base damage goes up one step. Its ability scores change by final size: Large Str +8, Dex -2, Con +2, Fly -2, Stealth -4; Huge Str +8, Dex -2, Con +4, Fly -4, Stealth -8; Gargantuan Str +8, Con +4, Fly -6, Stealth -12; Colossal Str +8, Con +4, Fly -8, Stealth -16. A Colossal base creature also gains the massive special quality.	SOURCEPAGE:p.184
Improved Rock Throwing	KEY:Improved Rock Throwing ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A jotunblood giant gains rock throwing even if the base creature lacked it, with a +1 racial bonus on attack rolls to throw rocks that stacks with the Rock Throwing ability. It can hurl rocks up to two size categories smaller than itself, out to five range increments: Large 120 ft., Huge 150 ft., Gargantuan 200 ft., Colossal 250 ft. A rock is any large, bulky, regularly shaped object of hardness 5 or more, and thrown-rock damage is three times the creature's base slam damage plus 1-1/2 its Strength bonus. A better rock throwing ability on the base creature is used instead.	SOURCEPAGE:p.184
Jotunblood Ash Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Ash Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Breath Weapon (Su): once every 1d4 rounds the giant breathes a 40-ft. cone of foulness and disease; each creature caught must make a Constitution-based Reflex save or be exposed to the ash giant's disease, then still make the disease's own Fortitude save. Quality: immunity to all magic except force effects and remove disease, which leaves it nauseated on a failed Fortitude save.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Athach	KEY:Jotunblood Athach ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:The jotunblood athach's poison becomes far more virulent, dealing 1d8 Str damage. Quality: darkvision +120 ft.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Cave Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Cave Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Charging Gore (Ex): during a bull rush the giant may impale a foe on its tusks instead of pushing it, dealing 6d6 + 1-1/2 its Strength modifier as piercing damage; a foe at least two size categories smaller is hurled as a free action like a rock, dealing the giant's flung-rock damage to anything it hits and to itself. Quality: frightful presence (120 ft.), to which cave giants are immune from one another.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Cliff Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Cliff Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Earth Shaking Blow (Ex): as a standard action the giant pounds the ground, producing an effect identical to earthquake in a 40-ft.-radius spread. Quality -- Swift Climber (Ex): a climb speed of double its base speed, Climb as a class skill, and accelerated climbing at full speed with a -5 penalty.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Cloud Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Cloud Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Breath Weapon (Su): once every 1d4 rounds the giant breathes a 40-foot cone of thunderous noise dealing 10d6 points of sonic damage, halved on a Constitution-based Reflex save. Quality: immunity to sonic damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Cyclops	KEY:Jotunblood Cyclops ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Eye Blast (Su): every 1d4 rounds the giant releases a 60-ft. line of energy as a touch attack dealing 10d6 force damage, halved on a Reflex save whose Charisma-based DC gains a +4 racial bonus. Quality -- Battle Insight (Su): an insight bonus to AC equal to its Wisdom modifier (minimum +0).	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Desert Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Desert Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Sandstorm Breath (Su): once every 1d4 rounds the giant releases a 40-ft. cone of blasting sand and wind dealing 10d6 slashing damage, halved on a Reflex save, and blinding for 1d6 rounds anyone who fails a Fortitude save; both saves are Constitution-based. Quality -- Sand Swimming (Ex): it moves through sand as if swimming through water at its base speed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Ettin	KEY:Jotunblood Ettin ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Extra Attacks (Ex): the giant has four heads and four arms and attacks with all four arms at no penalty. Quality -- Shift Sleeping (Ex): its heads sleep in shifts, so it can never be taken unaware while asleep and regains hit points and heals ability damage as though it had bed rest while still active; sleeping heads do not control their arms and cannot sleep in combat, and the giant is immune to sleep effects.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Fire Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Fire Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Breath Weapon (Su): once every 1d4 rounds the giant breathes a 40-foot cone of fire dealing 10d6 fire damage, halved on a Constitution-based Reflex save. Quality: its internal fire gives it cold resistance 20.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Frost Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Frost Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Breath Weapon (Su): once every 1d4 rounds the giant breathes a 40-foot cone of cold dealing 10d6 cold damage, halved on a Constitution-based Reflex save. Quality: its core of ice gives it fire resistance 20.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Hill Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Hill Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Earth-Shaking Bellow (Su): once every 1d4 rounds the giant lets loose a yell that works like earthquake, in a 40-foot cone directed away from it. Quality -- Meld into Earth (Su): at will it melds into earth, though not solid stone, as meld into stone but for as long as it wishes; move earth cast on its location expels it for 5d6 points of damage, and while melded it heals 1 hit point per round.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Jungle Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Jungle Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Animate Jungle (Su): once per day the giant brings all foliage within 60 ft. to life. Each round the plants attempt a grapple against every foe in the area using the giant's CMB, and a maintained grapple deals 1d8+10 damage; their CMD is the giant's as well. The foliage stays animate for a number of rounds equal to the giant's total Hit Dice. Quality -- Trackless Step (Ex): it leaves no trail in jungle and cannot be tracked, unless it chooses otherwise.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Marsh Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Marsh Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Entomb (Ex): as a full-round action, on a successful grapple check, the giant smashes a Large or smaller foe into marshy or muddy ground, entombing it. An entombed creature begins to suffocate unless it can survive without air; it may escape with a DC 25 Strength check, emerging prone, or allies may dig it free with 1d4+1 rounds of full-round actions. This works only in marshy or muddy terrain. Quality: immunity to disease.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Merrow	KEY:Jotunblood Merrow ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Drowning Touch (Su): on any successful natural attack the target's lungs fill with water and it begins to drown; an initial Fortitude save negates this, otherwise 2 consecutive Fortitude saves are needed to stop drowning. A target that makes either set of saves is immune to that giant's drowning touch for 24 hours. The save DC is Constitution-based. Quality -- Tireless Swimmer (Ex): it takes no nonlethal damage from long swims and cannot become nauseated, exhausted or fatigued in its native water.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Ocean Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Ocean Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Crushing Depths (Su): with a touch attack the giant imparts the pressure of the deep ocean, dealing 5d6 bludgeoning damage plus 10d6 nonlethal damage; a Charisma-based Fortitude save negates the bludgeoning damage but not the nonlethal. Quality: immunity to cold.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Ogre	KEY:Jotunblood Ogre ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Stunning Blow (Ex): once every 1d4 rounds the giant imbues its melee attacks with stunning force; a creature damaged must succeed on a Strength-based Fortitude save or be stunned for 1d2 rounds. Quality: darkvision +120 ft.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood River Giant	KEY:Jotunblood River Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Power of the River (Su): once per day, as a full-round action, the giant summons its total Hit Dice worth of river animals, magical beasts and vermin, which arrive on its next turn and serve for 12 hours or until released. They never attack their summoner but may act against other river giants. Quality -- Unerring Direction (Ex): on a river, directly or by boat, it can never become lost and is immune to effects that misdirect it, including most illusion and compulsion effects.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Rune Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Rune Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Thrown Runes (Su): once every 1d4 rounds the giant tears off and throws one of its runes, taking 1d6 points of damage itself. The rune flies up to 120 ft. and explodes for 10d6 points of force or chosen energy damage (acid, cold, electricity, fire or sonic) in a 30 ft. radius, halved on a Dexterity-based Reflex save; the rune returns at once but the self-inflicted damage is not healed. Quality -- Jotunblood Charisma (Su): a +8 racial bonus to the save DC of charm and compulsion effects used against giants, and against giants its mind-affecting, charm and compulsion effects bypass all immunities. This replaces a rune giant's command ability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Slag Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Slag Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Breath Weapon (Su): once every 1d4 rounds the giant breathes a 40-ft. cone of partially molten metal dealing 10d6 points of fire and slashing damage, or 5d6 to a creature immune to only one of those, halved on a Constitution-based Reflex save. Quality -- Legendary Crafter (Su): it can craft nonmagical and masterwork items of legendary quality.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Stone Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Stone Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Stone Calling (Su): the giant can call any unattended rock within 1,000 feet that it could normally lift and throw, resolving the attack as though it stood where the rock is and adding its Strength bonus to damage. It can hurl rocks at foes it cannot see, guessing their position, with a 50%% miss chance even when it guesses right. Quality: damage reduction 10/adamantine.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Storm Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Storm Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Breath Weapon (Su): once every 1d4 rounds the giant breathes a 40-foot cone of lightning dealing 10d6 points of electricity damage, halved on a Constitution-based Reflex save. Quality: sonic resistance 20.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Taiga Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Taiga Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Rage (Ex): the giant can rage as the barbarian ability for a number of rounds per day equal to its racial Hit Dice, stacking with any class or feat that grants rage. Quality -- Boreal Friendship (Su): a +4 bonus on all checks to befriend and influence creatures from cold, mountainous or forested environments, whose starting attitude towards it is one step friendlier.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Troll	KEY:Jotunblood Troll ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Great Rend (Ex): when the giant hits with both claws it automatically deals double the base creature's rend damage plus 1-1/2 its Strength bonus, replacing the troll's rend. Quality -- Statue Form (Su): as a free action once per round it turns to stone as the statue spell, gaining hardness 8, and may stay that way as long as it wishes, returning to normal as a free action, acting, and becoming a statue again as another free action.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Wood Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Wood Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Will of the Wood (Ex): once per day, as a full-round action, the giant makes animals and plants of Intelligence 2 or less within 200 ft. grow two size categories. They obey the giant until the next sunrise or sunset, whichever comes first, never turning on it though they may act against other wood giants. The total Hit Dice affected equals the giant's racial Hit Dice or its caster level, whichever is greater. Quality -- Speak with Plants (Sp): speak with plants as a constant spell-like ability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185
Jotunblood Other Giant	KEY:Jotunblood Other Giant ~ Jotunblood Giant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Trample (Ex): the giant can trample foes up to one size category smaller than itself, dealing its slam damage plus 1-1/2 its Strength modifier, or by size if it has no slam: Large 1d6, Huge 2d6, Gargantuan 2d8, Colossal 4d6. The save DC is Strength-based. Quality: fast healing 5.	SOURCEPAGE:p.185

###Block: Lawbound, Lifespark Construct, Limbjack
See Law	KEY:See Law ~ Lawbound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Vision	DESC:At will, a lawbound can identify any lawful creature, spell or magic item it can see, as the detect law spell at a caster level equal to its character level, and as though it had studied them for 3 rounds.	SOURCEPAGE:p.189
Aura of Order	KEY:Aura of Order ~ Lawbound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:A lawbound radiates an aura of order with a 10-foot radius.	SOURCEPAGE:p.189
Law's Shift	KEY:Law's Shift ~ Lawbound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once per day, by touch, a lawbound can force a creature's alignment one step towards lawful. A Will save negates the effect and grants immunity to that lawbound's law's shift for a day; otherwise the change is permanent and the target may suffer the usual penalties for changing alignment. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.189
Lawful Strike	KEY:Lawful Strike ~ Lawbound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any melee attack a lawbound makes with a natural or manufactured weapon deals an extra 1d6 points of damage to chaotic creatures and creatures with the chaotic subtype, and its attacks count as lawful-aligned for overcoming damage reduction.	SOURCEPAGE:p.189
Chaos's Failure	KEY:Chaos's Failure ~ Lawbound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:If a spell with the chaotic descriptor is cast within 60 feet of a lawbound, the caster must succeed on a caster level check or the spell fails and is wasted. The DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.190
Awakened Spark	KEY:Awakened Spark ~ Lifespark Construct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A lifespark construct keeps the construct type but loses several of its features. Roll or buy new Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma scores as for a new character, using half the allocated points under point buy; every other score is unchanged. It keeps its racial bonus feats but loses all other feats and repurchases them for its character level, and gains 2 + Int modifier skill points per HD, minimum 1, usually spent on the Craft skill that repairs it. It can speak even without a mouth, knowing its creator's language and choosing bonus languages from among those its creator knows.	SOURCEPAGE:p.191
Healing Immunity	KEY:Healing Immunity ~ Lifespark Construct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A lifespark construct cannot be affected by spells with the healing descriptor unless the spell specifically states that it affects constructs.	SOURCEPAGE:p.191
Open Mind	KEY:Open Mind ~ Lifespark Construct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A lifespark construct is not immune to mind-affecting effects and, perhaps from its old need for orders, takes a -2 penalty on saving throws against them. Golems remain immune to magic as their entries describe.	SOURCEPAGE:p.191
Spirit Within	KEY:Spirit Within ~ Lifespark Construct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A spirit resides in the lifespark construct, so astral projection, clone, magic jar and soul bind can affect it, though no other necromantic effect can and it is still immune to death effects. It cannot be raised or resurrected but can be reincarnated. Lifespark golems remain immune to magic as their entries describe.	SOURCEPAGE:p.191
Accelerated Repair	KEY:Accelerated Repair ~ Lifespark Construct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:As a full-round action, a lifespark construct can jerry-rig itself with an appropriate Craft check against a DC 10 lower than the DC to create the construct, minimum 10, healing 1d4 hit points per point by which it beat the DC. This provokes attacks of opportunity. It can instead make a standard repair effort, without the usual repair cost, taking one day of constant work.	SOURCEPAGE:p.192
Construct Limbs	KEY:Construct Limbs ~ Limbjack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:One or more of the creature's limbs are replaced with golem-like construct limbs. An arm is any limb that could wield a weapon or is not used for movement; a leg is any other. Each replaced arm without a natural attack gains a slam or claw dealing damage as a creature one size larger, primary if the creature has no other attacks and secondary otherwise; an existing natural attack on a replaced limb keeps its status and gains one damage step. The limbjack gains a shield bonus to AC of 1, plus 1 per replaced arm, plus 2 if all its legs are replaced. Replacing all its legs doubles its base land speed. Its Strength rises by +2 per replaced arm and by +2 more if all legs are replaced, and its Constitution by +2 if all arms or all legs are replaced; these stack. The CR rises by +1, a further +1 per 2 arms replaced beyond the first two, and +1 more if every limb is replaced.	SOURCEPAGE:p.193
Limb Defense	KEY:Limb Defense ~ Limbjack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:Against damage aimed specifically at a replaced limb, such as an attempt to sunder it or an attack from a foe touching or attacking it, the limbjack has DR 20/adamantine and acid, cold and fire resistance 30. Against spells that specifically target a replaced limb it has spell resistance equal to 15 + its CR.	SOURCEPAGE:p.193
Metal Body	KEY:Metal Body ~ Limbjack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:Enough of a limbjack is metal to make it vulnerable to effects that target metal: it counts as a ferrous creature for rusting grasp and other spells with special effects on metal.	SOURCEPAGE:p.193
Tireless	KEY:Tireless ~ Limbjack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A limbjack has no limit on how long it can run and risks neither fatigue nor exhaustion from forced marching.	SOURCEPAGE:p.193
Upgradable Limbs	KEY:Upgradable Limbs ~ Limbjack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Any natural attack tied to a replaced limb can be made masterwork, built from a different material, or turned into a magic weapon, at the cost of a longsword of the limbjack's size.	SOURCEPAGE:p.194
Limbjack Construction	KEY:Limbjack Construction ~ Limbjack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Making limbjack prosthetics and bonding them to a living creature works like building a golem: CL 9th; Price 1,200 gp x the recipient's HD x the number of limbs replaced; Requirements Craft Construct, greater polymorph, limited wish, regenerate, creator caster level 9th; Skill Heal DC 25; Cost 600 gp x the recipient's HD x the number of limbs replaced.	SOURCEPAGE:p.194

###Block: Magma Creature, Manimal, Metal-Clad Creature, Miniature
Fiery Aura	KEY:Fiery Aura ~ Magma Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.Aura	DESC:Any creature within 10 feet takes 2d6 points of fire damage per round it remains in range, halved on a successful Fortitude save. The magma creature can suppress or resume the aura as a free action. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.195
Magma Movement	KEY:Magma Movement ~ Magma Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A magma creature gains a burrow speed equal to its highest speed and can swim through magma and lava at that speed, as a creature with a swim speed moves through water. This grants no swim speed in water.	SOURCEPAGE:p.195
Magma Strikes	KEY:Magma Strikes ~ Magma Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:All of a magma creature's natural attacks gain burn (2d6) and grab, and it gains engulf dealing 2d6 bludgeoning and 4d6 fire damage against creatures at least one size category smaller than itself.	SOURCEPAGE:p.195
Earth Mastery	KEY:Earth Mastery ~ Magma Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A magma creature gains a +1 bonus on attack and damage rolls when both it and its foe touch the ground, and takes a -4 penalty when its opponent is airborne or waterborne. These modifiers apply to bull rush and overrun, whether initiating or resisting.	SOURCEPAGE:p.195
Manimal Form	KEY:Manimal Form ~ Manimal	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A manimal keeps every attack of the base creature except those on limbs that became legs, loses rake, and gains the weapon and armor proficiencies of a monstrous humanoid. Its space and reach suit its size, a long creature becoming tall, and greater-than-normal reach gaining 5 feet. Recalculate its base attack bonus, saves and skill points for its new type.	SOURCEPAGE:p.197
Animal Blood	KEY:Animal Blood ~ Manimal	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A manimal counts as an animal, a monstrous humanoid and a humanoid for spells, abilities and effects that target specific types. It gets a Will save against any spell or effect that specifically affects animals, even one that normally allows no save: DC 10 + the spell's level + the caster's relevant ability modifier, or for a non-spell 10 + half the manimal's HD + its Charisma modifier. A success grants immunity to that effect for 24 hours. Awaken has no effect on a manimal.	SOURCEPAGE:p.198
Amphibious	KEY:Amphibious ~ Manimal	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A manimal whose base creature had the aquatic subtype but not the amphibious quality gains it, breathing air and water equally well.	SOURCEPAGE:p.197
Light Fortification	KEY:Light Fortification ~ Metal-Clad Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:The metal plating gives the creature light fortification, as the armor special ability: a 25%% chance that a critical hit or sneak attack against it is treated as a normal hit.	SOURCEPAGE:p.199
Heavy Fortification	KEY:Heavy Fortification ~ Metal-Clad Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:The metal plating gives the creature heavy fortification, as the armor special ability: a 75%% chance that a critical hit or sneak attack against it is treated as a normal hit.	SOURCEPAGE:p.199
Special Fortification	KEY:Special Fortification ~ Metal-Clad Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:An adamantine-clad creature's plating goes beyond heavy fortification: see immune to precision damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.199
Vulnerability to Electricity	KEY:Vulnerability to Electricity ~ Metal-Clad Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A metal-clad creature takes half again as much damage (+50%%) from electricity unless it has some inherent resistance to it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.199
Metal Body	KEY:Metal Body ~ Metal-Clad Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A metal-clad creature counts as a ferrous creature for rusting grasp and other spells with special effects on metal.	SOURCEPAGE:p.199
Adamantine Plating	KEY:Adamantine Plating ~ Metal-Clad Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:An adamantine-clad creature has DR 10/adamantine and is immune to all precision damage, including sneak attacks and critical hits.	SOURCEPAGE:p.199
Divination Immunity	KEY:Divination Immunity ~ Metal-Clad Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:A lead-clad creature is immune to divination spells and effects cast to learn about it. Detect magic, detect poison, detect thoughts and alignment detections reveal nothing about it or what it carries; it is invisible and inaudible to scrying, arcane eye and clairaudience/clairvoyance; and neither discern location nor locate object can find it or its gear.	SOURCEPAGE:p.199
Mirrored Finish	KEY:Mirrored Finish ~ Metal-Clad Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:A silver-clad creature reflects gaze attacks and is immune to them, so a creature that actively gazes at it must save against its own gaze attack and suffers the consequences of a failure even if it would normally be immune.	SOURCEPAGE:p.199
Miniature Shrinking	KEY:Miniature Shrinking ~ Miniature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The creature shrinks four size categories, to a minimum of Fine, keeping its proportions relative to others pushed to the same category, so a miniature halfling is smaller than a miniature human. Its size modifier to AC becomes the one for its new size and its natural armor drops by the value for its old size: Fine to Medium -0, Large -2, Huge -5, Gargantuan -9, Colossal -14, never below +0. Divide the range of any sense with a stated range, and of any aura, by 20, rounded to the nearest 5 ft. Its racial Hit Dice drop by a quarter, and hit points, base attack bonus and the rest follow; fast healing or regeneration drops to a fifth of its value, minimum 1. Speeds fall to 5 ft. from 5-35 ft., 10 ft. from 40-55 ft., 15 ft. from 60-75 ft., and 20 ft. from 80-100 ft., with another increment above 100 ft. Natural attacks and manufactured weapons deal damage for the new size. Skill ranks above its new total become racial modifiers, and it keeps all its feats even without meeting the requirements, any excess counting as bonus feats. Its CR falls sharply against normal-sized foes: half or a quarter is a rule of thumb, but judge each creature against the Monster Creation appendix.	SOURCEPAGE:p.201

###Block: Mist Creature, Monstrous Lycanthrope
Cloud Sight	KEY:Cloud Sight ~ Mist Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Vision	DESC:A mist creature sees through clouds, gases, fogs, mists and smoke as though they did not hinder vision, so creatures and objects gain no concealment from them against it. It can use this while gaseous.	SOURCEPAGE:p.203
Mist Immunities	KEY:Mist Immunities ~ Mist Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A mist creature is immune to inhaled poisons and to gas-, fog- and cloud-based attacks and spells.	SOURCEPAGE:p.203
Air Mastery	KEY:Air Mastery ~ Mist Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Any airborne creature takes a -1 penalty on attack and damage rolls against a mist creature.	SOURCEPAGE:p.203
Air Breather	KEY:Air Breather ~ Mist Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A mist creature can breathe air even if the base creature breathed only water.	SOURCEPAGE:p.203
Gaseous Form	KEY:Gaseous Form ~ Mist Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A mist creature can assume gaseous form at will, as the spell but for as long as it wishes. Becoming gaseous or returning to its normal form is a move action, and it can use its spell-like abilities while gaseous.	SOURCEPAGE:p.204
Mist Stealth	KEY:Mist Stealth ~ Mist Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A gaseous mist creature in an area of fog, cloud, smoke or any similar condition gains a +15 circumstance bonus on Stealth checks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.203
Lycanthrope Forms	KEY:Lycanthrope Forms ~ Monstrous Lycanthrope	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A monstrous lycanthrope has a base form, a monster form and a hybrid form. The base monster may be any living creature whose size is within one step of the base creature's, and the hybrid is the larger of the two sizes. The base creature's type does not change, but it gains the shapechanger subtype and the base monster's subtypes, with all their abilities, in every form. In hybrid and monster form it has the base monster's senses, auras, natural attacks, special attacks and qualities, spell-like abilities and racial skill modifiers, plus the base monster's natural armor +2; in base and hybrid form it has the base creature's. Low-light vision and scent from the base monster apply in all forms. Hybrid form uses the base creature's land speed and the base monster's other movement modes. Natural spellcasting from the base monster works only in monster form. Its physical ability scores are unchanged in base form, and in hybrid and monster form take the higher of the base creature's and base monster's; a missing score on one side is filled from the other. It keeps the bonus feats and class skills of both. Its CR rises by a third of the base monster's CR, minimum +1.	SOURCEPAGE:p.205
Change Shape	KEY:Change Shape ~ Monstrous Lycanthrope	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Equipment does not meld between base and hybrid form but does between those and monster form. A natural monstrous lycanthrope shifts between any of its forms as a move-equivalent action. An afflicted one takes monster or hybrid form as a full-round action with a DC 15 Constitution check, or base form as a full-round action with a DC 20 check; under a visible full moon it gains +5 on checks to take monster or hybrid form and -5 on checks to return to base form, and it reverts to base form at the next sunrise or after 8 hours of rest, whichever comes first. A slain monstrous lycanthrope reverts to base form but stays dead. This is a polymorph effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.207
Curse of Lycanthropy	KEY:Curse of Lycanthropy ~ Monstrous Lycanthrope	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:One of a natural monstrous lycanthrope's natural attacks, usually a bite or claw, infects a target of generally humanoid form with lycanthropy in monster or hybrid form; a DC 15 Fortitude save negates. A victim whose size is not within one category of the lycanthrope's is unaffected.	SOURCEPAGE:p.207
Lycanthropic Empathy	KEY:Lycanthropic Empathy ~ Monstrous Lycanthrope	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A natural monstrous lycanthrope can communicate and empathize with monsters related to its monster form in any form, using Diplomacy to alter their attitude with a +4 racial bonus. An afflicted lycanthrope has this only in monster or hybrid form.	SOURCEPAGE:p.207
Monstrous Blood	KEY:Monstrous Blood ~ Monstrous Lycanthrope	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:In all forms a monstrous lycanthrope counts as both the base creature's and the base monster's type, where they differ, for spells and effects that target a specific type.	SOURCEPAGE:p.207

###Block: Moss Lich, Muck Creature, Negative-Energy Charged, Nocturnal Creature, Ofuda
Rejuvenating Seed	KEY:Rejuvenating Seed ~ Moss Lich	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:A moss lich can spend 1d10 days growing a rejuvenating seed, and after death regrows fully from it in 1d10 days. It can hold only one mature seed at a time. Destroyed again before the seed matures, it is gone for good, though its remains may give birth to one or more lesser plant creatures in 1d10 years. A spellcaster can become a moss lich deliberately by cultivating a moss patch for at least a year, fertilised weekly with its own blood (2d6 points of temporary Constitution damage) and 2,500 gp of rare components, with at least 9 ranks in both Knowledge (arcana) and Knowledge (nature); once the first seed matures it must kill itself to be reborn from the seed. A caster who fails usually becomes a ghost with aura of wild growth and the power to possess and animate nearby plants.	SOURCEPAGE:p.209
Verdant Healing	KEY:Verdant Healing ~ Moss Lich	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:In contact with moist, fertile soil a moss lich has regeneration equal to its HD, stopped by death effects and negative energy damage. An hour of such contact counts as a meal and a day's drink.	SOURCEPAGE:p.209
Slam	KEY:Moss Lich ~ Slam	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A moss lich gains a slam attack if the base creature had none, dealing damage for its size. Its natural attacks count as magic weapons.	SOURCEPAGE:p.210
Entrap	KEY:Entrap ~ Moss Lich	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A living creature struck by the moss lich's slam is infected with magical spores that grow at once into a tangle of vines covering it, acting as the entrap universal ability with permanent duration, hardness 5 and 2 hit points per HD of the moss lich. The vines die to any effect that kills plants.	SOURCEPAGE:p.210
Moss Shape	KEY:Moss Shape ~ Moss Lich	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:At will, as a standard action, a moss lich can turn into a patch of moss of its own size, or meld with an existing patch at least that large, as the tree shape spell.	SOURCEPAGE:p.210
Aura of Wild Growth	KEY:Aura of Wild Growth ~ Moss Lich	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:Plants within one mile of a moss lich grow twice as fast but yield half the normal crop, as weeds and wild plants overrun the fields and orchards.	SOURCEPAGE:p.210
Moss Magic	KEY:Moss Magic ~ Moss Lich	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A moss lich gains a +1 bonus on caster level checks in areas of thick vegetation, and any spell that lets it use or affect trees also lets it use or affect a patch of moss covering at least one square.	SOURCEPAGE:p.210
Verdant Stride	KEY:Verdant Stride ~ Moss Lich	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A moss lich passes through natural vegetation of any kind without leaving a trace and ignores vegetation-based difficult terrain, mundane or magical. It may selectively ignore any plant-based effect it created.	SOURCEPAGE:p.210
Muck Grab	KEY:Muck Grab ~ Muck Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:All of a muck creature's natural melee attacks gain the grab universal monster ability. It also gains a climb and a swim speed equal to half its highest speed, keeping an existing one if it is faster.	SOURCEPAGE:p.211
Earth Mastery	KEY:Earth Mastery ~ Muck Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A muck creature gains a +1 morale bonus on attack and damage rolls while touching earth, and takes a -4 morale penalty when attacking an airborne creature or attacking while airborne.	SOURCEPAGE:p.211
Water Mastery	KEY:Water Mastery ~ Muck Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A muck creature gains a +1 morale bonus on attack and damage rolls while touching water.	SOURCEPAGE:p.212
Exude Muck	KEY:Exude Muck ~ Muck Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a full-round action, a muck creature exudes a 10-foot-radius spread of slippery muck that stays until washed away and otherwise works as a grease spell, with a Constitution-based save DC. Creatures with the earth or water subtypes are immune.	SOURCEPAGE:p.211
Mudball	KEY:Mudball ~ Muck Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A muck creature can hurl a mudball as a ranged touch attack with a 20-foot range increment, dealing nonlethal damage as a slam of its size and coating the target in slippery sludge that affects its equipment as a grease spell and grants it fire resistance 3. The coating lasts 1 minute or until washed off with at least 10 gallons of water. Creatures with the water subtype are immune.	SOURCEPAGE:p.211
Smother	KEY:Smother ~ Muck Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:On a successful grapple check, a muck creature fills its opponent's mouth and nose with noxious muck. The victim must hold its breath or begin drowning, and cannot speak or cast spells with verbal components. Each round it cannot breathe it must make a Fortitude save or be nauseated until 1d4 rounds after the muck is cleared. Clearing the muck is a move action that provokes attacks of opportunity and requires a Constitution check at the same DC; it can be attempted while grappled. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.212
Air Breather	KEY:Air Breather ~ Muck Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A muck creature can breathe air even if the base creature breathed only water.	SOURCEPAGE:p.212
Lifesense	KEY:Lifesense ~ Negative-Energy Charged	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Vision	DESC:The creature gains lifesense 60 ft. if it did not already have it. This awareness is supernatural: it works inside a silence spell and is not negated by blindness.	SOURCEPAGE:p.213
Obscuring Energy	KEY:Obscuring Energy ~ Negative-Energy Charged	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:Flickering shadows and wisps of black smoke surround the creature, granting concealment (20%% miss chance). While it stands still the shadows deepen into total concealment (50%% miss chance). It also gains positive energy resistance 10.	SOURCEPAGE:p.213
Strong Resistance	KEY:Strong Resistance ~ Negative-Energy Charged	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:If a single attack of positive energy, such as a cleric's channel, would destroy the creature, it gets a Will save at a DC equal to that damage to halve it. Against any other effect that would banish or destroy it outright it gets a Will save even where none is normally allowed, or two saves and the better result where one is, and on a success the effect fails. This also applies to weaknesses that can destroy it, such as a wight's resurrection vulnerability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.213
Negative Strikes	KEY:Negative Strikes ~ Negative-Energy Charged	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Each of the creature's natural attacks, touch attacks, incorporeal touches and weapon attacks deals an extra 1d6 negative energy damage, and its natural weapons and any weapon it wields count as evil-aligned for overcoming damage reduction. It also gains energy drain (+1 level); a creature gaining energy drain from this template applies it to one natural attack chosen once and for all.	SOURCEPAGE:p.213
Searing Darkness	KEY:Searing Darkness ~ Negative-Energy Charged	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:As a standard action, the creature blasts a dark ray of negative energy as a ranged touch attack with a range of 100 ft. + 10 ft. per racial HD, dealing 1d8 negative energy damage per 2 total HD, to a maximum of 10d8, and healing undead twice that. It can use this once per day plus once more per 5 racial HD, including on itself to heal. This is a negative energy effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.214
Nocturnal Sight	KEY:Nocturnal Sight ~ Nocturnal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Vision	DESC:A nocturnal creature gains low-light vision, or darkvision 60 ft. if it already had low-light vision.	SOURCEPAGE:p.215
Light Sensitivity	KEY:Light Sensitivity ~ Nocturnal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A nocturnal creature is dazzled while it remains in an area of bright light, and takes a -4 circumstance penalty on Perception checks there.	SOURCEPAGE:p.215
Paper Body	KEY:Paper Body ~ Ofuda	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An ofuda's body of paper and ink weighs an eighth of the base creature's and is so buoyant it cannot enter water unless forcibly submerged. Its natural armor is halved, minimum +1, and it gets only half the normal hit points per Hit Die. It walks on water at half its fastest movement rate. It loses every defense, weakness and special quality of the base creature, along with all ranks and bonuses in Craft, Knowledge and Profession, which are reassigned to other skills.	SOURCEPAGE:p.216
Constructed	KEY:Constructed ~ Ofuda	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:For effects that target creatures by type, such as a ranger's favored enemy or a bane weapon, an ofuda counts as both an outsider and a construct. It gains a +4 racial bonus on all saving throws against mind-affecting effects, paralysis, poison and stun effects, and is immune to fatigue, exhaustion, disease and sleep. It can never gain morale bonuses and is immune to fear and emotion effects. It neither eats nor sleeps.	SOURCEPAGE:p.216
Limited Fire Immunity	KEY:Limited Fire Immunity ~ Ofuda	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:An ofuda is immune to its own fire-based abilities and effects, but not to those of other ofuda.	SOURCEPAGE:p.216
Vulnerability to Fire	KEY:Vulnerability to Fire ~ Ofuda	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:An ofuda takes half again as much damage (+50%%) from fire, regardless of whether a saving throw is allowed or whether the save succeeds.	SOURCEPAGE:p.216
Submersion Vulnerability	KEY:Submersion Vulnerability ~ Ofuda	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:An ofuda submerged in water takes a third of its maximum hit points in damage each round.	SOURCEPAGE:p.216
Deliberate	KEY:Deliberate ~ Ofuda	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:An ofuda moves slowly and methodically and can take only a single move action or standard action each round. It may move up to its base speed and make one attack in the same round as a charge, but can never pounce or make a full attack.	SOURCEPAGE:p.216
Empty Ego	KEY:Empty Ego ~ Ofuda	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:An ofuda is entirely without drive or passion. It obeys its summoner or creator as well as it can but never acts towards any other goal, and it loses all Craft, Knowledge and Profession skills.	SOURCEPAGE:p.217

###Block: Ooze Creature, Plague Bearer
Transparent	KEY:Transparent ~ Ooze Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:An ooze creature lacks the base creature's coloration, so a DC 15 Perception check is needed to notice it while it is motionless. It gains acid immunity and all other ooze traits, though an ooze creature with an Intelligence score does not gain immunity to mind-affecting effects, and it loses the base creature's natural armor.	SOURCEPAGE:p.218
Acid	KEY:Acid ~ Ooze Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Each of an ooze creature's natural attacks deals acid damage by size: Fine 1, Diminutive 1d2, Tiny 1d3, Small 1d4, Medium 1d6, Large 1d8, Huge 2d6, Gargantuan 2d8, Colossal 4d6. The acid harms organic material and metal but not stone. A creature grappling the ooze automatically takes that damage each round the grapple lasts, on top of any grapple damage. Clothing and armor take the same damage as the wearer unless a Reflex save prevents it, and a metal or wooden weapon that strikes the ooze takes the damage unless its wielder makes a Reflex save. A metal or wooden object in contact with the ooze for more than 1 round takes the ooze's total Hit Dice in acid damage with no save. The save DCs are Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.218
Ooze Strikes	KEY:Ooze Strikes ~ Ooze Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:All of an ooze creature's natural attacks gain grab, and a creature with no natural attacks gains a primary slam dealing damage for its size. It keeps its weapon and armor proficiencies, though its acidic touch makes manufactured gear a temporary arrangement at best.	SOURCEPAGE:p.218
Bilious Globule	KEY:Bilious Globule ~ Ooze Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:An ooze creature can hurl a glob of acid as a ranged touch attack, a thrown weapon with a 20-foot range increment, dealing its size's acid damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.218
Exude Ooze	KEY:Exude Ooze ~ Ooze Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:At will, as a full-round action, an ooze creature exudes a spread of slippery ooze centred on itself, sized and lasting by its own size: Fine one 5-ft. square for 2 rounds, Diminutive one 5 ft. square for 3 rounds, Tiny one 5 ft. square for 5 rounds, Small 5 ft. for 6 rounds, Medium 5 ft. for 6 rounds, Large 10 ft. for 12 rounds, Huge 10 ft. for 18 rounds, Gargantuan 15 ft. for 30 rounds, Colossal 20 ft. for 60 rounds. Any creature moving into, through or out of the area must succeed on a DC 15 Acrobatics check or fall prone, and each round in contact with the puddle it takes the ooze's acid damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.219
Create Spawn	KEY:Create Spawn ~ Ooze Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A living creature reduced to 0 or fewer hit points and lying prone in an ooze creature's exuded ooze makes stabilization checks normally, but on a failed check it turns at once into an ooze, gaining this template instead of losing a hit point. The new ooze creature rises the following round with average hit points for its character level, controlled as by dominate monster by the creature that exuded the ooze. The acid usually kills first, so this is rare and largely a matter of chance.	SOURCEPAGE:p.219
Remembered Abilities	KEY:Remembered Abilities ~ Ooze Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An ooze creature recalls the skills and abilities it had in life but not its personality or feelings. Every ooze creature has Intelligence 1 or higher and, poor strategist though it may be, can use its former self's abilities and attacks unless the template makes them impossible. It keeps its bonus feats, and any feat whose prerequisites it no longer meets becomes a bonus feat too.	SOURCEPAGE:p.219
Sluggish	KEY:Sluggish ~ Ooze Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:Each of an ooze creature's speeds falls to half the base creature's, and a fly speed becomes clumsy if it was not already.	SOURCEPAGE:p.218
Disease Cloud	KEY:Disease Cloud ~ Plague Bearer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.Aura	DESC:An invisible cloud of contagion surrounds the plague bearer. Every breathing creature within 30 ft. must make two Fortitude saves or contract two diseases, typically bubonic plague and mindfire, whose type becomes inhaled. The save DCs are Constitution-based, or Charisma-based for an undead plague bearer.	SOURCEPAGE:p.220
Total Disease Immunity	KEY:Total Disease Immunity ~ Plague Bearer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A plague bearer is immune to all diseases, including magical diseases and those brought on by curses.	SOURCEPAGE:p.220
Disease	KEY:Disease ~ Plague Bearer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:All of a plague bearer's natural melee attacks spread disease: a creature it hits must succeed on a Fortitude save or contract two diseases, typically filth fever and leprosy, of the injury type. A plague bearer with no natural melee attack spreads them with a melee touch attack, and the diseases are then contact type. The save DCs are Constitution-based, or Charisma-based for an undead plague bearer.	SOURCEPAGE:p.221
Carrier	KEY:Carrier ~ Plague Bearer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Though immune to their effects, a plague bearer still carries its infections and goes on doing so regardless of magical healing or successful Fortitude saves.	SOURCEPAGE:p.221
Diseased Flesh	KEY:Diseased Flesh ~ Plague Bearer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:A plague bearer carries a single disease in its body, usually blinding sickness. Any creature that bites it, swallows it whole or otherwise eats its flesh must succeed on a Fortitude save or contract that disease, whose type becomes ingested. The save DC is Constitution-based, or Charisma-based for an undead plague bearer.	SOURCEPAGE:p.221
Quick Incubation	KEY:Quick Incubation ~ Plague Bearer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Every disease a plague bearer carries has an onset time of instantaneous: the first effects appear immediately.	SOURCEPAGE:p.221

###Block: Plantblood, Poisonous Creature
Plant Flesh	KEY:Plant Flesh ~ Plantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:Much of a plantblood's internal anatomy is vegetable matter. Whenever a sneak attack, critical hit or other precision damage is scored against it, there is a 50%% chance the extra damage is negated and the damage is rolled normally.	SOURCEPAGE:p.222
Plant Feeding	KEY:Plant Feeding ~ Plantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A plantblood that spends at least 4 hours in direct sunlight need not eat that day.	SOURCEPAGE:p.222
Plantblood	KEY:Plantblood ~ Plant Nature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A plantblood counts as both a plant and the base creature's type for spells and effects that target plants, and can use magic items whose powers work only for plant creatures. It also gains a +4 bonus on saving throws against poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning, polymorphing and mind-affecting effects. A plantblood reduced to Dexterity 0 has grown roots and cannot move. Variant, plantblood plague: some plantbloods spread the template as a disease -- contact, injury or inhaled; save Fort DC 15; onset 1 day; frequency 1/day; effect the victim gains the plantblood template over 5 days; cure 2 consecutive saves, a single save postponing the effect one more day. A plantblood that spreads the template by an attack has its CR adjustment raised by +1.	SOURCEPAGE:p.222
Hive Mind	KEY:Hive Mind ~ Plantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Each podling plantblood is in constant communication with every other within 1 mile. Podlings within sight of one another cannot be caught flat-footed or flanked unless all of them are.	SOURCEPAGE:p.223
Implant	KEY:Implant ~ Plantblood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Once per day, as a full-round action, a podling plantblood can implant a seed in a helpless foe. If the victim qualifies for the plantblood template, the seed grows over 30 days, gradually taking over its organs, until it becomes a plantblood and its alignment shifts to neutral evil.	SOURCEPAGE:p.223
Detect Poison	KEY:Detect Poison ~ Poisonous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Vision	DESC:As the detect poison spell, but with a fixed range of 30 ft.	SOURCEPAGE:p.224
Detect Anti-Poison	KEY:Detect Anti-Poison ~ Poisonous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Vision	DESC:As detect poison, but it detects alchemical items, magic effects and magic items within 30 feet that neutralize or delay poisons, and tells whether a creature in that range is naturally immune or resistant to poison.	SOURCEPAGE:p.224
Poisonous Cloud	KEY:Poisonous Cloud ~ Poisonous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.Aura	DESC:An invisible cloud of poisonous gas always surrounds the creature, affecting anything that breathes the air or water within 10 feet. Poison cloud--inhaled; save Fortitude; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d3 Str plus sickened for 1 hour; cure 2 saves. A successful save shortens the sickened condition to 1 minute. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.224
Toxic Flesh	KEY:Toxic Flesh ~ Poisonous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:The creature's flesh exudes a contact poison delivered by any physical contact it makes. The poison loses its potency once removed from the creature, so it cannot be placed on objects, and anything that eats the creature's flesh or swallows it whole suffers as though it had touched it. Toxin--contact or ingested; save Fortitude; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d2 Dex and nauseated; cure 2 consecutive saves. Ingested, the frequency becomes 1/minute for 6 minutes with an onset of 1 minute. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.224
Venom	KEY:Venom ~ Poisonous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Each of the creature's natural attacks that deals slashing or piercing damage delivers both its toxin and its venom; bludgeoning natural attacks deliver only the toxin. Venom--injury; save Fortitude; frequency 1/round for 4 rounds; effect 1d2 Con; cure 1 save. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.225
Poisonous Breath	KEY:Poisonous Breath ~ Poisonous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Once every 1d4 rounds, as a standard action, the creature sprays a disorienting contact poison in a 60-ft. cone; each creature in the area must succeed on a Reflex save to avoid the spray. Poison breath--contact; save Fortitude; onset 1 minute; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d4 Int and 1d4 Wis damage and confusion; cure 1 save. A successful save halves the ability damage and negates the confusion. Both save DCs are Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.225
Poison Item	KEY:Poison Item ~ Poisonous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:As a swift action, a poisonous creature can coat any manufactured weapon or object, including magic items, with a single dose of poison drawn from its own saliva, sweat or blood. The poison is identical to the venom on its natural attacks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.225
Virulent Poisons	KEY:Virulent Poisons ~ Poisonous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A poisonous creature's poisons, toxins and venoms resist treatment: the DC of Heal checks to treat them rises by 5, and spells such as delay poison and neutralize poison must be cast twice in a row to work against them.	SOURCEPAGE:p.225

###Block: Positive-Energy Charged, Primitive, Prismatic
Positive Blindsight	KEY:Positive Blindsight ~ Positive-Energy Charged	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Vision	DESC:The creature gains blindsight +60 ft. This awareness is supernatural: it works inside a silence spell and is not negated by blindness.	SOURCEPAGE:p.226
Positive Energy Aura	KEY:Positive Energy Aura ~ Positive-Energy Charged	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:The creature emits a 5-ft. radius aura of bright positive energy that deals 1d6 positive energy damage to undead and heals 1d6 damage to living creatures in range, and lights a 15 ft. radius as bright light.	SOURCEPAGE:p.226
Negative Energy Immunity	KEY:Negative Energy Immunity ~ Positive-Energy Charged	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:The creature is immune to negative energy, which also means it can never be healed. Positive energy effects still damage it, though its fast healing usually erases the damage at once. Existing channel resistance drops by 1, minimum +0, and it loses every weakness tied to positive energy, including damage or penalties in bright light or daylight.	SOURCEPAGE:p.226
Resistance to Control	KEY:Resistance to Control ~ Positive-Energy Charged	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:Against any effect that would command, dominate or otherwise control it, the creature gets two saving throws and takes the better result, or a Will save to negate where none is normally allowed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.226
Positive Strikes	KEY:Positive Strikes ~ Positive-Energy Charged	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Each of the base creature's natural attacks deals positive energy damage instead of its normal physical damage, which can grant temporary hit points through overcharge; other kinds of energy damage are unchanged. Every special attack that dealt negative energy damage, such as channel energy, now deals positive energy.	SOURCEPAGE:p.226
Energy Infusion	KEY:Energy Infusion ~ Positive-Energy Charged	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:The creature's energy drain becomes energy infusion, filling a target with positive energy instead of draining levels. For each level the base creature's energy drain would have removed, the infusion deals the target's total Hit Dice multiplied by its Constitution modifier, or Charisma if undead, in positive energy damage. A Will save resists, even where the original effect allowed none. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.227
Overcharge	KEY:Overcharge ~ Positive-Energy Charged	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:All the creature's positive energy effects heal living creatures, and healing beyond full hit points becomes temporary hit points lasting 24 hours or until lost to damage. If a creature's accumulated temporary hit points exceed its maximum hit point total it explodes in a burst of positive energy and dies instantly, as disintegrate with no save. The burst deals 1d6 damage plus 1d6 per 10 temporary hit points it carried, in a 5 ft. radius plus 5 ft. per 5 HD of the overcharged creature. That damage can heal and further charge living creatures in range, so one burst can set off others in a chain reaction.	SOURCEPAGE:p.227
Transform Undead	KEY:Transform Undead ~ Positive-Energy Charged	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:When an undead creature of no more HD than the positive-energy charged creature is destroyed by it, that creature immediately becomes another positive-energy charged creature at its original full hit points, staggered for the first 1d4 rounds and not under its maker's control.	SOURCEPAGE:p.227
Constant Agony	KEY:Constant Agony ~ Positive-Energy Charged	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:The creature loses all spellcasting, though it keeps the base creature's spell-like abilities, and loses the summon ability. Its constant agony gives it a -20 penalty on concentration checks, and spell-like abilities that used Intelligence now use Charisma. It has no Intelligence score and is mindless, and a creature reduced to Wisdom 0 is insane. It keeps its racial skill bonuses but loses all skill ranks, and loses every feat but its bonus feats. It cannot speak and loses any telepathy.	SOURCEPAGE:p.228
Primitive Slam	KEY:Primitive Slam ~ Primitive	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A primitive with no other natural attacks gains a primary slam attack dealing damage as a creature one size category larger. It loses all the base creature's skill ranks and repurchases them for its racial Hit Dice, treating Climb, Perception, Stealth and Survival as class skills, while keeping racial skill bonuses and any ranks from class levels.	SOURCEPAGE:p.229
Prismatic Body	KEY:Prismatic Body ~ Prismatic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:A prismatic's body glows like a candle, lighting a 5-foot radius, and the hue changes at random each round. While lit it gains no concealment from darkness or shadow. Once per round, as a free action with a DC 15 concentration check, it can suppress the light or choose its colour; the random shifting resumes on its next turn unless it makes another DC 15 check, and restoring a suppressed light is a free action. While the light is suppressed it gains none of the immunities from its prismatic body. Variant, prismatic curse: a creature that survives exposure to one of the prismatic spells may be cursed with this template -- curse; save Fortitude at the DC of the prismatic spell; onset immediate; effect the creature gains the prismatic template. Such a prismatic takes a -4 penalty to Wisdom, cannot suppress its light, and may need rare magic or an artifact to be cured.	SOURCEPAGE:p.230
Prismatic Immunities	KEY:Prismatic Immunities ~ Prismatic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:The hue of the prismatic's light grants an immunity, rolled at the end of each round on 1d8: 1 red, fire; 2 orange, acid; 3 yellow, electricity; 4 green, poison; 5 blue, mind-affecting effects; 6 indigo, cold; 7 violet, sonic; 8 two colours, roll twice rerolling any 8.	SOURCEPAGE:p.230
Prismatic Light	KEY:Prismatic Light ~ Prismatic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A prismatic is immune to the adverse effects of spells with the light descriptor and of its own spell-like abilities, and to all blinding, dazzling and dazing effects caused by light. A base creature that suffered in bright light loses that vulnerability. Its spell-like abilities accumulate with its Hit Dice: 1-2 3/day dancing lights; 3-4 at will flare and 2/day color spray; 5-6 1/day hypnotic pattern; 7-8 1/day daylight; 9-10 1/day searing light; 11-12 1/day rainbow pattern; 13-14 1/day prismatic spray; 15-16 1/day scintillating pattern; 17-18 1/day prismatic wall; 19-20+ 1/day prismatic sphere. The caster level is its character level and the save DCs are Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.230

###Block: Psychic
Psychic Focus	KEY:Psychic Focus ~ Psychic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A psychic has one or more of eight focuses, and gains the abilities of each of them: a clairaudient hears sounds made elsewhere and has power over sound; a clairvoyant sees distant events and has power over sight; an empath feels others' emotions and has power over them; a precognizant sees the future and knows how to act on it; a psychometer reads the history and qualities of an object or place by concentrating; a pyrokinetic makes and controls flame with a thought; a telekinetic moves objects and produces force effects with its mind; and a telepath reads and projects thoughts. Each focus adds its own CR increase: clairaudient, clairvoyant and empath +0 up to 10 HD and +1 at 11 or more; precognizant and telepath +1; pyrokinetic and telekinetic +1 up to 10 HD and +2 at 11 or more; psychometer +0. Its caster level is its total Hit Dice and the save DCs are Charisma-based. To take more than one focus, apply each focus template in turn.	SOURCEPAGE:p.232
Clairaudience	KEY:Clairaudience ~ Psychic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A clairaudient gains a +10 racial bonus on Perception checks to listen. A psychic with both this focus and clairvoyance simply has a +10 racial bonus on Perception.	SOURCEPAGE:p.234
Clairvoyance	KEY:Clairvoyance ~ Psychic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A clairvoyant gains a +10 racial bonus on Perception checks to spot. A psychic with both this focus and clairaudience simply has a +10 racial bonus on Perception.	SOURCEPAGE:p.234
Empathy	KEY:Empathy ~ Psychic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:An empath gains a +10 racial bonus on Sense Motive checks and a +5 racial bonus on Bluff, Diplomacy and Intimidate.	SOURCEPAGE:p.234
Foresight	KEY:Foresight ~ Psychic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:A precognizant is constantly under a foresight effect at a caster level equal to its character level, receiving instant warning of danger and a general idea of how to protect itself. It is never surprised or flat-footed and gains a +2 insight bonus to AC and on Reflex saves, lost whenever it would be denied its Dexterity bonus to AC. It also gains a +8 insight bonus on Initiative rolls.	SOURCEPAGE:p.233
Psychometry	KEY:Psychometry ~ Psychic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A psychometer gains a +5 racial bonus on Appraise, Disable Device, Perception and Use Magic Device, and on Survival checks made to track. It must touch a single object or creature to use its at-will abilities, which otherwise work as the spells.	SOURCEPAGE:p.235
Conscious Immunity to Fire	KEY:Conscious Immunity to Fire ~ Psychic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Immunity	DESC:While it is conscious, a pyrokinetic is immune to fire.	SOURCEPAGE:p.233
Telekinetic Flight	KEY:Telekinetic Flight ~ Psychic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A telekinetic gains a +4 deflection bonus to AC, keeps the base creature's speeds and gains a fly speed equal to its highest speed with perfect maneuverability. An existing fly speed either stays or rises to its highest other speed plus 5 feet per point of Charisma bonus, whichever is faster, with perfect maneuverability. Flight gained this way is supernatural.	SOURCEPAGE:p.233
Informed Prediction	KEY:Informed Prediction ~ Psychic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:If a telepath has successfully used detect thoughts on a creature within the last 24 hours, it gains a +2 dodge bonus against that creature's attacks and a +2 insight bonus on saves against its spells and special attacks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.233
Telepathy	KEY:Telepathy ~ Psychic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A telepath gains telepathy 100 ft. as a supernatural ability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.234

###Block: Qlippoth-Blighted, Quadrupedal Creature
Sin Sense	KEY:Sin Sense ~ Qlippoth-Blighted	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Vision	DESC:A qlippoth-blighted can sniff out any creature carrying its attuned sin within 100 ft. While it senses its quarry the wounds and tumors on its body weep more freely as it is driven to hunt the source down. The ability otherwise works as detect evil with the creature already studied for three rounds.	SOURCEPAGE:p.236
Sin Attunement	KEY:Sin Attunement ~ Qlippoth-Blighted	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A qlippoth-blighted is attuned at its creation to a single sin, usually one of the seven deadly sins -- envy, gluttony, greed, lust, pride, sloth and wrath -- though others such as suicide, destruction, desertion or murder are possible, provided some specific demon represents that sin. Against creatures carrying that sin it gains a +2 bonus on all saves, skill checks, attack and damage rolls, and a +2 circumstance bonus to AC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.237
Sin Resistance	KEY:Sin Resistance ~ Qlippoth-Blighted	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:A creature carrying the qlippoth-blighted's attuned sin has a 20%% miss chance against it with any attack or effect. This is not concealment and does not stack with blur or displacement; only the best miss chance applies. Against such a creature the qlippoth-blighted may also reroll any one save or skill check per round made in reaction to its target, and must take the second result.	SOURCEPAGE:p.236
Sin Strike	KEY:Sin Strike ~ Qlippoth-Blighted	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Against a creature carrying its attuned sin, the qlippoth-blighted's critical threat range is doubled and every critical is automatically confirmed. Unlike other threat-range effects, sin strike stacks with them.	SOURCEPAGE:p.237
Kill the Sinful	KEY:Kill the Sinful ~ Qlippoth-Blighted	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A qlippoth-blighted can make a destructive strike against a creature carrying its attuned sin. The strike must be declared before the attack roll; on a hit the target must make a Fortitude save or drop to -1 hit points and start dying, and on a miss the attempt is spent. Usable a number of times per day equal to its Charisma modifier, minimum 1. This is a death effect; the Charisma-based save DC uses its total HD and gains a +2 racial bonus.	SOURCEPAGE:p.236
Sin Consumption	KEY:Sin Consumption ~ Qlippoth-Blighted	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:On killing a creature with the appropriate sin, the qlippoth-blighted siphons that sin from the departing soul as a free action, gaining +4 to one ability score of its choice, or +6 if the creature was a demon representing that sin, which is then utterly destroyed. The bonus lasts until the next such kill, when it may be kept or moved to another score, and only one score can carry it at a time.	SOURCEPAGE:p.237
Sinful Compulsion	KEY:Sinful Compulsion ~ Qlippoth-Blighted	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Weakness	DESC:When the qlippoth-blighted senses a creature carrying its attuned sin, it is compelled to find and kill it. Until it finds its quarry and attacks, its wounds tear wider and it is sickened. The compulsion affects creatures normally immune to compulsions or to the sickened condition; a DC 25 Will save resists both the compulsion and the sickening.	SOURCEPAGE:p.236
Vulnerability to Virtue	KEY:Vulnerability to Virtue ~ Qlippoth-Blighted	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A qlippoth-blighted takes 50%% more damage from holy or sacred damage and from effects with the good descriptor.	SOURCEPAGE:p.236
Vile Death	KEY:Vile Death ~ Qlippoth-Blighted	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:When a qlippoth-blighted dies, its soul is destroyed along with all the sin it carried, and its remains dissolve into a pool of rotten flesh and putrid fluid that acts as the centre of an unhallow spell at a caster level equal to its total Hit Dice. The body evaporates entirely after 1d10 rounds, taking the unhallow with it. Because body and soul are both gone, only true resurrection, miracle or wish can restore the base creature, and a demon destroyed this way is beyond any magic short of divine intervention.	SOURCEPAGE:p.237
Quadrupedal Body	KEY:Quadrupedal Body ~ Quadrupedal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The base creature's arms become legs and its hands hooves or paws, depending on whether its lower body resembles a horse or a lion. It must wear barding rather than armor and cannot wear boots made for bipeds. Without hands it cannot use weapons or a shield or manipulate objects better than a bear or horse could, and it loses all weapon and armor proficiencies unless it regularly gains a form with hands, in which case its class or type proficiencies return without needing feats. Its land and burrow speeds each rise by 10 feet; an existing climb speed becomes half its new land speed or 10 feet, whichever is faster; and a wing-borne fly speed drops one maneuverability step, to a minimum of clumsy. Its space and reach suit its new shape: Fine 1/2 ft., Diminutive 1 ft., Tiny 2-1/2 ft., all with no reach; Small and Medium 5 ft./5 ft.; Large 10 ft./5 ft.; Huge 15 ft./10 ft.; Gargantuan 20 ft./15 ft.; Colossal 30 ft./20 ft.; greater-than-normal reach adds 5 feet. It gains +4 CMD against trip attempts, and loses every feat, skill, special attack and special quality that needs fine manipulation, while any ability that required a humanoid form now requires a quadrupedal one.	SOURCEPAGE:p.238
Quadrupedal Attacks	KEY:Quadrupedal Attacks ~ Quadrupedal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:The creature keeps all the base creature's attacks with their primary or secondary status. A base creature with a single claw or slam gains a second attack of the same kind, status and base damage. A head with no bite attack gains a secondary bite, and an arm with no claw or slam gains a primary slam. Attacks granted by the template deal damage for the creature's size. A creature that can still use weapons and has free hands gains the undersized weapons ability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.238
Beast of Burden	KEY:Beast of Burden ~ Quadrupedal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Quadrupeds carry heavier loads than bipeds. Multiply the carrying capacity for the creature's Strength by its size: Fine x1/4, Diminutive x1/2, Tiny x3/4, Small x1, Medium x1-1/2, Large x3, Huge x6, Gargantuan x12, Colossal x24.	SOURCEPAGE:p.240

###Block: Quickling, Ravenous Creature, Rawboned, Saurian, Savant
Rapid Actions	KEY:Rapid Actions ~ Quickling	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A quickling gains one extra attack or move action each round. This does not stack with other haste effects. Each of its speeds is quadrupled, and a fly speed's maneuverability rises two categories, to a maximum of perfect. Appendix C on page 308 lists the quickling at +1 CR; this template follows its own entry on page 241, which says +3.	SOURCEPAGE:p.241
Quickling Casting	KEY:Quickling Casting ~ Quickling	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A quickling casts any spell or spell-like ability with a casting time of 1 round or less as a swift action. Longer casting times drop to 1 round and take an attack action. This cannot be combined with Quicken Spell or Quicken Spell-Like Ability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.241
Rapid Aging	KEY:Rapid Aging ~ Quickling	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A quickling ages 4 years for every year that passes.	SOURCEPAGE:p.241
Aging Vulnerability	KEY:Aging Vulnerability ~ Quickling	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A quickling takes 50%% more damage from aging effects, including the number of years aged.	SOURCEPAGE:p.241
Cannibalistic Healing	KEY:Cannibalistic Healing ~ Ravenous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:So long as it has fed on the flesh of its own kind within the last 24 hours, a ravenous creature has fast healing 10. Feeding on one of its own kind killed within the last hour heals all its ability damage and ability drain. Its kind means creatures of the same named species, the same broad category, or the same racial subtype, and creatures sharing a species' blood count too: a ravenous drow's kind covers drow, elves and half-elves, and a ravenous efreeti's kind covers all genies but not other fire elementals.	SOURCEPAGE:p.242
Ravenous Bite	KEY:Ravenous Bite ~ Ravenous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A ravenous creature with at least one mouth and no natural attack with it gains a secondary bite per mouth, dealing damage as a creature two size categories larger. An existing bite attack's damage rises by two steps.	SOURCEPAGE:p.242
Favored Prey	KEY:Favored Prey ~ Ravenous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A ravenous creature gains a +2 bonus on damage rolls against creatures of its own type and on Bluff, Perception, Sense Motive and Survival checks concerning them, rising to +4 against creatures of its own kind.	SOURCEPAGE:p.242
Hungry Frenzy	KEY:Hungry Frenzy ~ Ravenous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A number of rounds per day equal to its Charisma modifier, minimum 1, a ravenous creature can enter a rage identical to a barbarian's, but only against creatures of its own kind. While starving, the rage's bonuses and penalties double and it cannot end the rage at will until it has eaten enough to clear the nonlethal damage from starvation. A ravenous creature that already rages adds its Charisma modifier, minimum +0, to its daily rounds of rage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.242
Hungry Special Attacks	KEY:Hungry Special Attacks ~ Ravenous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Any creature of the ravenous creature's own kind takes a -2 penalty on saving throws against its spells and special attacks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.243
Ageless	KEY:Ageless ~ Ravenous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A ravenous creature does not age while it is not starving.	SOURCEPAGE:p.243
Sprint	KEY:Sprint ~ Ravenous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Once per hour, a ravenous creature can move at ten times its normal speed when it charges.	SOURCEPAGE:p.243
Ravenous Body	KEY:Ravenous Body ~ Ravenous Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A ravenous creature can eat other food, but only the flesh of its own kind satisfies its hunger. It must feed on its own kind at least once every three days or suffer starvation, and it dies when the nonlethal damage from starvation equals its Constitution score.	SOURCEPAGE:p.242
Warped Frame	KEY:Warped Frame ~ Rawboned	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A rawboned gains 2 additional racial Hit Dice of the die size appropriate to its type; PCGen cannot add racial HD through a template, so add them to the base race by hand. Its base land speed rises by 10 feet and each of its other movement modes by 5 feet, and its reach grows by 5 ft.	SOURCEPAGE:p.244
Rawboned Attacks	KEY:Rawboned Attacks ~ Rawboned	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A rawboned gains two claw attacks, a bite and a slam if the base creature did not have them, each dealing damage for its size.	SOURCEPAGE:p.245
Rend	KEY:Rend ~ Rawboned	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A rawboned gains rend with its bite and 2 claws if it did not already have it, dealing its bite damage raised two steps plus 1-1/2 its Strength bonus, minimum +0. An existing rend attack's damage rises by one step instead.	SOURCEPAGE:p.245
Vulnerability to Cold	KEY:Vulnerability to Cold ~ Rawboned	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A rawboned takes half again as much damage (+50%%) from cold, regardless of whether a saving throw is allowed or whether the save succeeds.	SOURCEPAGE:p.245
Saurian Attacks	KEY:Saurian Attacks ~ Saurian	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A saurian with at least one mouth and no natural attack with it gains a secondary bite per mouth, and with at least two arms and no natural attacks on them gains a primary claw per arm, each dealing damage for its size. A humanoid base creature gains the reptilian subtype.	SOURCEPAGE:p.246
Rake	KEY:Rake ~ Saurian	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A saurian gains rake with 2 claws, dealing damage equal to its claw attack.	SOURCEPAGE:p.246
Leaping Pounce	KEY:Leaping Pounce ~ Saurian	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:When a saurian charges a foe and jumps for at least the last 10 feet of its movement, it may make a full attack, including rake attacks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.246
Deductive Leap	KEY:Deductive Leap ~ Savant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:Once per round a savant may substitute its Intelligence modifier for the ability modifier a saving throw normally uses. The choice must be made before the roll, and may be made even if the savant does not know what the save is against.	SOURCEPAGE:p.247
Uncanny Dodge	KEY:Uncanny Dodge ~ Savant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:As the rogue ability. A savant that already has uncanny dodge from a class level or another template gains improved uncanny dodge instead.	SOURCEPAGE:p.247
Combat Insight	KEY:Combat Insight ~ Savant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Against any creature it has watched fight for at least 3 rounds, a savant gains a +2 insight bonus to AC and on attack and damage rolls.	SOURCEPAGE:p.247
Savant Insight	KEY:Savant Insight ~ Savant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A savant gains a +6 insight bonus on Bluff, Diplomacy, Intimidate and Sense Motive checks against creatures it has observed or dealt with for 1 minute, and can use all Knowledge skills, Disable Device, Linguistics and Use Magic Device untrained. It keeps the base creature's racial skill bonuses but loses all skill ranks, repurchasing them for its racial Hit Dice with those skills and the base creature's as class skills, and keeps any ranks from class levels.	SOURCEPAGE:p.248
Home Advantage	KEY:Home Advantage ~ Savant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:In any area it knows very well, a place where it feels at home, a savant gains a +4 insight bonus on initiative rolls and on Perception and Stealth checks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.248
Skill Mastery	KEY:Skill Mastery ~ Savant	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A savant chooses ten skills when the template is applied and may take 10 on checks with any of them, even when stress or distraction would normally prevent it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.248

###Block: Scalding Creature, Seasonal Creature, Seelie Creature, Selenic Creature
Cloud Sight	KEY:Cloud Sight ~ Scalding Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Vision	DESC:A scalding creature sees through clouds, gases, fogs, mists and smoke as though they did not hinder vision, so nothing gains concealment from them against it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.249
Steam Body	KEY:Steam Body ~ Scalding Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:The steam and vapour of a scalding creature's body make it hard to hit, granting it concealment at all times (20%% miss chance). It also gains a fly speed equal to its fastest speed with perfect maneuverability, or perfect maneuverability on an existing fly speed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.249
Breath Weapon	KEY:Breath Weapon ~ Scalding Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once every 1d4 rounds a scalding creature breathes a cloud of superheated steam, either as a 60 ft. line dealing 1d6 fire damage per Hit Die of the base creature, to a maximum of 20d6 with a Reflex save for half, or as a 10 ft. radius spread centred on itself dealing 1d6 fire damage per 2 Hit Dice, to a maximum of 10d6, with no save. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.249
Scalding Form	KEY:Scalding Form ~ Scalding Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:While in steam form a scalding creature can burn creatures within its cloud as an incendiary cloud spell, dealing 1d6 damage per 2 Hit Dice of the base creature each round, halved on a successful Reflex save; half of the damage is fire and half untyped whether or not the save succeeds. It can hold scalding form for a number of rounds equal to its Constitution modifier, minimum 1, moving at its fly speed, and can use the ability 1 + 1 per 5 HD times per day. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.249
Scalding Touch	KEY:Scalding Touch ~ Scalding Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A scalding creature gains a touch attack dealing an extra 1d4 fire damage, and each of its natural attacks deals that damage too. The damage scales with size.	SOURCEPAGE:p.250
Steam Form	KEY:Steam Form ~ Scalding Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A scalding creature can take the form of a cloud of steam at will, as the gaseous form spell. Becoming gaseous or returning to its normal form is a move action.	SOURCEPAGE:p.250
Turning of the Year	KEY:Turning of the Year ~ Seasonal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A seasonal creature's body and soul follow the turning year. When the season changes it loses the previous season's changes and gains the next one's. Its ability scores shift by season: spring Str +4, Dex +4, Con -4, Int -4, Wis -4, Cha +4; summer the same at +2 and -2; autumn Str -2, Dex -2, Con +2, Int +2, Wis +2, Cha -2; winter the same at -4 and +4, never below 1. It gains no extra skill points and does not recalculate skills for the Intelligence changes. Its save modifiers are morale bonuses: spring +2 against fear and -2 against cold; summer +2 against fire and -2 against cold; autumn +2 against cold and -2 against polymorph; winter +2 against cold and -2 against fear.	SOURCEPAGE:p.251
Spring Season	KEY:Spring Season ~ Seasonal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:In spring the creature has cold and fire resistance 5, deals +1d4 fire damage with each natural and manufactured weapon attack, and, if it casts spells or has spell-like abilities, gains +1 caster level and +1 to save DCs for transmutation effects. It gains a +2 circumstance bonus on Craft, Heal and Handle Animal, and on Knowledge (nature) and on Stealth in natural surroundings that match its colours.	SOURCEPAGE:p.252
Summer Season	KEY:Summer Season ~ Seasonal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:In summer the creature has electricity and fire resistance 5, deals +1d6 fire damage with each natural and manufactured weapon attack, and, if it casts spells or has spell-like abilities, gains +1 caster level and +1 to save DCs for evocation effects. It gains a +2 circumstance bonus on Acrobatics, Climb and Swim, and on Knowledge (nature) and on Stealth in natural surroundings that match its colours.	SOURCEPAGE:p.252
Autumn Season	KEY:Autumn Season ~ Seasonal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:In autumn the creature has cold and electricity resistance 5, deals +1d4 cold damage with each natural and manufactured weapon attack, and, if it casts spells or has spell-like abilities, gains +1 caster level and +1 to save DCs for transmutation effects. It gains a +2 circumstance bonus on Bluff, Disguise and Sleight of Hand, and on Knowledge (nature) and on Stealth in natural surroundings that match its colours.	SOURCEPAGE:p.252
Winter Season	KEY:Winter Season ~ Seasonal Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:In winter the creature has cold resistance 10, deals +1d6 cold damage with each natural and manufactured weapon attack, and, if it casts spells or has spell-like abilities, gains +1 caster level and +1 to save DCs for necromancy effects. It gains a +2 circumstance bonus on Escape Artist, Perception and Survival, and on Knowledge (nature) and on Stealth in natural surroundings that match its colours.	SOURCEPAGE:p.252
Seelie Sight	KEY:Seelie Sight ~ Seelie Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Vision	DESC:A seelie creature recognises a seelie or unseelie creature on sight through any mundane or magical disguise, and can see any creature in a faerie walk state. Anything that stops it seeing the creature at all, such as invisibility, blocks seelie sight.	SOURCEPAGE:p.253
Charmed Life	KEY:Charmed Life ~ Seelie Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:A seelie creature gains a +4 luck bonus on all saves against figment illusions and compulsion effects.	SOURCEPAGE:p.254
Faerie Walk	KEY:Faerie Walk ~ Seelie Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:At will, as a full-round action in untouched or uncultivated natural country of at least an acre, a seelie creature can enter a state like an ethereal jaunt, though it coexists with the Fey Realms rather than the Ethereal Plane.	SOURCEPAGE:p.254
Feyblood	KEY:Feyblood ~ Seelie Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A seelie creature that is not already fey counts as both fey and its own type for spells, abilities and effects that target either, keeping any immunity its own type grants unless the effect specifically targets fey. It can also use magic items whose powers are specific to fey creatures.	SOURCEPAGE:p.255
Seelie Pact	KEY:Seelie Pact ~ Seelie Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A seelie creature that becomes evil loses this template and gains the unseelie template.	SOURCEPAGE:p.255
Phases of the Moon	KEY:Phases of the Moon ~ Selenic Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:The selenic template is a set of eight templates, one for each phase of the moon, applied in turn and removed before the next: the changes never stack, and each lasts about 4 to 5 days. Intelligence changes from a phase grant no extra skill points or languages. The creature's alignment moves with the moon: at the new moon it becomes evil, or chaotic if already evil, and no further if already chaotic evil; waxing crescent and waning crescent shift one step towards evil, or towards chaotic if already evil; waxing gibbous and waning gibbous shift one step towards good, or towards lawful if already good; at the full moon it becomes good, or lawful if already good, and no further if already lawful good. The half-moons leave its mood, and its alignment, untouched.	SOURCEPAGE:p.256
Shadow's Friend	KEY:Shadow's Friend ~ Selenic Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:In low light or shadowy illumination the selenic creature gains a +2 morale bonus on attack and damage rolls.	SOURCEPAGE:p.256
Lycanthrope Control	KEY:Lycanthrope Control ~ Selenic Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Under a full moon, a selenic creature automatically senses every lycanthrope within 30 feet and, as a standard action, can force one of them into whichever lycanthropic form it chooses. The lycanthrope is stuck in that form until it or the selenic creature dies or the phase of the moon changes. A Will save at DC 11 + the selenic creature's total Hit Dice negates. The change happens on the selenic creature's turn, not the lycanthrope's.	SOURCEPAGE:p.257

###Block: Shadow-Traced Creature, Slithering Ooze, Smoke Creature
Distributed Mind	KEY:Distributed Mind ~ Shadow-Traced Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:A shadow-traced creature's mind is spread among its traces. If the creature or one of its traces is hit by a mind-affecting spell or effect, the others may attempt the same save one round later at the same DC, as the rogue's slippery mind, and the affected one succeeds if any of them do. A natural 1 on the original save prevents the use of distributed mind against that effect. The creature also loses any immunity to mind-affecting effects.	SOURCEPAGE:p.259
Sacrificial Transposition	KEY:Sacrificial Transposition ~ Shadow-Traced Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:When the creature would drop below 0 hit points and has at least one shadow trace, it may switch places with that trace as an immediate action, negating the damage or effect; the trace is dismissed as though destroyed. Usable once per round.	SOURCEPAGE:p.259
Leeching Absorption	KEY:Leeching Absorption ~ Shadow-Traced Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:When a hostile spell effect fails to beat the creature's spell resistance, every active shadow trace heals hit points equal to that effect's spell level.	SOURCEPAGE:p.259
Shadow Traces	KEY:Shadow Traces ~ Shadow-Traced Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:At will, as an immediate action, the creature makes three independent semi-real copies of itself. Traces act on its initiative and each has half its hit points, with duplicates of its abilities, magic and equipment, though a weapon disarmed from a trace vanishes after 1 round and ammunition it fires vanishes after use. A trace reduced to 0 hit points is destroyed and cannot be remade until all the traces are gone. If all the traces are destroyed the creature is staggered for 1 round and cannot make more for 24 hours; otherwise they last until combat ends or it dismisses them as a full-round action.	SOURCEPAGE:p.259
Traced Magic	KEY:Traced Magic ~ Shadow-Traced Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Weakness	DESC:While at least one trace is active, the traces mirror and weaken the creature's spellcasting and spell-like abilities: every magical effect from the creature or its traces counts as an illusion of the shadow subschool and is only 50%% real against anyone who makes a Will save to disbelieve.	SOURCEPAGE:p.260
Slithering Body	KEY:Slithering Body ~ Slithering Ooze	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A slithering ooze grows one size category, to a maximum of Colossal, and its natural armor changes by the value for its original size: Fine to Small +0, Medium +2, Large +3, Huge +4, Gargantuan and Colossal +5. Each speed doubles, and a creature with no climb speed gains one equal to its highest speed. Natural attack damage rises one step with the size change. Its space and reach follow its original size: Fine and Diminutive 5 ft./0 ft., Tiny 10 ft./0 ft., Small 15 ft./5 ft., Medium 20 ft./5 ft., Large 30 ft./5 ft., Huge 40 ft./5 ft., Gargantuan and Colossal 60 ft./5 ft. Its ability scores change by original size: Fine Dex +6, Con +2; Diminutive Str +2, Dex +6, Con +2; Tiny and Small Str +4, Dex +6, Con +2; Medium Str +8, Dex +6, Con +4; Large Str +8, Dex +6, Con +6; Huge and Gargantuan Str +8, Dex +4, Con +6; Colossal Dex +4, Con +2. It loses the engulf special attack.	SOURCEPAGE:p.261
Flow	KEY:Flow ~ Slithering Ooze	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A slithering ooze can enter another creature's space, though doing so provokes an attack of opportunity as usual. Neither the ooze nor the creature takes a penalty for fighting in the same space, and each provokes attacks of opportunity for movement normally.	SOURCEPAGE:p.262
Pseudopodia	KEY:Pseudopodia ~ Slithering Ooze	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A slithering ooze can make a number of attacks of opportunity per round equal to its Dexterity score, and as a full-round action can make one melee attack against every foe it detects within reach.	SOURCEPAGE:p.262
Diminished Space and Reach	KEY:Diminished Space and Reach ~ Slithering Ooze	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A slithering ooze does not occupy a cube: it covers its space as a spread, sloughing up walls and around corners, occupying every square its body covers in a plane of 5-foot cubes, with a maximum vertical reach of 5 feet from where its body pools. Off a surface, swimming or flying, it orients itself as a plane of ooze.	SOURCEPAGE:p.262
Incredible Compression	KEY:Incredible Compression ~ Slithering Ooze	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A slithering ooze's body flows like water: it takes no penalty for squeezing into a space smaller than its own and can pass through any hole, crack or barrier a liquid could.	SOURCEPAGE:p.262
Slick	KEY:Slick ~ Slithering Ooze	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An area a slithering ooze covers counts as ice for movement and Acrobatics checks and as slippery for Climb checks. If the base creature had engulf, the ooze may make an attack of opportunity against any creature that stands up from prone within its space. Creatures that ignore penalties for moving on ice or slippery surfaces are not immune to the penalties for moving over a slithering ooze.	SOURCEPAGE:p.262
Cloud Sight	KEY:Cloud Sight ~ Smoke Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Vision	DESC:A smoke creature sees through clouds, gases, fogs, mists and smoke as though they did not hinder vision, so nothing gains concealment from them against it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.263
Smokey Form	KEY:Smokey Form ~ Smoke Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:The smoke wreathing a smoke creature's semisolid body hides its exact position, granting constant concealment (20%% miss chance) as the blur spell, though of no magical origin. It loses any swim speed, keeps its other speeds, and gains a fly speed equal to its slowest speed (minimum 5 ft.) with perfect maneuverability, or perfect maneuverability on an existing fly speed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.263
Smoke Immunities	KEY:Smoke Immunities ~ Smoke Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A smoke creature is immune to inhaled poisons and to gas-, fog- and cloud-based attacks and spells.	SOURCEPAGE:p.263
Smoke Travel	KEY:Smoke Travel ~ Smoke Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:At will, as a move action, a smoke creature can use dimension door at a caster level equal to its total Hit Dice to move from any smoke-filled area to any other within long range (400 ft. + 40 ft. per HD).	SOURCEPAGE:p.263
Breath Weapon	KEY:Breath Weapon ~ Smoke Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once every 1d4 rounds, a smoke creature breathes a cloud of superheated smoke and cinders filling a 20-foot cube adjacent to or surrounding itself. Every creature in the cloud takes 2d6 points of fire damage each round with no save, and any breathing creature must also make a Fortitude save each round or take 1d4 points of Constitution damage; holding its breath on its initiative avoids the Constitution damage in later rounds. The smoke grants concealment as a fog cloud and holds its shape for 5 rounds against any wind, then disperses as normal smoke. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.264
Air Mastery	KEY:Air Mastery ~ Smoke Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Any airborne creature takes a -1 penalty on attack and damage rolls against a smoke creature.	SOURCEPAGE:p.264

###Block: Solaric Creature, Sonic Creature, Stone Idol
Solaric Immunities	KEY:Solaric Immunities ~ Solaric Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A solaric creature is immune to the harmful effects of bright light, including effects that blind or dazzle with light, to all effects with the light descriptor, and to light-based attacks such as color spray, prismatic spray and searing light. It also loses any weakness tied to bright light or daylight.	SOURCEPAGE:p.265
Sun Savior	KEY:Sun Savior ~ Solaric Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:In sunlight, or within the radius of a daylight spell, each of the solaric creature's speeds rises by 10 feet and it gains a +2 morale bonus on attack rolls, checks and saves.	SOURCEPAGE:p.265
Solaric Light	KEY:Solaric Light ~ Solaric Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A solaric creature's spell-like abilities accumulate with its Hit Dice: 1-2 3/day flare and at will light; 3-4 1/day flame blade and heat metal; 5-6 1/day continual flame and scorching ray; 7-8 3/day daylight; 9-10 2/day searing light; 11-12 1/day flame strike; 13-14 1/day greater teleport, whose destination must be lit by sunlight or a daylight spell; 15-16 1/day sunbeam; 17+ 1/day sunburst. The caster level is its total Hit Dice and the save DCs are Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.265
Improved Blindsight	KEY:Improved Blindsight ~ Sonic Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Vision	DESC:A sonic creature sees by sound, even from inside a solid object, discerning objects and creatures within 60 feet whatever the terrain or barriers and without needing line of effect. A silence spell negates it and leaves the creature relying on the base creature's vision. This replaces blindsight, and a base creature that already had blindsight adds its range to this one.	SOURCEPAGE:p.266
Natural Invisibility	KEY:Natural Invisibility ~ Sonic Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:A sonic creature is naturally invisible and immune to sonic damage, both extraordinary abilities. It loses the base creature's armor, shield and natural armor bonuses, gaining instead a deflection bonus to AC equal to its Charisma bonus or +1, whichever is higher, and it can carry no equipment of any kind.	SOURCEPAGE:p.266
Silence Vulnerability	KEY:Silence Vulnerability ~ Sonic Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:An incorporeal creature normally has a 50%% chance to ignore a spell from a corporeal source, but silence is an exception for a sonic creature. Inside a silence spell it is entangled and all its normal and special attacks are negated. A silence spell cast directly on it instead leaves it nauseated for 1 round per caster level on a failed save, with no silencing or entangling effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.266
Sonic Touch	KEY:Sonic Touch ~ Sonic Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:All the base creature's attacks become incorporeal touch attacks, and a creature with no natural attacks gains a primary incorporeal touch. Any such attack that dealt hit point damage now deals sonic damage, and any other energy damage it carried becomes sonic too. A touch granted by the template deals damage as a slam of a creature one size larger. Special attacks needing corporeal contact are lost unless they deal hit point damage, which becomes sonic damage in the same amount, and spell-like abilities that dealt acid, cold, electricity or fire damage now deal sonic damage. A sonic creature cannot cast spells with material components unless it has Eschew Materials.	SOURCEPAGE:p.267
Sonic Trample	KEY:Sonic Trample ~ Sonic Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:As a full-round action, a sonic creature can move up to twice its speed in a straight line, damaging creatures and objects it passes through. Each creature may make a Reflex save for half damage or an attack of opportunity; an unattended nonmagical object gets no save, and nothing can be damaged twice in a round this way. A sonic creature harms nothing it passes through unless it intends to. The damage is that of a slam attack of a creature two size categories larger plus 1-1/2 its Dexterity modifier, or the base creature's trample damage modified by Dexterity instead of Strength. The save DCs are Dexterity-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.267
Wounding Sound	KEY:Wounding Sound ~ Sonic Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:When a sonic creature is wounded its body makes a thunderous report. Anyone within 30 feet must make a Fortitude save or take 1d6 points of sonic damage, be stunned for 1 round and be permanently deafened. A creature that cannot hear, or that saves, is neither stunned nor deafened but still takes 1d6 points of sonic damage on a failed save. Every unattended object in the area automatically takes 1d6 points of sonic damage each time. The save is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.267
Cacophony	KEY:Cacophony ~ Sonic Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A sonic creature gains a +10 racial bonus on Perception and never takes a penalty on Perception from ambient noise or its own din. It cannot move silently: its body always hums or keens, giving it a -15 penalty on Stealth even while stationary, and it loses any Stealth bonus the base creature had from coloration.	SOURCEPAGE:p.268
Stone Body	KEY:Stone Body ~ Stone Idol	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:A stone idol gains all the defensive abilities and immunities of a construct, hardness 8, and takes half damage from energy and ranged attacks. It loses bonus hit points from Constitution and gains a construct's bonus hit points for its size. Its Intelligence becomes 6 whatever it was, and its skill ranks are redistributed for the new score.	SOURCEPAGE:p.269
Vulnerability to Sonic	KEY:Vulnerability to Sonic ~ Stone Idol	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:A stone idol takes half again as much damage (+50%%) from sonic damage, regardless of whether a saving throw is allowed or whether the save succeeds.	SOURCEPAGE:p.269
Stone Fear	KEY:Stone Fear ~ Stone Idol	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:At will, as a free action, a stone idol projects a continuous aura of fear: every creature within 60 feet must succeed on a Will save or be shaken for 1 hour. Creatures charmed, dominated or summoned by the idol are immune, and the idol can suppress the aura at will. This is a fear effect with a Charisma-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.269
Charming Gaze	KEY:Charming Gaze ~ Stone Idol	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Any creature within 10 feet of the stone idol must succeed on a Will save or be affected as by charm monster. While the idol's creator keeps control of it, creatures charmed this way count as charmed by both the idol and its creator. This is a gaze effect at a caster level equal to the idol's total Hit Dice, with a Charisma-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.269
Creator's Failsafe	KEY:Creator's Failsafe ~ Stone Idol	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:While it keeps control of the idol, the creator is immune to all the idol's special attacks, both those from this template and those kept from the base creature. Ordinary physical attacks still affect the creator, so it could stand unharmed in the idol's breath weapon yet be hurt by its melee attack.	SOURCEPAGE:p.270
Power from Worship	KEY:Power from Worship ~ Stone Idol	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:For every ten creatures of Intelligence 6 or higher currently charmed by its gaze, the stone idol gains 5 temporary hit points and a +2 bonus on Perception checks. Temporary hit points lost to damage cannot be regained, though charming more creatures grants new ones. The creator shares these benefits while it keeps control.	SOURCEPAGE:p.270
Restless Spirit	KEY:Restless Spirit ~ Stone Idol	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A stone idol has a will of its own, held under its creator's while control lasts, and it knows its creator by their linked spirits, so no deception lets another command it. If its Charisma exceeds its creator's, or its gaze charms more creatures of Intelligence 6 or higher than ten times its creator's character level, the two make an opposed Charisma check. If the idol loses, the creator keeps control for a full day whatever happens, and the process begins again afterwards. If the creator loses, the idol is free forever and usually seeks to destroy its maker before pursuing its own ends, keeping as many intelligent creatures charmed as it can.	SOURCEPAGE:p.270
Stone Idol Creation	KEY:Stone Idol Creation ~ Stone Idol	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A stone idol is built like a golem and weighs three times what the base creature does. It costs 1,500 gp times its CR, and assembling the body needs a DC 20 Craft (sculpting or masonry) check and the Craft Construct feat. The creator's character level must equal or exceed 4 + the idol's CR. A stone idol need not be stone: built from iron, gold, obsidian or any other solid material, its hardness is that of the material.	SOURCEPAGE:p.270

###Block: Suzerain, Swamp Lord, Swarmblooded, Teratocephalos
Dauntless Courage	KEY:Dauntless Courage ~ Suzerain	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:A suzerain is immune to fear, as is any ally within 30 feet who regards it as their leader.	SOURCEPAGE:p.271
Born to Lead	KEY:Born to Lead ~ Suzerain	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:While a free-willed follower of the suzerain is in sight and able to witness its deeds, the suzerain gains a +4 morale bonus to AC and on attacks, damage rolls, checks and saves. Mounts, familiars, animal companions and trained animals do not count as free-willed; cohorts and followers gained through Leadership do. A suzerain with teamwork feats can also grant the use of any one of them, once a day as a free action, to a number of its Leadership cohorts and followers equal to its leadership score, for a number of rounds equal to its Charisma modifier (minimum +1). A suzerain with cavalier levels extends its tactician ability by the same number of rounds.	SOURCEPAGE:p.271
Enchanting Presence	KEY:Enchanting Presence ~ Suzerain	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:The first time a creature that is not already hostile comes within 30 feet of the suzerain and can see, hear or otherwise notice it, its attitude shifts one category towards the positive; a Will save negates. The suzerain's later actions, or simple time, can shift it further. This is a mind-affecting enchantment effect with a Charisma-based save DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.272
Inspiring Example	KEY:Inspiring Example ~ Suzerain	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Every ally within 60 feet that can see or hear the suzerain gains a morale bonus equal to its Charisma modifier on all attack and damage rolls, checks and saves, as long as the suzerain lives.	SOURCEPAGE:p.272
Stirring Speech	KEY:Stirring Speech ~ Suzerain	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:As a standard action, a suzerain can inspire greatness, as the bard ability, in its allies within 30 ft., a number of times per day equal to its Charisma bonus.	SOURCEPAGE:p.272
Marsh Healing	KEY:Marsh Healing ~ Swamp Lord	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A swamp lord gains fast healing 5 while in a marsh. Each of its speeds is 10 feet slower than the base creature's, to a minimum of 5 feet; a base creature with no land speed gains one 10 feet slower than its highest speed, and a swamp lord lacking a climb or swim speed gains the missing mode at its modified land speed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.273
Tentacles	KEY:Tentacles ~ Swamp Lord	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:A swamp lord gains two tentacle attacks with grab on top of the base creature's attacks, choosing once and for all whether they are primary or secondary if it has other natural attacks. They deal damage as an attack of a creature one size larger and reach 5 feet further than the base creature's normal reach. The swamp lord also gains constrict and engulf, both dealing its tentacle damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.273
Swamp Lord Magic	KEY:Swamp Lord Magic ~ Swamp Lord	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A swamp lord's spell-like abilities accumulate with its total Hit Dice: 1-2 2/day entangle and obscuring mist; 3-4 2/day warp wood; 5-6 1/day fog cloud and soften earth and stone; 7-8 1/day plant growth and quench; 9-10 1/day command plants; 11-12 1/day control water. The caster level is its total Hit Dice and the save DCs are Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.273
Commune with Marshlands	KEY:Commune with Marshlands ~ Swamp Lord	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:At will, a swamp lord can learn facts about the whole marsh it stands in and the country around it, as though it had cast commune with nature.	SOURCEPAGE:p.274
Trackless Step	KEY:Trackless Step ~ Swamp Lord	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A swamp lord leaves no trail in natural surroundings and cannot be tracked, unless it chooses to leave one.	SOURCEPAGE:p.274
Swamp Stealth	KEY:Swamp Stealth ~ Swamp Lord	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:In a marsh or forest a swamp lord gains a further +10 racial bonus on Stealth, for +15 in all. It may also use Knowledge (nature) as though trained.	SOURCEPAGE:p.274
Swarm Bleed	KEY:Swarm Bleed ~ Swarmblooded	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Each swarmblooded has an associated vermin swarm of CR no greater than a third of its HD (minimum CR 1) that spills into its own space when it is wounded, and over which it has no control. The trigger depends on its CR: at CR 1-3 a confirmed critical hit, bleed damage or death; at CR 4-9 those plus damage from a slashing weapon; at CR 10+ any damage at all.	SOURCEPAGE:p.275
Self-Swarm Immunity	KEY:Self-Swarm Immunity ~ Swarmblooded	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A swarmblooded is immune to the attacks and effects of the swarms its own swarm bleed creates.	SOURCEPAGE:p.275
Verminous Innards	KEY:Verminous Innards ~ Swarmblooded	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:Any effect granting a bonus on attack rolls, damage rolls or skill checks against vermin, such as a bane weapon or a ranger's favored enemy, grants the same bonus against the swarmblooded.	SOURCEPAGE:p.275
Grafted Head	KEY:Grafted Head ~ Teratocephalos	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The base creature's head is replaced with that of another animal or humanoid, scaled to fit. An animal becomes a magical beast and a humanoid a monstrous humanoid, each gaining the matching augmented subtype; a monstrous humanoid's type is unchanged. It acquires any of the head creature's senses that are better than its own, so a tiger-headed human gains low-light vision and scent while a human-headed tiger keeps them. Its mental scores shift: a head from a creature of higher Charisma grants +2 Charisma; a head from a creature of higher Intelligence or Wisdom sets that score to the head creature's -2, minimum 2, even if that is lower than the base creature's. It may take feats that have either the base or the head creature as a prerequisite.	SOURCEPAGE:p.277
Head Creature Attacks	KEY:Head Creature Attacks ~ Teratocephalos	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:The teratocephalos gains the head creature's bite and gore attacks and loses the base creature's. A head from a creature of the same size deals that creature's damage even if it is weaker; from a larger or smaller creature, scale the damage to the new size. It keeps the base creature's special attacks that come from its body or limbs and the head creature's that come from the head, such as a poisonous bite or a gaze. It also gains, at the head creature's own ability type: quills, so a porcupine-headed teratocephalos deals quill damage to anyone attacking its head; and the tongue and pull attacks of a giant frog for a frog-headed teratocephalos of Medium size or larger, though it can never swallow prey whole.	SOURCEPAGE:p.277
Head Creature Qualities	KEY:Head Creature Qualities ~ Teratocephalos	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The teratocephalos gains further qualities from its head, at the head creature's own ability type: gift of speech, letting a head from a speaking creature speak Common and further languages as its Intelligence allows; hold breath as long as the head creature for a cetacean-headed one; speak with species, letting an animal-headed one always communicate with both its body's and its head's species; a trunk used as an elephant or similar creature would; and breathe water for a fish-headed one, which then cannot breathe air even if the base creature could.	SOURCEPAGE:p.277

###Block: Thronefused, Thunder Child, Time Seer
Immunity to Sleep	KEY:Immunity to Sleep ~ Thronefused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A thronefused is immune to sleep effects.	SOURCEPAGE:p.278
+4 on saves against enchantments and illusions	KEY:Thronefused Saves ~ Thronefused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality	ASPECT:SaveBonus|+4 vs. enchantments and illusions	SOURCEPAGE:p.278
Bound Travel	KEY:Bound Travel ~ Thronefused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A thronefused loses all its modes of movement. As a full-round action it can start travelling in any one of the base creature's former modes at the same rate, with a flier's maneuverability one step worse. Once moving, its only full-round actions are to stop or to do something involving movement such as running or charging; otherwise it may only use its move action to keep travelling in the same mode. Changing modes takes one round to stop and another to start again, and it cannot take a 5-ft. step unless already moving. The manner of movement suits the base creature: an elf's throne may ride undulating vines, a wizard's may move by telekinesis.	SOURCEPAGE:p.278
Fusing Touch	KEY:Fusing Touch ~ Thronefused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:A thronefused can make a touch attack that fuses a victim's lower limbs into a shape like a chess pawn or a statue base. A Fortitude save resists, with a new save at the start of each round to break free. While fused the victim cannot move, loses its Dexterity bonus to AC and takes a -10 penalty on Reflex saves. Usable a number of rounds per day equal to 1 + the thronefused's Charisma modifier, minimum 1. A target with no lower limbs is immune. The save DC is Charisma-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.278
Throne Lore	KEY:Throne Lore ~ Thronefused	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:A thronefused gains a +5 racial bonus on all Knowledge skills and Linguistics and a -10 penalty on Acrobatics, Climb, Ride and Swim. Any feat it no longer qualifies for because of its reduced Dexterity becomes a bonus feat. A thronefused of Intelligence 10 or higher also gains spell-like abilities accumulating with its total Hit Dice: 1-2 1/day hypnotism; 3-4 3/day detect thoughts; 5-6 3/day suggestion; 7-8 1/day scrying; 9-10 1/day lesser geas; 11-12 1/day mass suggestion; 13-14 3/day vision; 15-16 1/day mass charm monster; 17-18 1/day moment of prescience; 19+ 1/day dominate monster. The caster level is its total Hit Dice or its own caster level, whichever is higher.	SOURCEPAGE:p.279
Cloud Sight	KEY:Cloud Sight ~ Thunder Child	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Vision	DESC:A thunder child sees through clouds, gases, fogs, mists and smoke as though they did not hinder vision, so nothing gains concealment from them against it, and it can use this while gaseous.	SOURCEPAGE:p.280
Electric Aura	KEY:Electric Aura ~ Thunder Child	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary.Aura	DESC:A thunder child emits an aura of electricity. Any creature within 10 feet must succeed on a Reflex save each round or take 1d6 points of electricity damage. The thunder child can suppress or resume the aura as a free action. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.280
Storm Immunities	KEY:Storm Immunities ~ Thunder Child	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Immunity	DESC:A thunder child is immune to electricity, to inhaled poisons and to gas-, fog- and cloud-based attacks and spells.	SOURCEPAGE:p.280
Breath Weapon	KEY:Breath Weapon ~ Thunder Child	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Once every 1d4 rounds, a thunder child breathes a 5-foot-wide line of lightning 100 feet long plus 10 feet per 2 HD, or a line half as long and 10 feet wide. Every creature in the area must make a Reflex save or take 1d6 points of electricity damage per 2 HD of the thunder child, minimum 1d6, halved on a success. The save DC is Constitution-based.	SOURCEPAGE:p.280
Electric Grapple	KEY:Electric Grapple ~ Thunder Child	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Any creature grappling or being grappled by a thunder child takes 2d6 points of electricity damage each round the grapple lasts.	SOURCEPAGE:p.281
Electricity	KEY:Electricity ~ Thunder Child	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Each of a thunder child's natural melee attacks, and its attacks with metallic melee weapons, deal +1d6 points of electricity damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.281
Air Breather	KEY:Air Breather ~ Thunder Child	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A thunder child can breathe air even if the base creature breathed only water.	SOURCEPAGE:p.281
Lightning Jump	KEY:Lightning Jump ~ Thunder Child	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:When a thunder child breathes lightning it may teleport, with no chance of error, to any point within the area of that attack as a free action, taken immediately after the breath weapon.	SOURCEPAGE:p.281
Uncanny Dodge	KEY:Uncanny Dodge ~ Time Seer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:A time seer gains uncanny dodge as an extraordinary ability, or improved uncanny dodge if the base creature already had uncanny dodge.	SOURCEPAGE:p.283
Preternatural Knowledge	KEY:Preternatural Knowledge ~ Time Seer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Once per round, as a free action, a time seer may attempt a DC 15 Wisdom check. On a success it gains a +4 bonus on its next attack roll, check or saving throw, whichever comes first; on a failure it misreads its vision and takes a -4 penalty on that roll instead.	SOURCEPAGE:p.283
Conflicted Vision	KEY:Conflicted Vision ~ Time Seer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:Before rolling initiative a time seer must attempt a DC 10 Wisdom check. On a success it gains +4 on the roll; failing by less than 5 it rolls normally; failing by 5 or more it takes -4 on the roll.	SOURCEPAGE:p.283
Unreliable Spellcasting	KEY:Unreliable Spellcasting ~ Time Seer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:Each time a time seer casts a spell or uses a spell-like ability it must succeed on a Wisdom check against DC 10 + the spell's level. On a failure nothing happens and the use or spell slot is wasted.	SOURCEPAGE:p.283

###Block: Transforming Construct, Unholy Creature
Alternate Form	KEY:Alternate Form ~ Transforming Construct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:As a full-round action a transforming construct can take an alternate form, chosen when the template is applied and never changed afterwards. It keeps its hit points across the change and may stay in either form indefinitely, and abilities bought with construct points carry over wherever the new form allows them. True seeing and similar magic reveal all its forms at once. It keeps every attack, special attack and special quality of the base creature except those tied to limbs the alternate form lacks. The template may be applied more than once for more forms, each adding +1 CR; under the Ultimate Magic construct modification rules each form is a complex modification requiring Craft Construct and polymorph at 12,500 gp and +1 CR, and for a creature built with animate objects each form counts as two Small objects against the spell's limit. In roller or swimmer form the construct cannot be tripped, and natural attacks granted by an alternate form deal damage as a creature one size larger.	SOURCEPAGE:p.288
Bipedal Form	KEY:Bipedal Form ~ Transforming Construct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Available only to a construct that is not already bipedal. In bipedal form its land speed doubles, or becomes twice its fastest speed if it had none; swim and burrow speeds halve; and a fly speed's maneuverability drops one category, minimum clumsy. It gains two primary slam attacks if it had none, a second matching slam if it had one, and nothing further if it already had two or more. It can wield weapons and is proficient with any two specific weapons, and gains Two-Weapon Fighting as a bonus feat.	SOURCEPAGE:p.285
Climber Form	KEY:Climber Form ~ Transforming Construct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Available only to a construct with no climb speed. In climber form its land, burrow, fly and swim speeds each halve, to a minimum of 5 feet, and it gains a climb speed equal to the base creature's highest speed, climbing sheer surfaces and ceilings like a spider. Climb becomes a class skill and it gains Skill Focus (Climb) as a bonus feat.	SOURCEPAGE:p.285
Digger Form	KEY:Digger Form ~ Transforming Construct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Available only to a construct made chiefly of stone or metal that has no burrow speed. In digger form it gains a burrow speed equal to the base creature's highest speed and loses any climb, fly or swim speed; a mostly metal body can burrow through stone. The tunnel fills in behind it as it goes. It gains tremorsense +60 ft., a primary gore attack with its drill, and dire charge, dealing double damage with a successful gore on a charge, plus Toughness as a bonus feat.	SOURCEPAGE:p.285
Flyer Form	KEY:Flyer Form ~ Transforming Construct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Available only to a construct that cannot fly. In flyer form it gains a fly speed of double the base creature's highest speed with average maneuverability and loses its land, burrow and swim speeds. It gains a +4 competence bonus on Perception, Fly as a class skill and a +8 racial bonus on Fly checks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.285
Roller Form	KEY:Roller Form ~ Transforming Construct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Available only to a construct that does not already move on wheels. In roller form its land speed doubles, or equals the base creature's highest speed if it had none; it loses any climb speed; swim and burrow speeds halve; and a fly speed's maneuverability drops one category, minimum clumsy. It gains a single primary ramming attack dealing slam damage plus 1-1/2 its Strength bonus, which cannot be combined with any other attack in the same round, and it replaces any trample with a new one dealing damage one size category above that slam plus 1-1/2 its Strength bonus, with a Strength-based DC.	SOURCEPAGE:p.285
Swimmer Form	KEY:Swimmer Form ~ Transforming Construct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:Available only to a construct with no swim speed. In swimmer form it gains a swim speed of double the base creature's highest speed and loses any fly speed, while land, climb and burrow speeds halve. It gains tremorsense +60 ft., a primary bite attack if it had none, dire charge, dealing double damage with a successful bite on a charge, and Swim as a class skill.	SOURCEPAGE:p.285
Awful Presence	KEY:Awful Presence ~ Unholy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural.Aura	DESC:Every nonevil creature within 30 ft. of an unholy creature automatically takes a -1 penalty on all attack rolls, checks and saves. This is a mind-affecting fear effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.289
Positive Energy Protection	KEY:Positive Energy Protection ~ Unholy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:When struck by a positive energy attack such as a cure spell, an unholy creature may make a level check (1d20 + total HD) against DC 11 + the attacker's character level. On a success the attack is cancelled in a bright flash, and if it came from a melee or melee touch attack the attacker takes 2d6 points of damage. An unholy creature is also immune to negative energy.	SOURCEPAGE:p.289
Protection from Good	KEY:Protection from Good ~ Unholy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural.Defensive	DESC:An unholy creature gains a +2 deflection bonus to AC and a +2 resistance bonus on saves against attacks by good creatures, and is immune to any attempt by a good creature to possess, charm or influence it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.289
Profane Attacks	KEY:Profane Attacks ~ Unholy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:Each of an unholy creature's melee attacks with a natural or manufactured weapon deals +1d6 points of extra damage to good creatures, and all its natural and manufactured weapons count as evil-aligned for overcoming damage reduction.	SOURCEPAGE:p.289
Unholy Spellcasting	KEY:Unholy Spellcasting ~ Unholy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:An unholy creature's effective caster level for necromancy spells and for spells with the curse or evil descriptors is +1 higher than the base creature's. The bonus stacks with itself, so a spell meeting both conditions is cast at +2 caster levels.	SOURCEPAGE:p.289
Unholy Body	KEY:Unholy Body ~ Unholy Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:An unholy creature is healed by negative energy and harmed by positive energy like an undead creature, so inflict light wounds heals it and cure light wounds hurts it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.290

###Block: Unseelie Creature, Verminoid, War Machine
Unseelie Sight	KEY:Unseelie Sight ~ Unseelie Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Vision	DESC:While using its invisibility, an unseelie creature can also see other invisible seelie and unseelie creatures. It automatically succeeds on saves against illusions produced by seelie and unseelie creatures and recognises them at once for what they are, and it can see any creature in a faerie walk state.	SOURCEPAGE:p.291
Unseelie Taint	KEY:Unseelie Taint ~ Unseelie Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Supernatural	DESC:The presence of, or contact with, an evil unseelie creature spreads a curse that blights flora and fauna; non-evil unseelie do not spread it. Unseelie taint--curse, special; save Will negates; onset 1 week; frequency 1/week; effect alignment shifts one step towards evil; cure special; Charisma-based DC. Any physical contact through a natural attack or touch exposes a target, and so does contact with already afflicted flora or fauna, though that grants a +2 circumstance bonus on the first save. The first successful save prevents the curse taking hold; later successes only stave off that week's shift. Remove curse lifts it until the victim turns evil, after which not even wish or miracle undoes the change. The unseelie creature that caused it must be permanently killed before remove curse or stronger magic can lift the curse, even if that creature has since lost the template.	SOURCEPAGE:p.291
Faerie Walk	KEY:Faerie Walk ~ Unseelie Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:At will, as a full-round action in untouched, uncultivated or blighted natural country of at least an acre, an unseelie creature can enter a state like an ethereal jaunt, coexisting with the Fey Realms and the Material rather than the Ethereal Plane. It may stay as long as it remains in such country and return as a free action. It cannot enter Material Plane structures not built by an unseelie creature, nor pass beyond the untouched, uncultivated or blighted area; crossing such a boundary makes it tangible at once, and doing so willingly costs it the use of faerie walk for a week. It can bring along a willing creature, or one affected by its sleep, under the same constraints, and that creature stays only as long as the unseelie creature does or until sent back. Faerie walk cannot be used in an area claimed by a seelie creature, under a hallow spell or similar magic, or within a magic circle warding against an alignment component the unseelie creature shares.	SOURCEPAGE:p.292
Feyblood	KEY:Feyblood ~ Unseelie Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An unseelie creature counts as both fey and its own type for spells, abilities and effects that target either, keeping any immunity its own type grants unless the effect specifically targets fey. It can also use magic items whose powers are specific to fey creatures.	SOURCEPAGE:p.292
Unseelie Pact	KEY:Unseelie Pact ~ Unseelie Creature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:An unseelie creature that becomes good loses this template and gains the seelie template.	SOURCEPAGE:p.292
Verminoid Body	KEY:Verminoid Body ~ Verminoid	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A verminoid walks upright on two legs and has two arms with hands that can use tools, keeping every other hideous feature of its vermin form. Unlike other monstrous humanoids its good saves are Fortitude and Reflex. A land speed below 10 feet, or none at all, becomes 10 feet. It keeps all the base creature's attacks except those on limbs that became arms, with their primary or secondary status, and gains the weapon and armor proficiencies of a monstrous humanoid; it loses rake and trample and any bonus against trip from multiple legs. Its space and reach suit its size, using the tall column at Large or greater, with 5 feet added if the base creature had greater than normal reach. A base creature with no Intelligence score gains Intelligence 8 and loses the mindless trait. It keeps only its bonus feats and takes new ones for its Hit Dice, and buys its skills afresh as a monstrous humanoid with the base creature's skills plus Perception and Survival as class skills. It can speak one language, usually an insectile dialect of Common, plus those its Intelligence allows. Its CR rises to 1/2 if the base creature's was below 1, and is otherwise unchanged.	SOURCEPAGE:p.293
Impenetrable Mind	KEY:Impenetrable Mind ~ Verminoid	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Defensive	DESC:A verminoid loses any immunity to mind-affecting effects but, thanks to its unthinking insect heritage, gains a +4 racial bonus on saves against them.	SOURCEPAGE:p.293
Metal Body	KEY:Metal Body ~ War Machine	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Weakness	DESC:Beneath its skin a war machine is largely metal, so it counts as a ferrous creature for rusting grasp and other spells with special effects on metal.	SOURCEPAGE:p.295
Sprint	KEY:Sprint ~ War Machine	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:Once per hour, a war machine can move up to ten times its normal speed when it charges.	SOURCEPAGE:p.295
War Machine Attacks	KEY:War Machine Attacks ~ War Machine	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Each of a war machine's natural attacks deals damage as though it were two size categories larger, and it can wield weapons up to two size categories larger than the base creature could without penalty.	SOURCEPAGE:p.295
Body Blades	KEY:Body Blades ~ War Machine	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Extraordinary	DESC:Spikes and blades cover a war machine's body. A creature attacking it with a handheld or natural weapon takes 1d8 points of slashing and piercing damage; incorporeal creatures and those using weapons of exceptional reach such as longspears do not. The war machine also deals 1d8 points of piercing and slashing damage to a grabbed opponent with each successful grapple check.	SOURCEPAGE:p.295
War Mount	KEY:War Mount ~ War Machine	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:For an extra 500 gp its creator can build a war machine able to carry them as a rider without exposing them to its body blades.	SOURCEPAGE:p.296
War Machine Construction	KEY:War Machine Construction ~ War Machine	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:A war machine is built like a golem and, being made of metal, weighs three times what the base creature does. CL 5th + the war machine's CR; Price 2,400 gp x twice its CR; Requirements Craft Construct, geas/quest, greater polymorph, limited wish, resist energy, creator caster level 5th + the war machine's CR; Skill Craft (weaponsmithing) DC 25; Cost 1,200 gp x its CR. It also gains the mindless universal monster ability, loses hit points from Constitution and gains a construct's bonus hit points for its size, keeps only its bonus feats, and keeps its racial skill bonuses although it has no skill points.	SOURCEPAGE:p.296

#
# End
